  {"a":"mel","b":"aatrox","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Solar Snare's root plus a Radiant Volley barrage lands a guaranteed punish on Aatrox before he has a W chain-pull to drag you into his Q sweetspots."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aatrox's takeover: Golden Eclipse cannot stop Umbral Dash closing on a 9s cooldown, Infernal Chains pulling, and World Ender's combat stats finishing you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Eclipse/Profane Hydra spike plus drain heal lets him out-sustain every short trade and heal back the Overwhelm chip you stacked all lane."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your peak-stack window swings back even — empowered Radiant Volley and a from-range R detonation chunk a melee Aatrox who has to walk through your Solar Snare field to reach you."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root and rain Radiant Volley to stack Overwhelm while he's stuck at melee range with no gap-closer up","Hold Rebuttal for Infernal Chains and the third Darkin Blade swing — it blanks their damage and is 38s down","Keep max distance and detonate Golden Eclipse from range, never letting him stand on you long enough to drain back the chip"],"foe":["Land Infernal Chains to drag you out of position, then Umbral Dash in and land The Darkin Blade's healing third swing","Hit level 6 and pop R combat stats to all-in your squishy body the instant his gap-closers connect","Survive your poke to first item where Eclipse and his drain passive out-sustain every short trade you take"]},"early":"Aatrox is at his weakest exactly when I want to fight — levels 1-2 he only has his Q knockups and no W chain-pull yet, so I sit at 550 range and rain Radiant Volley on him every time he steps up to last-hit. At level 2 with Q plus Solar Snare I get a guaranteed punish: root him in the field, then barrage him while he's stuck and stack Overwhelm on his frame. The one thing to dodge is the sweetspot tip of his Q knockups — each one heals him through his passive, so I never stand in a straight line at melee range where he can chain all three.","mid":"This is where it tilts to him. From level 3 his W chain-pull is online, and if it lands he E-dashes in and the sweetspot Q sequence flips any trade and procs his drain heal, so I hold Rebuttal to body-block the pull and keep Solar Snare for the disengage root, not the poke. At 6 his Golden Eclipse means nothing against his all-in — he just walks the gap with R combat stats up and out-heals my burst on a squishy mage with one CC and no dash. I refuse to facecheck or get caught in the wave; I poke from max range, bait his W, and only commit Solar Snare once his gap-closers are down.","late":"His first-item spike is his takeover — Eclipse and his drain passive let him out-sustain every short trade and heal back the Overwhelm I chipped all lane, so a straight 1v1 into a fed Aatrox is a losing drain war. But once I hit 2+ items it swings back to even: my empowered Radiant Volley and a from-range Golden Eclipse detonation chunk him while he has to walk through my Solar Snare slow field to even reach me, and my passive keeps scaling. So I stop trying to solo his sustain in the sidelane and pivot to teamfights, where I poke and execute with R from range and let my team peel his W-pull off me.","whys":["Aatrox at level 1 has only The Darkin Blade and no way to close, while you poke freely with Radiant Volley at 950 range and stack Overwhelm.","It's even — your level-2 Solar Snare root plus barrage is a real punish, but his Q sweetspot heal makes any trade he survives a wash.","Infernal Chains comes online: one 825-range pull drags you into Umbral Dash and the third Darkin Blade swing, and his passive heals him.","He out-trades you as his Q ranks and his drain stacks up — every extended melee exchange feeds his passive heal and shreds your squishy frame.","World Ender's combat stats walk through your poke, and it fears his minions rather than you — nothing stops it once Infernal Chains lands.","His Eclipse and drain spike out-sustains your short trades and heals back all the Overwhelm chip you stacked — close nothing, just survive the window.","Genuinely even late: he wins the isolated drain duel, but your empowered Radiant Volley and from-range R detonation keep you a real threat in any teamfight."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"akali","win":["Mel","Skill","Akali","Akali","Mel","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root is your one clean punish window before Akali has Twilight Shroud or Shuriken Flip, so land E if she steps inside 550."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Akali's nightmare flips on: once Twilight Shroud is up she goes untargetable inside the smoke and your E and R lose their lock, so she negates your whole stack-and-execute plan."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse should be your spike, but Akali's R two-part dash gap-closes past your 550 range and her execute deletes your squishy frame before stacks detonate."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Post-Shroud, Akali on a first AP item (Hextech/Riftmaker) one-shots you out of the smoke — your single CC on E is your only out and it is on cooldown for most of it."}],"wants":{"you":["Land E Solar Snare's root the instant Akali walks up to last-hit, before her Shroud and dash are leveled","Hold Rebuttal for Shuriken Flip and the Perfect Execution recast — it blanks their damage instead of feeding the dash","Build Overwhelm stacks with Q poke at max range and bait her into the open where Shroud can't hide her"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud to go untargetable, dodging your E root and R detonation entirely","Land Shuriken Flip to mark you, then recast the dash and follow with the R leap before your root is back","Farm safely to a first AP item, then all-in the moment your Solar Snare is on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is the only stretch this lane is yours: she has nothing but autos and one ability, so chunk her with Q and, the second she steps into CS range, slam Solar Snare's root and tag her with empowered autos to start Overwhelm. The whole game flips at level 3 when Twilight Shroud comes online — once she's in the smoke she's untargetable, so my E orb and R can't even lock her. Get your damage in before she has Shroud, because after that she dictates every trade.","mid":"From 4 onward this is survival, not domination. She has E shuriken-dash and at 6 her two-part R, both of which leap clean past my 550 range, and she just sits in Shroud waiting for my Solar Snare to go on cooldown before she commits. My only real tool is W Rebuttal — hold it for her engage, not her poke, because the barrier eats her dash window. Never push past river; one E-Shroud-R chain with a Dirk and she deletes me before a single Overwhelm stack detonates.","late":"Late, it's a coin-flip that leans on positioning. My infinitely-scaling passive keeps me relevant and if I'm behind a frontline I can poke and chip with Q from max range while my team eats her dive. But she only needs one Shroud-gated flank to vanish, R onto me, and execute through my squishy frame — so I hug peel, never facecheck, and save W for the instant she shows. If she's fed it's already lost; if she's even, a landed E root is the whole teamfight.","whys":["With one ability and your ranged auto you out-range and out-poke a level-1 Akali who has no Shroud and no dash yet — chip her and zone the wave.","Akali takes Q and you take E or Q — Five Point Strike costs 110 energy at rank 1, so her poke is rationed, but Shroud is one level away. Call it even.","Twilight Shroud comes online and breaks you: inside the smoke she is untargetable, so your E orb and R detonation lose their lock and she dictates the trade.","Her Q ranks and Shuriken Flip closes your gap on a 16s cooldown while Twilight Shroud comes back every 17s — your one root cannot cover both windows.","Golden Eclipse should be your spike, but her R two-part dash gap-closes past your poke and the recast execute deletes your squishy frame before stacks pop.","On a first AP item she one-shots you out of Shroud the moment your Solar Snare is down — your one CC can't cover the whole all-in window.","Your infinitely-scaling passive keeps you in the game and a landed E root is the fight, but she scales just as hard and can flank from Shroud — it comes down to positioning."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"akshan","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your only clean window: one Radiant Volley plus a ranged auto out-trades Avengerang before he has Dirty Fighting shields or Heroic Swing."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Akshan's threat window opens — Heroic Swing hooks a wall to close your 550 range, dodge Solar Snare, and burst you while your root is down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse can detonate stacks at any range, but Comeuppance dies on the first minion in line — keep the wave between you and stay topped up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His lethality spike (Youmuu's/Serpent's) out-DPS's your poke; he swings in, three-shots you, and swings out before you re-stack Overwhelm."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root to lock him out of an E-swing and chain Radiant Volley poke before he closes","Hold Rebuttal for Avengerang and Comeuppance, since nearly everything he owns is a projectile","Stack Overwhelm in short safe trades and use R range to punish him when he over-extends a swing"],"foe":["Use Heroic Swing off a wall to dodge your Solar Snare and gap your 550 range for a burst trade","Bait out Rebuttal then commit Q/W after the wall drops to chunk your squishy frame","Roam under Going Rogue's camouflage and snowball side lanes, since he out-ranges your DPS"]},"early":"Level 1 is your one clean window — you have a real range and stack advantage before his kit comes online, so throw Radiant Volley and weave a ranged auto to chip him while his Q is single-target and he has no W shields yet. The instant he hits 2-3 and gets E, the lane flips: his grapple-swing lets him dodge your Solar Snare and close your 550 range, so stop face-poking and only commit Q if his E is on cooldown. Save Rebuttal for his actual poke projectiles, not as a panic button.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are his, not yours — Akshan out-DPS's your poke once he can E-swing in, and your single root plus no dashes means once he's on top of you, you're getting three-shot. Your job is to hit Solar Snare to lock the swing, then immediately back off; don't greed a second rotation. At 6, Golden Eclipse gives you range burst on your stacks, but his camouflage passive and revive mean a won trade rarely becomes a kill — detonate to push him off, not to chase.","late":"By 2+ items it evens out: you're both squishy, and now your R range and Overwhelm execute can one-shot him across a fight if he's careless, the same way his lethality can delete you. Play with your team — your wall and root are teamfight tools that shut his swing engage down, and a clean Golden Eclipse detonation can blow him up before he swings out. Track his camo roams and ward your sides; if he's gone, he's snowballing someone else.","whys":["Level 1 with one ability and a ranged auto you out-poke Avengerang before he has Dirty Fighting shields or Heroic Swing mobility.","At 2 Heroic Swing comes online — he grapples a wall to dodge your Solar Snare and close your 550 range, and starts out-trading you.","With Q, W and E up he kite-skirmishes around your poke, swinging in and out faster than you can re-stack Overwhelm.","As his Q ranks and lethality builds he out-DPS's your trades; one root can't stop a mobile skirmisher with a reset swing.","Golden Eclipse gives you range burst, but Going Rogue's camouflage and its revive mean even a won trade seldom converts to a kill.","His first lethality item out-paces your poke — he swings in, bursts your squishy frame, and swings out before you answer.","By two items you're both glass: your R-detonate execute can one-shot him at range just as his burst deletes you, so it's a coinflip on who lands first."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"ambessa","win":["Mel","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Mel","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Level 1 you out-range her with Q bolts and empowered autos before she has her dash combo, and at 2 Solar Snare's root can punish a step-up."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Ambessa has Drakehound's Step riding Cunning Sweep and Lacerate she weaves through your Q rain and owns the all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution covers the gap your kite relies on — it reaches 1250, further than your Q, and suppresses on arrival, so Golden Eclipse never detonates."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first AP item lets you chain Q poke and detonate R, but Ambessa's bruiser item + chain CC still closes the gap — buy boots/Zhonya's-line to survive the dive."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root the instant she dashes in so your W wall and Q poke punish her before she resets her combo","Stack Overwhelm from max range with Q and empowered autos, then detonate Golden Eclipse when she commits","Keep Flash and E up for her engage — you have zero dashes, so your only escape is rooting her and walking away"],"foe":["Bait your E root with a feint dash, then commit Cunning Sweep into Lacerate and chain the Repudiation slam","Weave her dashes around your Q rain so the bolts miss and close to melee where you have no escape","Catch you with no E and all-in — without your root she runs you down and your squishy frame folds"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are your window before her combo is online. At 1 you out-range her — chip with Q bolts and your empowered autos to start stacking Overwhelm while she has no way to reach you. At 2 with Q + E, the moment she steps up for a CS, throw Solar Snare to root her and follow with Q for a guaranteed chunk. Do not waste E preemptively; her whole early game is faking a dash to bait your one piece of CC, and if you blow the root on a feint she dashes in clean.","mid":"This is where she takes over. By level 3+ Ambessa has her full dash-and-W combo and starts weaving through your Q rain — the bolts whiff on a moving, dashing target and she closes to melee where you have nothing. Hold W to eat her engage if it has a projectile component, but mostly your job is to keep E for the dash and never get caught with it down. At 6 her ult engage covers the exact gap your kite depends on; if she lands the combo, your stacks and Golden Eclipse don't save you because you're already CC-chained and chunked. Give up plates over your life and let your jungler punish her dives.","late":"Late game evens back out. Once you have items, your Q-empowered-auto poke and infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive let you sit at 550 range in teamfights and detonate Golden Eclipse on a stacked frontline from any range — you don't need to be near Ambessa to matter. The danger is the same as lane: if she flanks or dashes onto you with her combo and chain CC, you die before you can react. Play behind peel, hold E for her engage, and let your team body-block while you execute from the back.","whys":["Level 1 you have your ranged auto plus a Q at 550 range and she has no dash combo yet — you poke freely and she can't answer.","At 2 your Q + Solar Snare can punish a step-up, but she can fake a dash to bait your root, so the window is genuinely even.","With Drakehound's Step riding every cast she closes 650 through your Q rain and reaches melee, where your no-dash frame has no escape.","Levels 4-5 Cunning Sweep into Lacerate out-trades your short pokes — she re-dashes through your bolts and you cannot kite the gap.","Public Execution reaches 1250, further than your Q, and suppresses on arrival, so you are locked and chunked before Golden Eclipse detonates.","Her bruiser item and chain CC still close on you at first item; your AP spike pokes but doesn't stop a committed all-in.","From 2+ items your scaling passive and ranged R detonation let you matter in fights from max range, evening a lane she controlled in the mid-game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"aurora","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Solar Snare root plus Q barrage is the only window you out-trade her before her E blink is a real escape tool."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her threat window: Golden Eclipse is global, not range-gated, but at 120s her Between Worlds slow zone plus Twofold Hex burst beats one detonation."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Aurora's Lost Chapter / Liandry's spike lets her Q-poke through your Rebuttal cooldown and blink your Solar Snare with E."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive finally out-grinds her once you can chain Q-detonate-R from max range and she can't blink all of it."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) as a hard root while Across the Veil (W) is down, then Q-barrage the target that cannot move","Hold Rebuttal (W) to eat and reflect her Q poke projectile instead of wasting it on a body-block","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos at max range so a late R detonates for an execute she can't blink"],"foe":["Bait your Solar Snare (E), leap it with Across the Veil (W), then punish the 11s with Twofold Hex","Poke you under your own Rebuttal cooldown with Q so your short trade windows always lose","Heal off Spirit Abjuration spirits through your chip until Overwhelm stops mattering"]},"early":"Aurora is the one ranged matchup where your kit doesn't auto-win, because she pokes back at your range and her E blink dodges the Solar Snare root your whole game plan leans on. Levels 1-2 you trade Q barrages roughly even; the moment to push is Level 2-3 when you have E up and she may not have her blink available — land the root, then dump Q on the spot she can't move from. Don't throw a naked Solar Snare into a full-health Aurora holding E; she'll blink it and Q you for free while it's on cooldown.","mid":"This is her window, not yours. Once both ults are online your Golden Eclipse only fires on already-stacked targets, so a clean skirmish favours her R exile plus Q burst, which out-damages your detonation if you haven't pre-loaded Overwhelm. Use Rebuttal to swallow her Q projectile and reflect it rather than to body-block, and never commit an all-in unless her E blink is down. Farm with the edge of Q, chip Overwhelm passively, and refuse the coin-flip trades her first item (Lost Chapter into Liandry's) lets her win.","late":"The lane flips back to you very late. Your Overwhelm passive scales infinitely, so once you can chain Q poke into a max-range Golden Eclipse you start chunking or executing her squishy frame faster than she can blink away — her single E reposition can't dodge a detonation that's already stored on her. Keep stacking from safety, hold Rebuttal for her engage Q, and let your range plus the execute do the work she can no longer kite.","whys":["Two ranged mages with one ability each — you poke even, but neither can commit, so it's a coin-flip stat-check at Level 1.","She gets E + Q online and the blink means your Solar Snare root, your only lockdown, gets dodged the moment she holds it.","With W spirit and her blink up she out-trades your short windows — your Rebuttal reflects one Q but she has the mobility to reset and poke again.","As Twofold Hex ranks she pokes through your 38s Rebuttal and leaps every Solar Snare with Across the Veil (W), starving your stacks.","Golden Eclipse only detonates pre-stacked targets, so in a fair skirmish her Between Worlds slow zone plus Twofold Hex burst out-trades it.","Her Lost Chapter / Liandry's spike lets her out-poke and out-blink you, winning the itemized ranged mirror before your scaling kicks in.","Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm finally wins it — a stored max-range R detonation executes her squishy frame faster than one E blink can save her."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"camille","win":["Mel","Skill","Camille","Camille","Mel","Camille","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Your Radiant Volley (Q) outranges everything Camille has, and at level 2 Solar Snare (E) roots her if she steps up to last-hit — your one clean punish window before she has E hookshot."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Camille’s takeover: once Hookshot (16s) and Tactical Sweep are online she leaps past your poke, and a knock-up into the Q2 true-damage recast chunks your 550-range frame."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult The Hextech Ultimatum walls you into a 1v1 where she ticks magic+true through your kit while you have one root and no dash to peel — Golden Eclipse can't save you if you're already isolated."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Camille's Sheen/Stride spike: her Q true-damage proc and W cone heal out-trade and out-sustain your Overwhelm stacking the moment she lands E on you."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Radiant Volley (Q) pokes and Solar Snare (E) roots from max range to stack Overwhelm before her E hookshot is up","Hold Rebuttal (W) shield and the E root as your only peel for her E-in, never spending them on offense","Buy Grievous Wounds for Tactical Sweep’s heal — Precision Protocol’s recast lands true, so resistances will not save you"],"foe":["Hold Hookshot to dodge your Solar Snare and wall-dash past your Q barrage to land on top of you","Land the Q2 true-damage recast and Tactical Sweep’s outer-edge heal to out-sustain your poke","Hit 6 and isolate you with R The Hextech Ultimatum where her stats win the forced 1v1"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are the only stretch that is yours: Radiant Volley (Q) rains from well outside her 325-range Q, so chip her every time she steps up to last-hit and start stacking Overwhelm with your empowered autos. At level 2 with Q and Solar Snare (E) you can root a greedy CS step and punish it. The second she has Hookshot (E) on 16s and Tactical Sweep, this flips — she wall-leaps the barrage, knocks you up, and the Q2 true-damage recast shreds your 550-range frame. Never throw a Q from inside her 800-range E, and save Solar Snare for her commit, not for poke.","mid":"Levels 3-6 belong to her. Her full Q-W-E out-damages your poke the instant Hookshot lands the knock-up, and you have no dash and one root to answer a gap-closer this hard. Keep Rebuttal (W) up for her burst rather than her engage — it is 38s at rank 1, so spending it on chip books your own death. Treat Solar Snare (11s) as a panic-peel, not a poke tool: if it is down when she E’s in, you die. At 6 Golden Eclipse detonates whatever Overwhelm you stacked, but Hextech Ultimatum anchors you in the exact 1v1 her stats win, and one root will not break the box. Give ground and farm at range.","late":"Once Camille has an item or two the duel is hers outright — the Hookshot knock-up into Tactical Sweep’s outer-edge heal and the Q2 true-damage recast out-sustains your burst, and Hextech Ultimatum drops you in a box where her stats check your squishy frame with no peel left. Do not sidelane into a fed Camille; you are fragile artillery and she is built to delete exactly that. Your way back is the teamfight: Golden Eclipse detonates Overwhelm on her whole team from any range, and Solar Snare peels the second she ults a carry. Group, stack several bodies, never get caught alone.","whys":["Even — Radiant Volley (Q) outranges Camille's whole level-1 kit, but her Q true-damage last-hits match your chip and neither of you can safely commit before she has E.","Camille gets Hookshot and Tactical Sweep — she wall-leaps your Q barrage, knocks you up, and her Q2 true damage beats your poke now.","Her level-3 Q-W-E out-trades your 550-range body — Hookshot’s knock-up into the Q2 true-damage recast and W’s outer edge chunk you while you hold one root.","She owns the all-in: a Camille who lands E wall-dashes past your poke and her W cone heal out-sustains your Overwhelm stacking.","Her R The Hextech Ultimatum walls you into a 1v1 her stats win — Golden Eclipse can't peel you out of the box with no dash and one root.","Her Sheen/Stride spike arrives: Q true-damage proc and W cone heal out-trade and out-sustain your magic burst once she isolates you with R.","Genuinely even late — she scales to win the isolated duel, but your AoE Golden Eclipse and Solar Snare peel keep you relevant in any 5v5 teamfight."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root is your one clean punish window before her poison stacking takes over the lane."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Cassiopeia's Twin Fang spam on poisoned targets out-DPSes your Q poke, and Miasma's slow pins you inside its 700 range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her Petrifying Gaze face-stun lets her front-load Twin Fang burst the instant you're in range — Golden Eclipse rarely out-trades it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive keeps you a real R execute threat from max range even as she farms her ramp."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root at 1000, outside Twin Fang's 700, and step up only once her poison ticks off","Use Rebuttal on her Twin Fang chain — Noxious Blast is a ground zone, not a projectile to catch","Stay at 550 range, refuse to face her so she can never land Petrifying Gaze (R) frontally"],"foe":["Slowing you with Miasma (W) so you can't walk out of her Twin Fang's range","Poisoning you with Noxious Blast (Q) then chain-casting Twin Fang (E) to out-trade your poke","Catching you facing her for the full Petrifying Gaze (R) stun into burst"]},"early":"Cassiopeia's level 1 is one of the worst in the game — no poison engine yet, just one slow Noxious Blast — so your one-ability poke and ranged auto actually edge her here. Hit level 2 with Q plus Solar Snare and you have a real punish: root her stepping up to last-hit, then drop Q bolts before her Twin Fang comes online. After 3 it flips fast — once her poison is rolling, every Noxious Blast on you powers up Twin Fang, and she out-DPSes your Q. Don't sit in the poison; bait her Q with Rebuttal up and reflect it.","mid":"This is her window, not yours. By 4-5 her Twin Fang spam on a poisoned target simply out-damages your Q poke, and Miasma grounds you so you can't kite back to range — the one thing your kit depends on. Solar Snare is your only escape valve: root her when she walks up, then back off out of W range. At 6 her Petrifying Gaze is the trap — never trade facing her or you eat the full stun into Twin Fang burst. Golden Eclipse from range chips, but it doesn't win the all-in.","late":"Your Overwhelm passive scales forever, and that's the one reason this lane isn't hopeless late: from max range you stay a genuine R execute threat with stored damage on her squishy frame. But she's a hard scaler too, and a fed Cassiopeia kites with no-boots move speed and out-DPSes you in any extended fight. Play it as a poke-and-disengage pick for your team — land Solar Snare on her engage, reflect with Rebuttal, and detonate Golden Eclipse from outside Twin Fang range rather than dueling her.","whys":["Cassiopeia level 1 has only one slow Noxious Blast and no poison ramp — your ability plus ranged auto out-poke her clean here.","Your Q plus Solar Snare root is a real punish window, but her Q poison already threatens to power up Twin Fang if you overstay — call it even.","She gets Twin Fang online and her poison starts ramping; your Rebuttal reflect keeps it a coin-flip, but the poke war is tightening.","From 4-5 Twin Fang spam on a poisoned target out-DPSes your Q, and Miasma's slow pins you inside its 700 range.","Petrifying Gaze's face-stun lets her front-load Twin Fang burst on you, and Golden Eclipse doesn't win that all-in.","Her first-item Twin Fang ramp and your first-item poke peak roughly cancel — neither cleanly wins the trade.","Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive keeps you a max-range R execute threat even as she ramps, reclaiming a sliver of the late game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"chogath","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare lets you root Cho'Gath as he steps up to last-hit and free-poke him while he eats the field slow."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Cho'Gath's danger window — Feast is true damage at 175 range that no resistance stops, and all he needs first is Feral Scream's 300-range silence."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your power ebb: Cho'Gath has stacked Feast HP and your R/Overwhelm chunk barely dents a 4000+ HP tank you can't execute."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm keeps you relevant — kite at 550 range and let R detonate stacks, but never get caught alone or his W-Q-R deletes you."}],"wants":{"you":["Abuse levels 2-3: land Solar Snare's root on him as he walks up to CS, then stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos","Hold W for his Rupture pop and stay outside Feral Scream's 300 range, because silenced you have no kit at all","Get Q poke chip and a roam/plate lead in early before his Feast stacks make him unkillable"],"foe":["Stack Feast off CS and your corpse so his HP balloons past anything your Overwhelm execute can touch","Land Feral Scream's silence inside 300, walk on top of you, and Feast for true damage no resistance stops","Soak your poke, scale to 2+ items, and out-tank your kit while his R ignores any peel or sustain"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are your window, so press them hard. At 2 you usually have Q + Solar Snare: when Cho'Gath steps up to last-hit, drop the E orb on him for the ~1.5s root, then rain Q on top and weave an empowered auto to start banking Overwhelm. He has no answer to that — his Q knockup is a slow telegraphed line you sidestep, and his only sustain is Feast stacks he doesn't have yet. The one thing to respect is his W silence: never trade in silence range, because if he cuts off your Q and W you lose your kiting tools. Poke from max range, hold E for when he commits, and take plate/chip while he's still a 600-HP nobody.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are where this lane tilts away from you. Your Q ranking up and Overwhelm stacking still let you bully him in raw poke, but the moment he hits 6 the math changes: Feast is true-damage percent-HP that ignores your low HP pool entirely, and you cannot be the one to get hit by W-silence-into-Q-knockup. If he lands that combo he walks on top and Feasts you for an execute no shield saves. Keep W up to eat his Q line and stay disengaged — you can't all-in a tank, so trade your Q poke for his CS denial and roam to a winnable lane instead of forcing kills here.","late":"At first item this is at its worst for you — he's stacked Feast HP off CS and kills, and your R detonating Overwhelm barely scratches a 4000+ HP frame you have zero hope of executing. But your passive scales forever, so the very late game swings back: from full build your empowered autos and Q chip a percent of even his massive bar, and R can detonate stacks on him from any range while you kite at 550. The rule is simple — never get caught. One W-silence into Q-knockup into Feast deletes you instantly. Stay behind your team, poke from max range, and let teammates body-block his engage.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s, but your 550-range Q and empowered auto out-poke his single melee Q knockup before he has any Feast HP.","At 2 your Solar Snare roots him as he walks up to last-hit, and Q rains free magic damage he can't sustain without Feast stacks.","With Q, E and W online you root and poke, but Rupture still reaches 950 — you outlast him only if you never stop moving.","Even but tense — your Q still bullies him, but at 6 his Feast true-damage percent-HP execute and W silence threaten to delete you the instant he gets on top.","Cho'Gath's spike: Feast is true damage at 175 range, so no amount of armour or MR helps, and Feral Scream silences your whole kit first.","His stacked Feast health out-tanks your kit — your R and Overwhelm cannot execute a 4000+ HP target, and true damage ignores resistances.","Your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm reclaims it: empowered autos and Q chip a percent of even his huge bar, and R detonates stacks from range while you kite at 550."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"darius","win":["Mel","Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your only clean window: one ranged 550-range auto plus Radiant Volley poke before he has E to pull you in."},{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"The lane flips — Apprehend (26s at rank 1) drags you into Decimate range and starts Hemorrhage bleed that keeps ticking as you walk away."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Darius's biggest threat window: Noxian Guillotine refreshes only on a killing blow, so bank Solar Snare's root to break the 460-range leap, not to open a trade."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your only real comeback: chain Q pokes and detonate Golden Eclipse from max range so you never give him an E-pull window."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 1 with a ranged auto plus Radiant Volley, then refuse every step into his E range","Step into Decimate range only after Apprehend whiffs — Solar Snare and Rebuttal answer the pull","Survive to 2+ items where you can stack Overwhelm with Q from 550 range and execute with R from safety"],"foe":["Land Apprehend (E) to pull you out of position and start stacking Hemorrhage bleed","Stack 5 Hemorrhage to enrage for massive AD, then land the true-damage Noxian Guillotine","Force you into melee range repeatedly so his pre-9 all-in dominance never lets you kite"]},"early":"Your one good moment is level 1: you have a 550-range auto and Radiant Volley before Darius has Apprehend, so chip him and hold the line. The instant he hits 2 it inverts — his E pull yanks you straight out of Solar Snare range and into his passive-empowered Q sweetspot, and every melee exchange stacks Hemorrhage bleed you literally cannot poke off because it ticks while you back away. Do not contest CS inside E range; take the lost minions. Save Solar Snare's root for the moment he flashes or E-pulls, never to start a fight.","mid":"Levels 4 through 6 are his lane, not yours — your Q ranks and Overwhelm stacks mean nothing if he's never out of E range to take the poke. He wins essentially every melee all-in from 1 to 9, so the game is: hug your turret, last-hit at max Radiant Volley range, and treat Solar Snare as a panic-disengage, not a trade tool. Apprehend is 26s at rank 1: the moment it whiffs you own roughly twenty seconds of free Q poke, and that is the only window worth stepping up in. At 6, wait for it to be down before you commit anything.","late":"This is where you claw back, but only if you survived lane near-even. From 2+ items your Q pokes from 550 range, Overwhelm stacks on every empowered auto, and Golden Eclipse detonates from any range — so you can chunk or execute him without ever letting Apprehend reach you. Never face him in a side lane where he can E-pull you into a wall; play with your team, kite to max range, and detonate R the instant he commits. One clean E on you and you still die — respect it all game.","whys":["You have a 550-range auto and Radiant Volley while he has no Apprehend yet — chip him and own this single window before it flips.","His E pull drags you out of Solar Snare range into a passive-empowered Q and starts Hemorrhage bleed you can't kite off.","With Q, E and Apprehend online he out-trades you in every melee exchange and his bleed punishes your short trades.","He out-trades you at melee, and every Decimate blade that clips you heals him — poke range is what starves his sustain.","Noxian Guillotine refreshes on kills, so one E-pull into 5 Hemorrhage stacks feeds a true-damage execute your root can't answer.","Your first item lets you chain Q pokes and detonate R from range, finally trading without stepping into his E.","From 2+ items you stack Overwhelm with 550-range Q and execute with Golden Eclipse from safety — but one clean E still kills you."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"drmundo","win":["Mel","Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Skill","Dr. Mundo","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Your only real window: ranged Q poke and a Solar Snare root chunk Mundo before his passive regen and Heart Zapper healing come online."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Mundo's E bonus damage and percent-HP Q cleaver flip the lane — his sustain now outpaces every chunk your Q can land."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Maximum Dosage's massive heal-over-time means your Golden Eclipse execute can't finish him — he tanks the detonate and walks away full."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His cleaver carves your current health while Sunfire/Heartsteel HP makes your Overwhelm stacks a rounding error — pure scaling loss."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his passive with the first Solar Snare — it soaks one immobilise, and the next root is the one that holds","Force every fight at 550 range so his gap-close-less body never closes the kiting gap","Reflect Infected Bonesaw with Rebuttal — it is a projectile on a 4s cooldown"],"foe":["Spam Infected Bonesaw to carve your current health while his regen heals it back","Hit Level 6 for Maximum Dosage so your R execute can't kill through the heal","Build HP and reach 2+ items where his drain-tank stats statcheck your poke"]},"early":"Your one good window is levels 1-2, before Mundo's passive regen and Heart Zapper healing are rolling. Land Solar Snare's root and rain Radiant Volley on him while he's stuck — every stack of Overwhelm you bank now matters because you won't get to bank much later. Infected Bonesaw is a thrown projectile, so Rebuttal eats it and throws it straight back at him: hold W for the cleaver, not for chip. His passive also soaks the first immobilise that lands, so treat your opening root as bait and the second one as the real hold.","mid":"From level 3 the lane inverts. Blunt Force Trauma's bonus AD and a current-health cleaver every 4 seconds carve your squishy frame while his passive regen heals back whatever you poke. You can't out-DPS the drain with a poke kit. At 6 it gets worse — Maximum Dosage instantly restores a slice of his missing health and keeps regenerating after, so even a fully-stacked Golden Eclipse won't finish him. Use your root purely to disengage and survive, not to commit.","late":"This is unwinnable in a straight 1v1 once he itemizes. Infected Bonesaw scales off your current health, so it bites hardest while you are full and tapers as you drop, and your Overwhelm stores raw magic damage that his huge HP pool and R heal simply absorb. Don't try to fight him — kite with Solar Snare and your move-speed Rebuttal purely to stay alive, farm side waves at max range, and let your team peel him while you poke from the back. You will never solo-kill this Mundo; your job is to not die to him.","whys":["At level 1 with just Q and your ranged auto you out-range him and poke freely before his passive regen and Heart Zapper heal exist.","Once he has the Q cleaver his percent-HP poke and self-heal start matching your Solar Snare chunk — it's a genuine coinflip on who steps up.","With E bonus damage and Heart Zapper healing online his sustain outpaces every chunk Radiant Volley lands — but Rebuttal still reflects the cleaver.","His drain-tank scaling kicks in: his Q carves your low HP while regen heals back your poke faster than you can stack Overwhelm.","Maximum Dosage's heal-over-time means your Golden Eclipse detonate can't execute him, but your root still buys a clean disengage — call it even.","First-item Mundo with HP facetanks your barrage, and his 975-range cleaver reaches a step further than Radiant Volley does.","Late, neither solo-kills cleanly — he's unkillable through his R but can't catch your 550-range kite, so it's a stalemate you survive."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"fiora","win":["Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Solar Snare root plus Q poke is your one clean punish window before Lunge (13s) and Riposte (24s) are both reliably up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks from range, but she Q-dashes in and W-parries your E root, so commit only when her W is on cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your AP + mana lets you chain Q pokes and W back her vitals procs, but a Fiora with Tiamat/serration starts winning extended trades if she sticks to you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Grand Challenge reveals all four Vitals and heals her whole side off them, out-scaling the chip your passive keeps stacking."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) on her so the root stops her Q-dash gap-close and locks a free Q barrage","Bait out her W parry on a throwaway Q, then commit your real E root and Golden Eclipse burst","Hold Rebuttal for her all-in — she throws no projectile to reflect, so it is 38s of flat damage immunity"],"foe":["Q-dash through your minions to close your 550 range and force a melee bruiser fight","Save Riposte to parry Solar Snare — blocking a root upgrades her counter-stab to a stun","Proc passive vitals with autos and Q angles to chunk your low-HP frame with true damage"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are your one real window, but Fiora makes even that tense. Q poke from max range to start Overwhelm and look for Solar Snare (E) as she steps up to last-hit, since the root cancels Lunge and guarantees a follow-up Q. The trap is Riposte (24s): it parries all damage, and blocking an immobilise upgrades its counter-stab from a slow into a stun — so your root is the worst thing you can feed it. Bait it with a Q, then commit. Rebuttal blanks her burst; it has nothing to reflect.","mid":"Levels 4-6 your Q ranks up and stacks accumulate, but this is when Fiora wakes up. Lunge is down to 9.5s and she closes your 550 range through the wave onto her Vitals. At 6 Golden Eclipse detonates everything from any distance, so the dream is E-root, stack, execute — but Riposte parries the cast, and if it catches the root you eat a stun. Bait it with a throwaway Q first, then commit the real E. Buy Grievous Wounds: Grand Challenge heals her side off Vitals.","late":"Late you keep poking and your infinitely-scaling passive stays relevant, but Fiora out-duels you the moment Lunge gets her on top of you. Grand Challenge reveals four Vitals and heals her whole side off them, and you have no dash and one root to peel a fed duelist. Play around your team, use Solar Snare to peel rather than to engage, and spend Rebuttal on her burst — it blocks damage, it does not reflect her. Never sidelane alone into a Fiora at her item spikes.","whys":["Fiora's vitals and clean Q-dash gap-close edge a one-ability Mel at level 1, before your Q count or Solar Snare exist to punish her step-up.","Even with your Q-plus-E root window, Riposte negates the root and stuns you for it, and Lunge answers your range, so she shades level 2.","Fiora can save W to parry your E or ability cast and Q-dash through your poke, neutralizing your strongest early trade pattern.","As her Q-dash and vitals true damage scale up, she closes your 550 range repeatedly and out-trades the windows you used to win.","Golden Eclipse threatens an execute, but she Lunges in and Riposte blanks your E or R cast, flipping the all-in if you misread her 24s.","Your AP spike helps, but a Fiora with her first item parries the key cast and out-duels you in any extended fight she forces.","Her vitals true damage and percent-HP shred melt your squishy frame late, and your single CC cannot keep a fed duelist off you."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Galio","Galio","Skill","Skill","Galio","Galio"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your one clean window — auto and chip him at 550 range before his W taunt and stacked MR turn your bolts to chip."},{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare root is your only guaranteed punish; land E when he steps up for a CS or you get nothing this lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse barely dents a Galio building MR, and at 6 Hero's Entrance reaches 4000 range — he stops laning and roams."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first MR/health item (Abyssal Mask, tank boots) makes your stacked Overwhelm execute math fall apart — you stop killing him."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit your Level 1-2 power spike and chunk him with Q + Solar Snare before he stacks magic resist","Hold W (Rebuttal) to eat and reflect his Q (Winds of War) tornado poke back at him","Watch the backward hop that starts Justice Punch — that tell is when Solar Snare must be ready"],"foe":["Stack magic resist and Abyssal Mask so your Overwhelm and Q poke barely register","Land Shield of Durand (W) taunt or Justice Punch (E) to lock you in melee where you die","Hold Hero's Entrance (R) to collapse on another lane or to knock you up for his jungler"]},"early":"Your Level 1 and 2 are the whole lane — at Level 1 sit at 550 range and auto him, and at 2 with Q + Solar Snare you get one guaranteed root-punish when he steps up to last-hit. Bait his Q (Winds of War) tornado and pop W (Rebuttal) to eat it and fire it back as your own magic damage; that wall is your best tool here. His tornado stops at 825 while your Q reaches 950 and your snare 1000, so you never need to walk up — his W (Shield of Durand) charges a taunt that drags you into melee, and once taunted you eat free Q-into-passive damage.","mid":"From Level 3 on this slips away fast. He starts stacking magic resist and your Q poke and Overwhelm stacks stop chunking him the way they chunk a juggernaut — he's an AP tank built specifically to blunt you. Respect his Justice Punch (E): 11s at rank 1, and Riot's own tell is that he briefly steps BACK before he charges — that hop is your cue to spend Rebuttal or walk. It only stops on a champion, so it comes through your wave untouched and minion cover buys you nothing. Use Solar Snare purely to peel and kite, never to commit.","late":"You don't win the late 1v1 and you barely scratch him — every MR item and his Abyssal Mask makes your stacked-Overwhelm execute math collapse, so stop hunting kills on him. Your value is range and your R (Golden Eclipse) detonating his team from max distance, not dueling Galio. Track his Hero's Entrance (R) at all times: 180s at rank 1 but reaching 4000 range and 5500 by rank 3, it shields his whole team into a fight two lanes away. Group, poke the squishies, and let your team trade for the tank.","whys":["Level 1 you have a 550-range auto and he doesn't, and he hasn't stacked MR yet — chip him freely before W and his magic resist come online.","Q plus Solar Snare's root is a real punish if he steps up for CS, but he can sidestep the orb or take it on minions, so it's a coin-flip skill window.","By 3 he has W (Shield of Durand) taunt charging and starts building magic resist — your poke stops mattering and his taunt threatens to drag you into a lost melee trade.","As his MR scales your Q and Overwhelm stacks fall off a cliff against an anti-AP tank, while Justice Punch charges through your wave to close the gap.","Golden Eclipse barely dents a magic-resist-stacking Galio, and his 180s Hero's Entrance turns every other lane into a fight he wins for free.","His first MR/health item breaks your execute threshold entirely — you can no longer convert stacks into a kill, so he owns every trade.","Full-build Galio is unkillable for you and his global R plus taunt let him erase you any time — concede the duel and play for range and team."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"gangplank","win":["Mel","Mel","Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank","Gangplank","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + E online lets you root him with Solar Snare the instant he steps up to light a barrel, then rain Radiant Volley on him before he can clear it."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"W joins your kit — Rebuttal eats his Parrrley and fires the 625-range projectile back as your own magic damage, turning his farm tool into your harass."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gangplank's danger window: Cannon Barrage goes global on a 160s cooldown, and a chained 3-barrel detonation can chunk your squishy frame faster than you stack Overwhelm toward the execute."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Essence Reaver/Trinity and crit come online his autos and barrels statcheck you; his global R and W cleanse let him roam and scale past your poke."}],"wants":{"you":["Root him with Solar Snare once Remove Scurvy is spent — your snare returns in 11s, his cleanse takes 22s","Hold Rebuttal for Parrrley — the keg blast is a zone, but his 625-range Q bounces back","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos early and end the lane before his crit items come online"],"foe":["Place barrels at the edge of your range and chain-detonate them to poke you down without committing","Use Remove Scurvy (22s at rank 1) to cleanse your Solar Snare root, then scale behind minions","Reach 2+ crit items and use global Cannon Barrage to take over the map past your fragile mid-game"]},"early":"Gangplank wants to sit back and chip you with barrels, but pre-6 his barrels are slow to chain and he is melee-range to refresh them — that is your window. At level 2 with Radiant Volley and Solar Snare, root him the second he steps up to light a barrel for CS and dump Q on top; he cannot clear the orange while snared. At 3, Rebuttal completely flips his poke: time the wall to swallow his Q or a barrel and you fire it back as magic damage while shielding the hit.","mid":"Your levels 4-5 are still strong, but the lane tilts at 6 — that is HIS spike, not yours. Cannon Barrage gives him global pressure and his barrel chains start to hurt your squishy frame faster than you execute him with Overwhelm. Keep poking at max range and bait Remove Scurvy early: it is 22s at rank 1 while Solar Snare is back in 11, so the second root always sticks. Do not stand in barrel-detonation range while building stacks, and respect that one clean 3-barrel chain can delete you.","late":"This is Gangplank's game and you have to accept it. He is a hard global scaler — crit items, Trinity/Essence Reaver and a map-altering Cannon Barrage out-statcheck your poke once he is itemized, and his W cleanse beats your only hard CC. Your infinitely-scaling passive keeps you relevant but you stay fragile and he kites your snare. Win the lane early, take plates and tempo off your level 2-3 advantage, and let your team answer his splitpush and global R rather than dueling him.","whys":["Mel: with one ability and your 550-range auto you out-poke a melee-range Gangplank who has to walk up to light and refresh his barrels.","Mel: Solar Snare's ~1.5s root plus Radiant Volley guarantees a punish the instant he steps into the barrel he just placed.","Skill: your Rebuttal wall can eat his Q and barrel poke and fire it back, but a good Gangplank spaces barrels at the edge of your range — it comes down to your timing vs his.","Gangplank: as his Q barrels rank and chain he starts trading even-to-up with your short windows while staying out of Solar Snare range.","Gangplank: Cannon Barrage adds map-wide pressure on a 160s cooldown, and a chained barrel detonation chunks your frame faster than Overwhelm executes him.","Gangplank: his first crit/Trinity spike turns autos and barrel chains into real burst, and Remove Scurvy cleanses your one root.","Gangplank: a hard global scaler statchecks you at 2+ items, his W beats your only CC, and Cannon Barrage takes over the map your poke can't touch."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Gnar","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Gnar's worst window for you — Boomerang Throw reaches 1100 to your Q's 950 and his Hop dodges Solar Snare, so his early poke beats your stack-building."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Mega Gnar's spike: Wallop is a 7s AoE stun that cancels your kite outright, and GNAR! adds a wall-slam stun — fight him in open ground, never near terrain."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Gnar's Rapidfire / first AD spike with mini-form kiting still out-trades you; bank Solar Snare's root to punish only when he whiffs a boomerang."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your power window: stacked Overwhelm plus AP lets Golden Eclipse execute him from range, and W eats his Boomerang to flip his only mini-form poke back on him."}],"wants":{"you":["Bank Solar Snare for the window after his Hop — it is 22s at rank 1 to your snare's 11s","Reflect Boomerang Throw with W — denying the catch costs him the refund","Stall to 2+ items where stacked Overwhelm and Golden Eclipse execute him from max range"],"foe":["Out-range your Q barrage with Boomerang Throw and kite back with Hyper move speed","Build Rage and force the fight in mega form for Wallop's 7s AoE stun","Flash or hop past your kite to land the stun and burst you before R detonates"]},"early":"Gnar is the rare melee-adjacent top that out-ranges and out-pokes you early. Boomerang Throw flies 1100 to your Q's 950 and his Hop sidesteps Solar Snare, so don't waste E hoping to root him on cooldown — but Hop is 22s at rank 1 to your snare's 11s, so the second root inside that window lands. Soak Q poke at max range, build Overwhelm slowly, and accept that levels 2-3 are his. Hold W to eat his next Boomerang: denying the catch keeps it on its full cooldown instead of a refunded one.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as your Q ranks and Overwhelm accrues, but level 6 is a real danger spike — once his Rage fills he transforms to Mega Gnar, and Wallop's AoE stun on a 7s cooldown cancels your entire kite. GNAR! only stuns if it slams you into terrain, so fight him in open ground and the ultimate becomes a knockback you survive. Respect his Rage bar like a cooldown: when it's near full, hug tower and don't step up for a Q. Only commit your R if his transform is down or you've already rooted him.","late":"This is where you reclaim the matchup. With 2+ items your Overwhelm stacks and AP turn Golden Eclipse into a long-range execute that detonates him no matter how far he kites, and your W reliably eats his Boomerang and fires it back as your own damage. Punish every whiffed boomerang with the Solar Snare root into a full Q-stack-R chain. Wallop's mega-form stun is still the one thing that kills you, so keep Flash for his all-in and hold fights away from walls.","whys":["Gnar's Boomerang Throw out-ranges your single ability and ranged auto at level 1, so he pokes you down before you can build Overwhelm stacks.","His level-2 Boomerang plus a Hop sidesteps your Solar Snare, denying the guaranteed root you'd normally land on a stepping-up melee.","At level 3 Rebuttal arrives and reflects Boomerang Throw, denying the catch that refunds its cooldown — his poke costs him.","Levels 4-5 even out as your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from trades, but his Hyper move speed still lets him kite your barrage.","Level 6 Mega Gnar arrives: Wallop is the unconditional AoE stun on 7s, while GNAR! only stuns if it slams you into a wall.","His first AD item plus mini-form Boomerang kiting still out-trades your poke; you can only punish when he whiffs a boomerang into your root.","From 2+ items your stacked Overwhelm and AP let Golden Eclipse execute him from range, and W eats his Boomerang to flip his only poke back on him."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"gragas","win":["Mel","Gragas","Mel","Gragas","Gragas","Gragas","Gragas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q+E spike: land Solar Snare's root and rain Radiant Volley on a Gragas stepping up for CS — your one clean early punish before Body Slam is online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gragas hits 6: Body Slam charges in and stuns, then Explosive Cask flips you under turret — one mistake with your root down becomes a kill from a screen away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Gragas with Lost Chapter/Rod and Drunken Rage's damage reduction soaks your Radiant Volley and engages anyway — your poke stops pricing him out."},{"when":"Late","text":"His Body Slam into Explosive Cask outranges the safety your no-dash kit needs — one missed Solar Snare and you have nothing to disengage."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2-3 first and land Solar Snare's root into a Radiant Volley barrage before Body Slam is online","Save Rebuttal for his Body Slam engage — it blanks the damage and the move speed carries you clear of him","Keep max poke spacing so his E body-slam can't reach you in one dash, and never get walked toward turret"],"foe":["Body Slam onto you the instant Solar Snare is down, closing your 550-range buffer and stunning","Soak your Radiant Volley under Drunken Rage and let Happy Hour heal it all back","Land Body Slam into Explosive Cask to flip you under turret for an unanswerable all-in"]},"early":"Your only real window is levels 2-3. Get Q + E first and the moment Gragas steps up to last-hit, land Solar Snare's root and dump Radiant Volley on him — that's a clean chunk Happy Hour can't fully heal back yet. After that, respect Body Slam: it charges your range down in one dash and stuns, and Drunken Rage has him taking reduced damage. Don't trade autos into him, don't push past river, and hold Rebuttal — it's your only disengage if he commits.","mid":"Once Gragas has Drunken Rage and Body Slam into Explosive Cask online, the lane tilts to him. He soaks Radiant Volley behind damage reduction while Happy Hour heals the rest back, so your poke stops pricing him out. At 6 he can charge in and Cask you under turret. But Body Slam is 14s at rank 1 against Solar Snare's 11s — spend the root on his engage and yours is back before his is.","late":"This stays his lane. Body Slam into Explosive Cask outranges the safety your dash-less, one-CC kit depends on, and Drunken Rage's damage reduction blunts the Overwhelm stacks you'd need to execute him. Your passive scales, but he's a durable AP bruiser who only needs one charge to delete your spacing. Group with your team, never sidelane alone into him, and keep Rebuttal for the moment he commits — it blanks the engage damage and the move speed carries you out.","whys":["Mel poke and Gragas last-hitting is even at level 1 — your single ability and ranged auto trade against Happy Hour healing him on every cast.","Gragas with Body Slam threat and Happy Hour sustain shrugs off your one-ability poke and out-bullies your squishy frame before your combo is online.","Mel's Q + E + W spike lets you root with Solar Snare and chunk him with Radiant Volley before Explosive Cask exists — your one favored window.","Body Slam closes your range in one charge and stuns, but it is 14s to your snare's 11s — your root is back first if you spend it on his engage.","Your Golden Eclipse window is real on paper, but Explosive Cask flips you under turret from a screen away — his level 6 spike beats your kill threat.","Gragas with Lost Chapter and Drunken Rage's damage reduction soaks your Radiant Volley and engages anyway — your poke stops pricing him out.","Body Slam into Explosive Cask outranges your dash-less disengage, and Drunken Rage blunts your Overwhelm chip — one missed root kills you."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"garen","win":["Mel","Garen","Garen","Garen","Garen","Garen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — root him as he steps up to last-hit and chunk him before his Q silence can reach you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range — once he's poked low it executes through his passive regen."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With mana and AP you chain-poke freely — but put Rebuttal up BEFORE Decisive Strike lands, because his silence denies the cast entirely."},{"when":"Late","text":"Garen builds Stridebreaker/Force of Nature and ignores poke — once he flashes onto you, his Q silence locks you and R executes your low HP."}],"wants":{"you":["Stay at 550 range and stack Overwhelm with Q + empowered autos before he can close","Land Solar Snare's centre root on his dash — his Q breaks the slow field but not the root","Hit Level 6 and detonate Golden Eclipse to execute him as his passive regen tries to heal the poke"],"foe":["Flash or Q-dash onto you, silence your cast and stick with Stridebreaker to deny the kite","Open with Decisive Strike's silence so your Rebuttal never gets cast, then walk you down","Survive to 2+ tank items so your poke stops mattering and his R executes your squishy frame"]},"early":"At Level 1 just poke with Q and hold range — he can only walk at you, and Perseverance stops regenerating the moment any damage touches him, so chip him off it rather than trading for trades' sake. The lane flips at Level 2: with Q + Solar Snare you root him the moment he steps up for CS, then Q the rooted target and walk off before his Q silence range can touch you. By 3 you add W — Decisive Strike silences, so Rebuttal has to go up before the dash connects, and after that it is your shield and move speed to peel.","mid":"This is your lane. His only gap-close is Decisive Strike (Q) and a Flash, so every all-in is telegraphed — but Decisive Strike breaks free of all slows, so Solar Snare's outer field will not hold him. The centre root is not a slow, so land the orb ON him and he stays put. At 6 Golden Eclipse turns the stacks you've built into a ranged execute that beats Perseverance, so poke him to ~40% and detonate. His Q silence cancels your cast, so never be mid-animation when the dash lands.","late":"You win this lane outright, but late Garen stops being a lane and becomes a statcheck — Stridebreaker and tank items let him eat your poke and his missing-HP true-damage R executes your squishy frame the instant he reaches you. Courage is 22s at rank 1 and gives tenacity on top of the shield, so a pre-cast shortens your root every time. Close the game on your first-item dominance; if it goes long, never get caught without Flash.","whys":["Garen is a strong level-1 walk-up bruiser and you've only got Q and your ranged auto — poke but don't commit, just deny his last-hits and his passive regen.","Q + Solar Snare lets you root him as he steps up for CS and punish, all from outside his Q silence range.","With W added you blunt his all-in, but Decisive Strike silences — Rebuttal has to be up before the dash lands, not after.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from every trade he can't answer — Decisive Strike is 8s, so his engage window is narrow and readable.","Golden Eclipse detonates your built stacks as a ranged execute that beats his passive regen and his short-trade pattern.","Mana and AP let you chain Q pokes and detonate freely while he has no tool to close the 550-range gap.","Garen out-scales the squishy: tank items eat your poke and his missing-HP true-damage R executes you the moment he reaches you."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"graves","win":["Mel","Skill","Graves","Graves","Skill","Graves","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + E online lets you land a Solar Snare root onto a Graves who has to walk into 525 auto range to last-hit, your one clean punish window before he gets E."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Once Graves has Quickdraw he rolls through your Q poke onto you — and dashing toward a champion gives him double True Grit resistances on arrival."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks from any range, so even when he kites out of melee you can chunk or finish him on the way out."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With your first AP item online and stacks chaining, you outrange and execute him before Eclipse Collector and tank stats let him reset the fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Root a stepped-up Graves with Solar Snare, and punish the reload when his shotgun runs dry","Hold W to eat his shotgun and fire it back — and stand behind your wave, since his bullets stop on units","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos so Golden Eclipse executes him from range when he dashes out"],"foe":["Use his E dash to roll through your Q barrage and close past 550 range onto you","Dash in for double True Grit resistances, then burst your squishy frame with a shotgun volley","Drop Smoke Screen to cut your vision and break line of sight on your poke, then all-in"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: at 550 range you poke with Q's barrage and chip free damage before Graves can do anything with one ability. The real prize is your Level 2-3 window — when he steps up to last-hit, fire Solar Snare and root him, then dump Q on top. His shotgun holds limited ammo and must reload, so that animation is the punish window nothing else in his kit covers. But respect the turn: the moment he has Quickdraw (usually level 3) he can roll through your bolts and onto you. His bullets cannot pass through units, so fight with your own wave between you.","mid":"This is where Graves takes over. As his shotgun and lethality scale, his E lets him close past your range on demand, and Smoke Screen cuts your sight range — you lose the target, not the attack, and cannot aim Radiant Volley at what you cannot see. You cannot trade autos: his burst beats your poke and you have no dash to reset. But his bullets cannot pass through units, so keep your own wave between you and the shotgun. Play around your one root: if he dashes in, Solar Snare him point-blank and W his return fire, then disengage. At Level 6 things even out because Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks from any range, so even a Graves who kites out eats damage on the exit.","late":"The late game swings back to you if you survived lane. Once your first AP item is online, your Q chains, Overwhelm accumulates off every poke, and Golden Eclipse executes him from a screen away before his Eclipse/Collector burst and bruiser-ADC tankiness let him reset the duel. End of the Line detonates on terrain, so he aims it at a wall to cut off a retreat you have no dash for — hold Flash for that, not for the damage. Fight from range with your team and finish him as he rolls out.","whys":["You poke at 550 with Q's barrage while Graves has only one ability and must walk into range to farm — pure free chip.","At level 2 your Q+E root can punish a stepped-up Graves, but his shotgun burst answers if he sidesteps the orb — genuinely even.","With Quickdraw online Graves rolls onto you gaining double True Grit resistances, and his shotgun burst shreds your squishy frame.","His shotgun and lethality scale faster than your Q ranks — he closes on demand and Smoke Screen cuts your sight, so you lose the target, not the attack.","Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm on him from any range, clawing the window back even when he kites out of melee — a true coinflip.","His lethality spike lets him pick the fight, dash in, burst and roll out — but Smoke Screen is 26s at rank 1, so the disengage is not free.","With your first AP item your Q chains and Golden Eclipse executes him from range before his burst and ADC-tank stats can reset the duel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"gwen","win":["Mel","Skill","Gwen","Mel","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare online: root her as she steps up for CS and chunk her with Q before her E dash and W mist exist to bail."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks from range, but she answers with Hallowed Mist untargetability and her own R reset chase."},{"when":"1st item","text":"She hits her Riftmaker/Nashor power tier; her Q true damage and E attack-speed start out-trading your single-target poke up close."},{"when":"Late","text":"Gwen scales past you: W untargets your Q barrage, E gap-closes onto your 550 frame, and Q true damage shreds you with no peel."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root the moment she steps into CS range, then layer Q bolts and empowered autos to stack Overwhelm","Force short trades before level 4 while she is a melee with no Hallowed Mist and no Skip ’n Slash refund","Save Rebuttal for Needlework — it is her only projectile, so it is the one cast you can send back at her"],"foe":["Reach level 6 and her Riftmaker spike so her Q true damage and W untargetability out-scale your poke","Bait Solar Snare, then E-dash onto you and sit in Hallowed Mist where your Q and stacks cannot touch her","Heal off A Thousand Cuts procs and farm safely to the 2-item window where she duels you flat"]},"early":"Gwen is a melee with no dash until Skip ’n Slash comes online, so levels 1-3 are your window. Hold Solar Snare for the exact moment she walks up to last-hit, root her, and chain Q bolts plus an empowered auto to stack Overwhelm. Don’t dump everything chasing into mist range. Snip Snip is a 450-range cone, not a missile, so Rebuttal blocks its damage but has nothing to reflect until Needlework at 6. She trades it all back with her passive heal, so this is a coin-flip, not a free lane.","mid":"Level 3 is your peak with Q, root and Rebuttal all online to poke, lock and negate her step-up. But once Skip ’n Slash refunds its own cooldown on every hit and W Hallowed Mist exists at 22s, the lane tilts. She baits your Solar Snare, dashes in, and parks in mist where your Q barrage and Overwhelm stacks find no target. At 6 Golden Eclipse detonates stacks from any range, but she answers with the mist and her R chase, so respect the all-in.","late":"This is Gwen’s game. She is a hard scaler and you are a 550-range mage with no dash and one CC. Once she has Riftmaker and Nashor, Snip Snip’s true damage chunks you, Skip ’n Slash closes your poke gap, and Hallowed Mist eats your kit on command. Buy Grievous Wounds early — A Thousand Cuts heals her off every proc. Your path is to snowball the early window; if lane went even, play picks and team detonations, never the 1v1.","whys":["Both of you are mediocre at level 1 with one ability up: you have Q poke and a ranged auto, she has no Skip ’n Slash yet, so it is a wash.","Level 2 she usually has Snip Snip true damage plus Skip ’n Slash to dash in and trade through your single bolt before you have your root.","Level 3 is yours: Q, Solar Snare root and Rebuttal all online let you lock an escape-less melee and poke her down before mist exists.","By levels 4-5 Skip ’n Slash and Hallowed Mist (22s) let her bait your root, dash in and sit untargetable where your Q and stacks whiff.","At 6 her R reset chase and Hallowed Mist out-leverage your Golden Eclipse detonation since she can vanish from your stacked damage on demand.","Her first item spike (Riftmaker/Nashor) turns Q true damage and E attack-speed into a melee burst that beats your short-range poke.","She out-scales hard: full-build Gwen untargets your barrage with W, gap-closes with E and shreds your frame with true damage and no peel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Mel","Skill","Skill","Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You never out-range Hextech Micro-Rockets' 1325 — land Radiant Volley on the choke while he has one turret down."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"His turret nest comes online — beams plus Micro-Rockets out-zone your Q, and CH-2 Grenade's 11s cooldown never shortens."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"UPGRADE!!! into CH-2 Grenade is his kill window — Golden Eclipse cannot save you while stunned inside three turret beams."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once you have Lost Chapter and an AP item your Q chip and Overwhelm stacks let you trade back through his turret HP — the lane re-opens to even."}],"wants":{"you":["Use Rebuttal's projectile wall to eat and return his W rockets or E grenade during a trade","Land Solar Snare's root on him while he's away from his turret nest so he can't retreat into the beams","Push waves with Radiant Volley to deny him free turret setups and keep Overwhelm stacks ticking"],"foe":["Stack three turrets on the wave so their beams plus W poke out-zone your max-range Q","Land CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade dead-centre to stun you inside the turret nest","Wall you off the minions with turret placement and out-sustain your short trades into a scaling 2-item lead"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely yours — a lone H-28 G Evolution Turret only threatens what walks into it, so tax the wave with Radiant Volley from its real 950 range and start stacking Overwhelm. Do not believe you out-range him, though: Hextech Micro-Rockets reach 1325, further than any spell you own, so the poke war is his the moment W is ranked. Sidestep CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade before you ever commit a Q — only a direct hit stuns, the ring around it merely slows, and eating that stun inside the nest at level 2-3 is how this lane goes wrong fast.","mid":"This is his window, not yours. From level 3 through 6 his turret nest zones you off the wave and out-DPS's your short trades, and your single CC can't break the setup the way it shreds an immobile melee. At 6 UPGRADE!!! into CH-2 Grenade is a kill on you — you have no dash and Golden Eclipse won't detonate fast enough while you are stunned in three beams. Play for the slow Q chip from 950, stepping up only in the 11s after his grenade whiffs, and use Solar Snare to root HIM when he strays from the nest rather than burning it to escape.","late":"The lane re-opens once you're itemized. With Lost Chapter mana and an AP item your Radiant Volley chips through turret HP, and accumulated Overwhelm stacks plus a ranked-up R let you threaten the execute through his zone — it grades back toward even. Rebuttal becomes a real tempo tool here: time the wall to return a rocket or grenade mid-trade and you flip his poke onto him. Don't try to out-splitpush his turret-walled waves; group, use your range to detonate from safety, and let your stacks do the work his turrets can't out-heal.","whys":["Before turrets stack, Radiant Volley's real 950 range taxes the wave — but Micro-Rockets reach 1325, so never trade poke.","One turret plus your Q is roughly even — bait his E grenade out before you commit so a root doesn't catch you on the wave.","His nest out-zones your Q, but every beam, rocket and grenade is a projectile Rebuttal throws back at him.","His turrets out-DPS a short trade, so tax from 950 and pop Rebuttal to walk out — it blanks damage and adds speed.","His E stun into a full beam field is a kill — you have no dash and Golden Eclipse can't detonate fast enough while rooted.","First item he's at his most dominant: rockets, beams and grenade out-chip your poke before your AP comes online.","With Lost Chapter and an AP item your Q and stacked Overwhelm trade back through turret HP — the lane grades back to even."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"illaoi","win":["Mel","Skill","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Radiant Volley's 950 range and Searing Brilliance autos chunk her before any tentacle or Vessel heal exists — your one window."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Test of Spirit (E) is up, any Radiant Volley that clips your own torn spirit echoes a share of that damage straight back onto you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Leap of Faith (R) spawns one tentacle per champion it hits — caught in that field with no dash, you simply do not walk out."},{"when":"Late","text":"You scale via Searing Brilliance and detonate R from range, but one missed Solar Snare into her field still kills you instantly."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 1-2 race — poke with Q and empowered autos before her tentacles and sustain come online","After Test of Spirit lands, stay inside leash range of your spirit — running out of it is what makes you a Vessel","Detonate Golden Eclipse (R) from max range and disengage with Rebuttal (W) — never duel her on her field"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit (E) to rip your spirit and force you off your own poke spacing","Trap you inside a full tentacle field where every slam heals her and shreds your HP","Hit her ultimate (Leap of Faith) when you have no Flash or Snare up to escape"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are the only part of this lane that belongs to you. Sit at Radiant Volley's 950 range, Q the wave-and-Illaoi overlap, and use your Searing Brilliance empowered autos to stack Overwhelm before she has a tentacle field built. At level 2 your Q-plus-Solar Snare can land a real punish if she steps up for a tentacle slam on the wave. But the second Test of Spirit and a couple of tentacles are online the math flips hard — every tentacle that connects with a champion heals her, so buy Grievous Wounds early or your chip just refunds itself.","mid":"This is where you lose the lane. By 3-5 her tentacle field out-sustains your whole poke pattern and Harsh Lesson leaps 400 units onto you every 4 seconds. If Test of Spirit rips your spirit, do NOT sprint away — leaving it, or letting it die, is exactly what turns you into a Vessel. Stay inside its leash, out of tentacle reach, and wait it out. At 6 Leap of Faith spawns a wall of slams; with zero dashes and one CC, getting caught in that field is just death. Hold Solar Snare as peel, never as engage.","late":"You claw a little back late as Searing Brilliance keeps scaling and you can detonate Golden Eclipse from any range without stepping into her field. Play purely as a disengage poke threat in teamfights — Rebuttal (W) her tentacle-empowered abilities, chip her down from max range, and let your team body her since she's immobile off her field. But one missed Snare or one facecheck into a fresh tentacle wall still erases you instantly, so respect her R timer all game.","whys":["At level 1 with just Q and your ranged auto you out-poke her before any tentacle field exists — chunk her free.","Your level-2 Q plus Solar Snare can punish a step-up, but her first tentacle slam already starts healing the damage back — it is a coin-flip window.","With Test of Spirit up, a Radiant Volley that clips your own torn spirit echoes that damage back onto you — reposition first.","Her ranked-up tentacle field out-sustains your poke entirely and her E forces you off your spacing — you cannot duel here.","Leap of Faith spawns a wall of tentacles and you have no dash to escape it — one R catch is lethal.","Her tentacle DPS plus sustain on her field outscales your first-item poke spike in any extended fight.","You detonate Golden Eclipse from range and disengage with W, but a single missed Snare into her field still one-shots you — genuinely knife's-edge."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"irelia","win":["Mel","Skill","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia","Irelia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare (E) is your one clean punish window — root her if she walks up to CS before her Q dashes are up."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Irelia hits her Q-reset rhythm; once she can dash minion-to-you and E-stun, your poke advantage flips and she dives your barrage."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Defiant Dance (W) cuts physical damage only and heals nothing — your magic burst goes through it, so 6 is a real window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Irelia's Trinity/Sheen spike is her takeover — her Q-resets through the wave ignore your kiting and her passive shred eats your squishy frame."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) root the instant she dashes in, then back off and re-poke with Q from max range","Hold Rebuttal (W) to eat her Q dash damage or block follow-up, never waste it early","Buy Grievous Wounds — Bladesurge heals on cast and refreshes off Marked targets, so a big wave is free sustain"],"foe":["Get a minion or your champ to Q-dash to, resetting it to close the gap past your poke","Land E stun after the Q gap-close, then Bladesurge-heal off the wave and full-combo you","Snowball a Sheen/Trinity lead and use Q-resets to dodge your Solar Snare and dive you repeatedly"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is the only stretch you breathe. Throw Radiant Volley (Q) at max range to chip her and stack Overwhelm, and at 2 keep Solar Snare (E) up — if she steps into the wave for a last-hit before her Q dashes are online, root her and punish with Q. Do NOT walk up to auto her: the second she has minions to Q-reset off she closes the gap and your 550 range stops mattering. Bait nothing here, just farm and land free pokes while she's dash-starved.","mid":"Levels 3-6 she takes over. Once Irelia can Q-dash minion-to-you and chain into her E stun, your kiting dies — she is inside your range and her passive armour shred melts you. Defiant Dance is the one button that does nothing here: it cuts physical damage only and heals nothing, so keep firing magic into the charge. Her sustain is Bladesurge, which refreshes off any Marked target — in a big wave she chains it. Save Solar Snare purely as peel the moment she dashes, not as poke; whiff it and you're dead. Hold Rebuttal to soak the dash. Give up CS, ping for ganks, and never sit inside stun range.","late":"It stays rough. Once Irelia itemizes a Sheen/Trinity her Q-resets let her flicker through the whole wave onto you, and a fed Irelia simply runs you down before your Overwhelm stacks detonate. Vanguard's Edge is the part to fear: the blades leave a wall, and with no dash in your kit that wall is the thing that actually kills you — hold Flash for it, not for the damage. Your scaling passive matters in teamfights, not the 1v1. Group, stay behind frontline, and detonate Golden Eclipse from max range while your team peels.","whys":["You out-range her with Radiant Volley (Q) and she has no minion to Q-reset off yet — poke freely before her dashes come online.","Your Q + Solar Snare root can punish a step-up, but she's a Q-rank from her dash rhythm — it's a coin-flip who lands first.","At 3 she Q-dashes minion-to-you and E-stuns through your poke; your kiting collapses the moment she has reset targets.","Her Q-resets and passive shred eat your short trades as Overwhelm ranks up — she's inside your range every exchange now.","Defiant Dance reduces physical damage and does not heal, so your magic burst ignores it — her W is dead weight against you.","Irelia's Sheen/Trinity spike turns every Q-reset into a dive your single CC can't answer — she owns the all-in.","A fed Irelia statchecks your squishy frame and dashes onto you faster than your stacks detonate — survive via team, not the duel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"jax","win":["Mel","Skill","Jax","Jax","Jax","Jax","Jax"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"One ability and a 550-range auto — last-hit from max range and chip Jax before he has E to dodge it."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your only real window: Q poke plus a Solar Snare root, and Counter Strike is 17s at rank 1 — that whiff is a free trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Jax R flips the duel — his Grandmaster's stats plus E Counter Strike stun mean his all-in beats your Golden Eclipse burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Jax's Trinity/Blade spike is his takeover — every Q-W gap-close in CS range is now a death sentence for you."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold 700-plus and deny him a leap target — Leap Strike cannot reach from where your 950 Q and 1000 snare land","Hold W Rebuttal for his Q-W engage — the shield plus move speed buys the escape you have no dash for","Keep him at 550 range and stack Overwhelm off Q chip so an early skirmish can still snowball before he itemizes"],"foe":["Open on the Empower auto-reset wind-up, then Leap Strike past your poke once E is down","Pop E Counter Strike during your auto-poke to dodge it and stun you for the kill","Reach Trinity Force and R, then dive your squishy 550-range frame every wave"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are the only patch of grass you own. With one ability and your 550-range auto you can chip Jax before he has E Counter Strike to dodge your poke, and at 2 the Q barrage plus Solar Snare's root can punish him if he steps up for a cannon. But understand what you're racing: the moment he hits 3 he has Q leap, W reset and E dodge-stun all online, and you have zero dashes to answer the gap-close. Never throw Q into auto range hoping to trade — that's exactly when he E's, eats the auto, and runs you down.","mid":"This is where it slips away. Jax's Q-W gap-close erases your 550 range, and if you auto or Q into his E Counter Strike window he dodges it and stuns you — your single root on E is your whole defense and it's on a long cooldown. Hold W Rebuttal for his actual engage, not his poke; the shield and move speed are the only thing buying you space. At 6 his Grandmaster's stats make his all-in flatly stronger than your Golden Eclipse burst, so don't trade R for R hoping to win it. Root-and-disengage, never root-and-fight.","late":"You do not win this 1v1, full stop — an itemized Jax with Trinity and R out-statchecks your squishy frame and his E dodges your autos and R-detonation autos alike. Your job is to never be the one he finds. Stay at max range in fights, save E Solar Snare to peel him off yourself or a carry, and use your infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive on whatever else walks into your poke. If he's fed, this is a flash-or-die lane — ping for ganks and let your team body him, because you can't.","whys":["You have one ability and a 550-range auto while Jax has no E to dodge it yet — chip him freely from max range.","Your Q poke plus Solar Snare's root can punish a Jax who walks up, but he has the tools to dodge once he hits 3 — it is a coinflip window.","At 3 he has Leap Strike, Empower and Counter Strike up — but Q is only 700 range and needs a unit to jump to.","Counter Strike eats the autos you stack Overwhelm with, but never your spells — keep the Q barrage going anyway.","His R Grandmaster's stats plus E stun make his all-in flatly stronger than your Golden Eclipse burst at 6.","Jax's Trinity Force spike turns every Q-W into a death sentence for your 550-range squishy frame.","An itemized Jax out-statchecks you and dodges your autos with E — you cannot win the duel, only kite and peel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"jayce","win":["Skill","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Skill","Jayce","Jayce"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Acceleration Gate (E) then Shock Blast (Q) fired through it out-ranges you — he chunks you off CS before Q+E come online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks from any range — your one real kill window if you landed Solar Snare to set up the burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Mercury Cannon's first hit shreds your armour and MR, then Thundering Blow knocks you back into the combo — his hardest all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"You finally out-scale a falling-off Jayce with your infinite Overwhelm passive — group and detonate stacks before he can poke-pick you."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Rebuttal for the Shock Blast he sends through his own Acceleration Gate, not for the ungated ones","Land Solar Snare's root the moment he steps to cannon range, then chain Q poke to stack Overwhelm","Survive to two items where your infinite-scaling passive overtakes his fading poke"],"foe":["Drop Acceleration Gate, fire Shock Blast through it, and keep you below the execute threshold all lane","Open with the Mercury Cannon armour-and-MR shred, then Thundering Blow into the combo","End the lane on his poke lead before your Level 6 R and late scaling come online"]},"early":"Jayce out-pokes you outright in the first three levels and that is the honest truth — a Shock Blast fired through his own Acceleration Gate gains missile speed, range and damage, and he does it before you have Solar Snare or Rebuttal to answer. The gate is your tell: once it drops, the empowered bolt is coming through it, so hold Rebuttal for that one and let the ungated bolts go. Don't walk up to throw a Q he'll gate-poke you for — last-hit at max range, hold E for when he commits to cannon range.","mid":"This stays his lane through levels 4-5 — his Shock Blast keeps you below the Overwhelm thresholds you need and you can't trade back without eating the hammer combo. Know what starts it: Mercury Cannon is a 6s stance swap whose first attack strips your armour and magic resist before anything else lands, so that auto is the tell, not the leap. At 6 you get your one swing: land Solar Snare's root and Golden Eclipse detonates whatever stacks you built, from range. Miss it and Thundering Blow knocks you into the combo instead.","late":"Here is your light at the end: Jayce falls off and your passive scales forever. Once you're two-plus items your Overwhelm stacks chunk and execute, and grouped fights let you detonate R on multiple stacked enemies from max range where his single-target poke can't pick you. Don't try to re-fight the lane 1v1 on his terms — play for teamfights, stack Overwhelm with Q barrages, and keep W ready to deny the engage that catches squishy you.","whys":["Shock Blast through his own Acceleration Gate out-ranges and out-damages your Q at level 1 — he pokes you off CS before a stack builds.","Even with Q+E you can't trade into his cannon poke; he chunks you the instant you step up to throw, and your root won't reach.","Thundering Blow's knockback plus the cannon burst beats your Q-E-W trade, and you have no dash to reset the spacing.","Your Overwhelm stacks can't accumulate because his Q keeps you out of range; he owns levels 4-5 on poke alone.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks from any range — land Solar Snare's root first and this is the one window you genuinely threaten him.","First item, Mercury Cannon shreds your armour and MR and Thundering Blow opens the combo before your R is back — his peak, not yours.","Jayce falls off and your infinite-scaling Overwhelm passive overtakes him — group, stack, and detonate R from range to reclaim the game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Karma","Karma","Skill","Karma","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Karma's Mantra is live from level 1, so her RW Focused Resolve root is on the table immediately — but both Qs are 950, so the poke war is symmetric, not lost."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates my accumulated Overwhelm from any range — this is my one clean window to flip the lane and threaten an execute through her shield."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Karma's Mantra-empowered W root makes my dashless frame an easy gank setup — respect the 12s tether timer or get collapsed on."},{"when":"Late","text":"Both go even — her shield-and-speed peel cancels my poke, my passive execute claws value back, and the lane decides on flanks and flash."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Solar Snare for when Karma steps up to poke, then chain Q bolts onto the rooted target to stack Overwhelm fast","Bank Overwhelm stacks for level 6 so Golden Eclipse detonates for a real chunk or execute from max range","Use Rebuttal to eat her Q poke and her RQ projectile, then fire it back as my own magic damage"],"foe":["Trade her low-cooldown Q into mine at matched 950 range and reset with E shield-and-speed before I answer","Land Focused Resolve (W) inside 675 to set up a collapse on my dashless frame","Spam E shields on herself to negate my Q chip and out-sustain my short trade windows"]},"early":"Karma plays the early bully here, but not on range — Inner Flame and Radiant Volley are both 950, so the Q trade is symmetric and I can take it. What she really has is E shield-and-speed to step in, poke, and slide back. The threat to respect is Focused Resolve (W): Mantra is live from level 1, so RW root-and-tether exists immediately. It is only 675 range though, against my 1000 Solar Snare — hold my ground, out-space the tether, and if it does land, break it by walking. Farm, eat what I must, and bank Overwhelm stacks.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay hers — her empowered Q and E sustain out-trade my short windows, and her shields erase my Radiant Volley chip. My one window is level 6: once Golden Eclipse is up, every banked Overwhelm stack becomes detonate-from-anywhere damage, so set it up by landing Solar Snare and chaining Q bolts on the rooted target before I pop R. Focused Resolve is a flat 12s at every rank and never shortens, so count it and step up inside it. Bait her E shield first; with it down, R plus a Q threatens the execute.","late":"Late this evens out. Karma's shield-and-speed peel still cancels my poke and keeps her squad mobile, but my infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive and Golden Eclipse's any-range execute claw real value back in teamfights — I can detonate stacks on a carry from the backline she can't peel from. Never get caught alone: I have no dash and one root, and a Focused Resolve tether into a flank ends me. Win the fight on vision and let my R reach what her shields can't.","whys":["Inner Flame and Radiant Volley are both 950, so level 1 is an even poke trade — what beats me is her E shield-and-speed resetting the exchange.","Her RW root-and-tether locks my dashless frame, but it is only 675 range against my 1000 snare — I get to pick the spacing.","With Q, E and her empowered RQ online she pokes, shields and roots faster than my Overwhelm stacks can accumulate.","Levels 4-5 her low-cooldown Q and E sustain out-trade my short windows and her shields erase my Radiant Volley chip.","At 6 Golden Eclipse detonates my banked Overwhelm from any range — my one even window to flip the lane through her shield.","First item, her Mantra-empowered W root turns my flashless, dashless frame into a free jungle collapse.","Late it evens — her shield-and-speed peel cancels my poke, but my scaling passive and any-range R execute reclaim the value."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"kassadin","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Skill","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke plus a Solar Snare root lands a guaranteed punish on a Kassadin who steps up to last-hit — his weakest, most melee-able window."},{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Radiant Volley plus empowered autos stack Overwhelm quickly, but Void Stone's magic reduction is always on and Null Sphere shields against magic — buy penetration, not more raw AP."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His first Riftwalk: R blink turns the lane from a poke war into a hide-and-seek, letting him dodge my Solar Snare and start closing the gap on cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kassadin's takeover — stacked Riftwalks plus Rod of Ages/Rocketbelt let him blink onto my squishy body and burst me before R detonates; his Q shields him, it never silences me."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root every time he oversteps, then chain Radiant Volley and empowered autos to stack Overwhelm before he hits 6","Build magic penetration early — Void Stone's reduction is always on and Null Sphere shields magic","Win the lane outright before his 2+ item Riftwalk spike — detonate Golden Eclipse on stacked Overwhelm while he still has to melee me"],"foe":["Survive to 6 and use Riftwalk to dodge my Solar Snare and close the range my poke depends on","Farm Force Pulse charges off my own Q and E casts, then cone-slow me as he blinks in","Stack Riftwalks at 2+ items to blink in, burst my squishy frame, and out-scale my poke"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are mine because Kassadin is a melee with no Riftwalk yet — he has to walk into my 550 range to last-hit, and that's where I punish him. At level 2 I pick up Solar Snare and Radiant Volley: root him on any greedy CS step, then rain Q on the snared field and feed empowered autos to stack Overwhelm. Two things blunt that chip, and neither is his passive shield, because he hasn't got one: Void Stone is flat magic damage reduction that is always on, and Null Sphere grants a shield that absorbs magic specifically. His Q does not silence — it interrupts channels, and I have none — so Rebuttal is never locked out of my hands.","mid":"Levels 4-5 I keep ranking Q and stacking Overwhelm, but this is where it levels out — he's farming for 6 and I can't kill through Void Stone and a Null Sphere shield without a root landing first. Watch what I am feeding him: Force Pulse charges off spells cast in his vicinity, so my own Q and E casts load the cone he slows me with. The real shift is level 6: Riftwalk is 5s at rank 1 and falls to 2s by rank 3, so his blink sidesteps the single tool my whole zone depends on. Hold Solar Snare for when he commits rather than throwing it on cooldown, because a whiffed root against a blinking Kassadin just hands him a free window to walk up.","late":"This is Kassadin's game, full stop — he's a hard scaler and I'm a fragile artillery mage with no dash and one CC. At 2+ items his stacked Riftwalks let him blink straight onto me, and every point of damage I own is magic, which is exactly what Void Stone reduces and what his Null Sphere shield absorbs — magic penetration is not a luxury item here, it is the build. He never silences me, so Rebuttal and Solar Snare are always in hand; the problem is landing them on a 2s blink. I don't solo-duel a fed Kassadin. I take plates with my early lead, pressure the map so his scaling never matters, and detonate R from max range before he closes.","whys":["Kassadin is a weak, escape-less melee at level 1 while I poke from 550 range — chip him with Radiant Volley and empowered autos before his shield matters.","Solar Snare's root plus Q punishes any step-up to last-hit, and a pre-Riftwalk Kassadin has no way to escape the follow-up — this is my cleanest kill window.","Even now — I still out-range him and stack Overwhelm, but Void Stone's flat magic reduction blunts every point of my chip and I need a root to kill.","It stays a coin-flip through 4-5: I rank Q and accumulate stacks, but he's farming safely toward 6 and his shield keeps eating my poke.","Riftwalk comes online and his blink dodges my Solar Snare — the lane flips from my poke war into his hide-and-seek as he starts closing the gap on cooldown.","His first item plus stacked Riftwalks let him blink past my poke; he never silences me, but a 2s blink dodges the root I depend on.","Full-build Kassadin out-scales me hard — he Riftwalks onto my squishy body and bursts me before R detonates, so I play safe and let my team handle him."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"kayle","win":["Mel","Mel","Skill","Skill","Kayle","Kayle","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare online lets you root her into a free Radiant Volley as she steps up to last-hit — punish a Kayle who has nothing but melee autos and an E poke before level 6."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Stacked Overwhelm from repeated Q pokes turns every trade into a chunk on a meleed-out Kayle who can't fight back through your range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Divine Judgment goes invulnerable through your Golden Eclipse execute — at 160s bait it out, then detonate, as her ranged form starts to bite."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Her threat peak: ranged-form Nashor's/Shojin Kayle out-DPSes your poke, kites your single Solar Snare, and her R survives anything you burst — close the lane long before here."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack Overwhelm with repeated Radiant Volley pokes and empowered autos so a meleed-out Kayle is always low before level 6","Land Solar Snare's root the instant she walks up to last-hit and follow with Q to deny her CS and chunk her","Buy Grievous Wounds for Celestial Blessing and end the lane in your 1-5 window, before her ranged form"],"foe":["Survive to level 6 and pop Divine Judgment invulnerability to negate your execute and burst window","Reach level 11 and 2+ items for ranged-form autos that kite your single Solar Snare and out-DPS your poke","Farm safely with E poke and waveclear, soaking XP until her infinite scaling outpaces your fragile frame"]},"early":"Kayle is one of the weakest early laners in the game and you punish exactly that — at level 1 she has melee autos and Starfire Spellblade, which costs no mana, so trade knowing the E is always up. Level 2 is your window: Q plus Solar Snare means the moment she steps up to last-hit, you root her and rain Q on top, and her short range gives no answer. Hold Rebuttal for Radiant Blast — it is a projectile, so the reflect sends her poke and its resistance shred back at her.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep her meleed out — rank up Q, keep landing Radiant Volley as she walks for CS, and let Overwhelm stacks pile up so each trade hurts more than the last. This is genuinely even-skill, not a free win: she is farming under tower and scaling, and if you whiff Solar Snare you give up your only lockdown. Buy Grievous Wounds early, because Celestial Blessing heals her on a flat 15s. Level 6 flips toward her — Divine Judgment is 160s at rank 1, and her invulnerability simply waits out Golden Eclipse and your whole burst window, so bait the ult first, then re-detonate.","late":"Once Kayle hits level 11 and 2+ items she takes the lane and the game. Ranged form means she out-ranges your Radiant Volley, kites your one Solar Snare with her movement, and her R survives anything Golden Eclipse can throw at her — your fragile 550-range frame just gets DPS'd down. Do not try to 1v1 a fed Kayle in a sidelane; you lose that statcheck. Your job was to make her early miserable and end before this window, then pivot to grouping where your long-range Q and R disengage matter and your team focuses her before her invuln resets.","whys":["You out-range a level-1 Kayle who has only melee autos and a free Starfire Spellblade — chip her with Radiant Volley and stack Overwhelm for free.","Q plus Solar Snare lets you root her as she steps up to last-hit and chunk her with a follow-up Volley before she has any way to fight back.","It's even-skill — your stacked Overwhelm pokes hurt, but she's safely farming under tower and one missed Solar Snare gives up your only lockdown.","You still out-trade a meleed-out Kayle as Q ranks and Overwhelm piles up, but she's soaking XP toward the R spike, so it's a coin-flip on execution.","Divine Judgment’s invulnerability phases through your Golden Eclipse execute and your entire burst window, so she survives the all-in you owned a level ago.","Her first ranged item lets her kite your single Solar Snare and poke your squishy frame from outside your Volley range as her DPS comes online.","Full-build ranged Kayle out-ranges, out-DPSes, and out-survives you with R — don't sidelane-duel her; group and have your team kill her before she resets invuln."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q Radiant Volley plus Solar Snare gives me a guaranteed root-punish if Kennen walks into Q range to last-hit, my best early stack-building window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kennen's takeover: a level-6 Slicing Maelstrom plus a third Mark of the Storm stuns me through my one root and bursts my squishy frame before I can detonate Golden Eclipse."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Hextech Alternator / Liandry's spike out-pokes my Q from energy he never runs dry, chunking me down while I'm mana-gated between Radiant Volleys."},{"when":"Late","text":"Even ground again: my infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive plus Rebuttal eating his projectiles lets me trade the poke war back if I survive his mid-game."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) roots to lock Kennen and stack Overwhelm with Q Radiant Volley before his Mark of the Storm can stun me","Hold Rebuttal (W) for Thundering Shuriken — his Q is his one projectile; Electrical Surge is on-hit and never reflects","Survive his level 6 and first-item poke window, then out-scale with my Overwhelm passive into the late game"],"foe":["Stack Mark of the Storm with Q-W poke and Electrical Surge autos to land the third-stack stun on me","Hit level 6 and chain Slicing Maelstrom into the stun-lock to burst my squishy body before I detonate R","Abuse his energy economy to out-poke my mana-gated Radiant Volley between item spikes"]},"early":"Level 1 is a near-mirror poke standoff — we're both 550-range mages, so I trade Q for his Thundering Shuriken and neither of us commits. My real window is level 2: with Radiant Volley and Solar Snare I can root him the instant he steps into Q range to last-hit, then dump a Q on the rooted target to start stacking Overwhelm. Hold Rebuttal for his Shuriken — eating it and firing it back swings a trade hard. Don't burn E as poke; it's my only CC and I need it to punish his oversteps, not to chip.","mid":"Levels 3-5 tilt to Kennen and I have to respect it. Once he has Q and W up he stacks Mark of the Storm faster than I can answer, and his energy means he never runs dry the way my mana does between Radiant Volleys. Keep him snared when I can and refuse the extended poke war on his terms. Level 6 is his spike, not mine: Slicing Maelstrom plus a third mark stuns me through my single root and bursts my fragile frame before I can detonate Golden Eclipse — never sit in Maelstrom range with my E down. Bait his stun, then play for the gaps between his ult windows.","late":"His first-item Liandry's / Alternator spike is his hardest poke window — he chips my low HP from energy while I'm mana-gated, so I farm safe and don't contest him head-on. But the lane swings back to even late: my Overwhelm passive scales infinitely, Rebuttal reflects Thundering Shuriken, his one projectile — Electrical Surge is on-hit and passes through, and once I have mana and AP I can detonate R from any range. Don't try to win the mid-game duel — survive it, then use my range and the Solar Snare root to punish him in teamfights where his squishy frame is just as exposed as mine.","whys":["It's a 550-range mirror poke standoff — my Q Radiant Volley trades evenly with his Thundering Shuriken and neither of us can safely commit yet.","Kennen edges it as his Mark of the Storm chain comes online — even with my Solar Snare root, his Q-W poke stacks toward a stun faster than I can answer on cooldown.","He owns the wave once his full poke is up — his energy never runs dry while my Radiant Volley is mana-gated, so he out-chips me in any extended trade.","His Mark of the Storm stacks plus Electrical Surge autos out-pressure my single Solar Snare root, and he pokes my squishy frame from outside my commit range.","His level-6 Slicing Maelstrom into a third mark stun-locks me through my one root and bursts me before I can detonate Golden Eclipse — this is his takeover.","His Liandry's / Alternator spike out-pokes my mana-gated Q from infinite energy, chunking my low-HP body down between Radiant Volleys.","Even again late — my infinitely-scaling Overwhelm passive and Rebuttal eating his projectiles let me trade the poke war back if I survived his mid-game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"kled","win":["Mel","Skill","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your 550-range auto plus a single ability lets you chip his mount HP before he ever gets a Bear Trap on a Rope in range."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Kled has Q hook + remount, his Skaarl-charge dismount answer flips the lane — he sticks to you through Solar Snare's root and shreds your squishy frame."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His Chaaaaaaaarge!!! R is a free gap-close engage that ignores your kiting entirely — he can flank a wave and be on you before you finish a Q channel."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kled scales hard with bruiser items; even in an even lane his remount sustain and dismount burst out-statcheck your poke once he's itemized."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Level 1 by poking his mount HP with max-range Q and empowered autos before he can hook","Land Solar Snare's root on a dismounted Kled to kite and stack Overwhelm for an R execute","Hold Rebuttal to eat his Bear Trap on a Rope projectile and fire it back as your own damage"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) to reel himself onto you and force a committed dismount fight","Skaarl-charge dismount to stick through your root and out-trade your short windows","Use Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) to engage from off-screen and remount mid-fight for the sustain swing"]},"early":"Level 1 is the one clean window I get — Kled starts mounted but his Skaarl mount has its own HP pool, and my 550-range Q plus empowered autos chip it for free before his Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) can hook me in. The instant he hits 2 and his hook is online, that flips: if his Q lands he reels himself onto me, and I have zero dashes to peel off. Hold Rebuttal (W) specifically for his Q grab — eating that projectile and firing it back is my only hard answer to his engage. Never walk up to throw Radiant Volley (Q) when his hook is up.","mid":"This is Kled's lane to take. A dismounted Kled who Skaarl-charges sticks to me right through Solar Snare's (E) root and remounts mid-fight, healing the chunk I just dealt — my short trade windows don't out-DPS his remount sustain. At 6 his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) is a free gap-close from off-screen, so I can be poking a safe wave and still get run down. I keep Rebuttal for the Q hook, save Solar Snare to root him AFTER he commits (not as a poke tool), and call for jungle help rather than trying to 1v1 a remounting Kled.","late":"Past two items this stays Kled's window — he's a hard scaler, and his bruiser build plus dismount burst and remount sustain out-statcheck my poke even though my Overwhelm passive scales infinitely. My one path is range discipline in teamfights: detonate Golden Eclipse (R) on stacked targets from max distance and never let him flank me with his charge. If he Chaaaaaaaarge!!!-engages onto me without my flash up, I'm dead — peel and positioning are everything, because the straight 1v1 belongs to him.","whys":["Kled's Skaarl mount has its own HP and his hook isn't online yet, so my 550-range Q and empowered autos chip him for free before he can engage.","At 2 his Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) reels him onto me and I have no dash to escape — his remount fight beats my single root.","With Q hook plus dismount online he sticks through Solar Snare's root and out-trades my short windows; my W can only answer one hook.","Repeated trades favor his remount sustain — every chunk I land he heals back on Skaarl, while my squishy frame can't absorb his dismount burst.","Chaaaaaaaarge!!! is a 140s off-screen gap-close that ignores my kiting entirely and shields him on arrival — level 6 is his, not mine.","His first bruiser item plus remount sustain out-paces my first-item poke, and he can engage onto me on R's cooldown faster than I can reset.","Still his lane late — bruiser stats and remount sustain out-pace my poke; max-range Golden Eclipse keeps me relevant only if his charge never lands."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare lands a guaranteed root-punish — your one clean early window before his W block negates your poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm, but his R isolates you and strips his own resists for the all-in — he wins the trade if he reaches you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Ntofo pull plus a 10s Footwork dash close your 550 range once he has a sustain item — your poke can no longer kite him off."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your infinite-scaling passive keeps you relevant, but a fed K'Sante one-shots your squishy frame through the All Out form — never get caught alone."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root before he gets W up so your Q barrage and Overwhelm stacks actually connect","Hold Rebuttal for the Path Maker stun, not for Ntofo chip — it is your only layer","Hold E for his W dash-in and detonate R from max range before his All Out form reaches you"],"foe":["Block your Q poke with W and dash onto you the instant you step into 550 range","Land the two-stack Ntofo pull, then All Out you through a wall and burst your squishy frame","Scale to first item and the All Out form where your kite no longer outruns his gap-close"]},"early":"Open careful and cash the one clean window you get: at 2, Solar Snare's root into a full Q barrage is a guaranteed punish when he steps up — and even that is only a coin-flip, because Path Maker's charge soaks the damage and stuns straight back. From 3 the lane slides his way: he eats your Q inside that charge, walks you down off one root, and you have no dash to reset the trade. Stack Overwhelm off safe pokes, hold Rebuttal for Path Maker rather than Ntofo chip, and treat every trade past level 3 as something to escape cleanly rather than something to win.","mid":"Levels 6-11 are survival, not domination. His R isolates you, strips his own resists for the all-in, and dashes onto a frame that dies to one full rotation — and once his first sustain item is in, his Q knockup plus W dash close your 550 range before your kite can reset it. Hug your side of the wave, detonate Golden Eclipse from absolute max range the moment he commits instead of saving it for a perfect picture, and hold E strictly for his dash-in. Concede the CS you can't take safely; this phase's only job is delivering your stacks to late game.","late":"Your infinite Overwhelm scaling finally claws the matchup back to even — he can't out-scale a passive with no cap, and your stacked detonations start genuinely hurting even a full tank. But the assassination threat never expires: a fed K'Sante in All Out form one-shots your squishy frame, so never sidelane alone and never show without E up. Fight from the backline with peel, root him when he R-isolates a teammate, and pour Golden Eclipse into whoever his engage exposes. You win the game's last fights — as long as you're alive for them.","whys":["You poke with one ability and your ranged auto, but his W block negates it and his passive sustains — genuinely even, nobody commits.","Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed Q punish, but Path Maker's charge soaks the damage and stuns straight back — a coin-flip at best.","His W block shuts off your Q barrage and his Q knockup ends your trades — he starts to out-skirmish your single CC.","As your Q ranks he simply blocks it with W and walks you down — no dash on you, one root, can't kite him.","Golden Eclipse needs range, but his R isolates you, strips his resists, and dashes onto your squishy frame for the kill.","His first sustain item plus Q knockup and W dash close your 550 range instantly — your poke can't reset the trade anymore.","Your infinite Overwhelm scaling claws back relevance vs his tankiness, but his All Out burst still threatens you — even with peel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"lillia","win":["Mel","Skill","Lillia","Lillia","Skill","Skill","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — root her and land free Overwhelm stacks before Blooming Blows speed carries her off."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lillia's danger window: W/E spam and her passive DOT out-sustain your short pokes while she dances out of E range and refuses to commit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse vs her Lullaby — but Lullaby only sleeps targets already carrying Dream Dust, so stay unmarked at 6."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your power peak: AP + mana lets you chain Q, root with E and execute her squishy frame with R before she can kite to safety."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) to pin a slippery target, then Q-stack Overwhelm and detonate with R","Use Rebuttal (W) to eat Swirlseed (E), her only projectile, and the slow it carries","Reach 2+ items where AP scaling lets your poke chunk her squishy frame faster than she can kite"],"foe":["Spam Q (Blooming Blows) and W (Watch Out! Eep!) to kite past your E range and mark you","Refuse short trades and farm with passive burn while dancing out of Solar Snare's lockon","Hit her Lullaby (R) sleep to set up an all-in or jungle gank past your single CC"]},"early":"Lillia is an off-meta skirmisher who lives on kite, so your whole early game is about pinning her down. Level 1 you out-range her — chip with Q and your ranged auto, but don't overstep into her passive burn. Your real window is level 2: with Q and Solar Snare (E) up, snare her and dump Overwhelm stacks before Blooming Blows speed carries her out. Hold W for Swirlseed, the one projectile she owns, then accept that from level 3 she'll try to slip every short trade with movement and burn.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are hers if you let them be — her Q and W spam plus passive burn out-damage your one-and-done pokes while she stays outside E range and never commits. Don't chase; that's exactly what feeds her kite. Bait her abilities, last-hit at max Q range, and wait for your E to land cleanly. At 6 her Lullaby only puts targets already carrying Dream Dust to sleep, so the counterplay is refusing to eat a spell before she ults, not dodging the cast — and it is 150s if she spends it.","late":"This is where you take over for good. With AP and a full mana pool you chain Q, root with E and execute her with R before she can bounce to safety — she has the squishy frame your Overwhelm execute is built to delete. She'll try to disengage and DOT you from range, so don't get greedy chasing across the map; land one Solar Snare, commit the full combo, and she folds. Win the side-lane 1v1 cleanly and the only thing she can do is sleep your carries in a teamfight — peel for that and the matchup stays yours.","whys":["You out-range her with Q and ranged autos at level 1, and her passive DOT can't trade with poke she can't reach.","Your level-2 Q + Solar Snare can root her mid-bounce, but she can W-kite the follow-up — it's a coinflip on whether your E lands.","Levels 3-5 her Q and W spam plus passive burn out-damage your short pokes while she dances out of Solar Snare range.","She refuses to commit and kites every trade with Blooming Blows move-speed, farming safely while your poke goes wide.","At 6 it's a CC race — your Golden Eclipse execute vs her Lullaby sleep — and whoever lands their cast first takes the all-in.","First item neither snowballs cleanly: she kites your single root and you stack her from range, a tense even window.","With 2+ items your AP and mana let you chain Q, root with E and R-execute her squishy frame before she can kite away."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"lucian","win":["Skill","Lucian","Lucian","Skill","Mel","Mel","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare lets you root him mid-dash and land a free Radiant Volley, your cleanest early punish before his E is up reliably."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Lucian's biggest threat window: with Lightslinger double-shots and Relentless Pursuit refreshing off ability hits, he out-trades your single-target poke and dashes onto you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates accumulated Overwhelm stacks from any range, turning a poke lane into a burst threat he can't dash away from once stacked."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With mana and AP online you chain Q pokes and hold Rebuttal for Piercing Light and The Culling, the shots it can actually return."}],"wants":{"you":["Root him at max range, never beside him — the immobilise empowers his next two autos","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, then detonate with Golden Eclipse for the execute","Hold Rebuttal for Piercing Light, Ardent Blaze or The Culling — the three he throws"],"foe":["Use Relentless Pursuit (E) and Culling tempo to dash past your poke and burst you up close","Catch you with Lightslinger double-shots when Solar Snare and Rebuttal are on cooldown","Trade with Piercing Light (Q) through minions while his passive procs out-DPS your single ability"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Lucian if he plays it right. His Lightslinger passive double-shots after every ability, so a Piercing Light into auto out-trades your single Radiant Volley before you have the projectile count to commit. Your one window is Level 2: with Q + Solar Snare you can root him as he steps up and land a guaranteed Volley — but root from range, since immobilising him also arms two bonus-damage autos. Otherwise respect his range and don't walk into a Q-auto-auto trade you can't win.","mid":"This is where the lane swings to you. As Radiant Volley ranks up and Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated pokes, his short-range double-shot trades stop paying off. At 6, Golden Eclipse detonates every stack from any range, so even if he dashes to safety the burst still lands — bait his Relentless Pursuit, then root him from max range once it's down, never from beside him, since immobilising him arms two bonus autos. Hold Rebuttal for Piercing Light or The Culling instead.","late":"You keep the edge into your first item — mana and AP let you chain Volleys, sit at max range, and detonate Overwhelm freely while he has to walk into your wall to deal damage. The honest risk: Lucian with a kited Culling and full crit can delete you if he ever catches you without Rebuttal or Flash, since you have zero dashes and one CC. Keep Solar Snare for his engage, never get caught mid-Volley animation, and let your team body-block his dashes in skirmishes.","whys":["You both have one ability and an auto — you can poke at 550 range but lack projectile count to commit, while his Lightslinger double-shot edges the raw trade.","Lucian's Piercing Light into a double-shot auto out-damages your single Radiant Volley, and every Lightslinger attack he lands cuts Relentless Pursuit's cooldown.","His Lightslinger passive and E mobility let him win the short trade before your full Q-E-W kit and Overwhelm stacks come online.","As Radiant Volley ranks and Overwhelm accumulates, your repeated poke starts out-damaging his double-shot bursts — the lane levels off.","Golden Eclipse detonates built-up Overwhelm from any range, so his Relentless Pursuit dash to safety no longer escapes your burst.","With mana and AP you chain Volleys at max range and hold Rebuttal for Piercing Light and The Culling, the projectiles it returns.","You sit beyond his Q-auto range stacking Overwhelm and detonating freely, while he must enter your Rebuttal wall to trade."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"malphite","win":["Mel","Skill","Malphite","Malphite","Mel","Malphite","Malphite"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + E online means you can land Solar Snare's root and free-poke Malphite with Radiant Volley while he's stuck eating it — your strongest early window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks on him from range, but this is also when his R Unstoppable engage comes online and flips the lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Malphite buys armour his Ground Slam hits harder off it, and Thunderclap-empowered autos start winning the short trades."},{"when":"Late","text":"A full-armor Malphite walks through your poke and R-flashes onto you — without Flash or peel you get one-shot engaged and deleted."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2-3 first and root him with Solar Snare, then free-cast Radiant Volley while he's stuck in the field","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos and burst him with Golden Eclipse before his R is up","Hold Rebuttal for Seismic Shard or his engage, then kite out of the speed steal"],"foe":["Land R Unstoppable engage (ideally with Flash) to close the gap your poke can't stop","Steal your speed with Seismic Shard, then walk in for Thunderclap-empowered autos","Survive your poke, itemize armor, and scale into a tankier all-in he wins"]},"early":"Malphite stacks armor, not magic resist, so your Radiant Volley poke and empowered autos hurt him far more than his Q poke hurts you — and you out-range him hard at 550. At Level 2-3 with Q + E you can land Solar Snare's root and rain a free Volley on him while he's pinned, building Overwhelm stacks he can't trade back. Seismic Shard is a projectile, so Rebuttal can return it — and keep the chip coming, because Granite Shield only recharges after a few seconds without a hit. Never sit in his Q, which steals your speed outright.","mid":"This is the knife's edge: at 6 your Golden Eclipse detonates all your stored Overwhelm on him from range, but his R also comes online — one Unstoppable engage (especially R-Flash) closes the distance your poke can't defend and his W-empowered combo chunks your squishy frame. Respect his R cooldown above everything: hold your own Flash and Rebuttal for the instant he engages, root him with Solar Snare to peel, and don't get caught creep-pushed into his all-in range. Levels 4-5 he's already itemizing armor, so your trades go even-to-his-favor if you let him walk up.","late":"Late game flips against you — a full-armor Malphite simply walks through your poke and R-Flashes onto you, and you have zero dashes, one CC, and a glass frame to survive it. Your headline lead came from the early poke window, not the teamfight, so your job late is to never be the R target: stay behind your frontline, keep Flash and Rebuttal up for his engage, and let your team body him while you detonate Overwhelm from max range. If he gets onto you uncontested, you die before your stacks matter.","whys":["Malphite stacks armor with no early MR, so your ranged Volley and empowered autos out-poke his Q while you sit safely at 550 range.","Q + E lets you root him with Solar Snare and free-cast Radiant Volley on the pinned target — a guaranteed punish he can't answer.","With W up too the lane is even — you out-poke, but he can Q-slow and step in for trades, so neither side fully owns Level 3.","Levels 4-5 stay yours on range — Unstoppable Force is offline, and his armour buys nothing against magic damage while it feeds Ground Slam.","His R Unstoppable engage comes online and ignores your kite — one R-Flash closes the gap and his W-empowered combo bursts you.","A first armor item plus his Q slow lets him walk through your poke and win the short all-in once he's on top of you.","Full-armor Malphite statchecks your squishy frame — he R-engages from any angle and you have no dash, one CC, and no peel to survive it."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"maokai","win":["Skill","Maokai","Maokai","Maokai","Maokai","Maokai","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Maokai hits 2 first and W-roots you onto a Q knockback the moment you step up to last-hit with your auto."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His real all-in window: Twisted Advance gap-closes through your kite, Bramble Smash knocks you out of position, and Sap Magic has already refilled what you chipped."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your one good window: Lost Chapter mana plus a stacked Overwhelm means a Golden Eclipse detonation can chunk him if he ever facechecks without W up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Stalemate — your passive scales but he is unkillable as a frontline tank, so the lane goes even while the game is decided elsewhere."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Solar Snare purely for Twisted Advance — at 11s against his 14s you can afford to keep it for the engage","Poke with Q only when his W is on cooldown, since otherwise he dashes onto you before the bolts land","Save W (Rebuttal) shield and move speed for his Q knockback follow-up, not for poke"],"foe":["Land W root-dash onto you, then Q knockback to lock you in melee where you have no escape","Refill through Sap Magic, whose heal your own Volley ticks keep bringing back up","Hold his W to bait your E, then dash on you the moment Solar Snare is on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1 is roughly even — you out-range him with your 550 auto and one Q, so chip him while he can only walk up. But the moment he hits 2 this flips: his W is a targeted root-dash that closes your kite gap instantly, and he chains Q to knock you off your spot. Do NOT step into auto range to stack Overwhelm if his W is up — he will dash on you and you have zero dashes to escape. Hold your E (Solar Snare) purely as an anti-engage; root him when HE commits, never spend it offensively into a tank who just heals it off.","mid":"This is his lane. Sap Magic's heal cooldown drops every time one of your spells strikes him, and Radiant Volley ticks repeatedly, so the chip that should snowball just refills him each wave. At 6 his W dash plus Q knockback is a guaranteed pick if your E is down — and a tank does not care about a single root the way a squishy would. Rebuttal still blanks his damage and hands you the move speed to walk back out of melee, so hold it for the dash itself. Farm at max range, ping for jungle, and only commit if you catch him with W on cooldown.","late":"The lane settles into a stalemate. Your passive scales infinitely so you stay relevant, but Maokai becomes an unkillable frontline tank — your Overwhelm execute threshold is a fantasy against his HP and resists. Neither of you wins the 1v1: he can't burst you down, you can't kill a tank. Play for teamfight value where your R can detonate stacks across his whole team from range, and keep Flash for Nature's Grasp, which walls off the retreat you have no dash to make.","whys":["Even start — your 550 range and Q out-poke his single melee Q, but neither of you has the tools to commit at level 1.","He hits 2 first and his W root-dash plus Q knockback punishes any step-up before you have E to answer the engage.","Maokai owns it — his W gap-close beats your kite and his sustain refills whatever your Q chipped, so trades net in his favor.","Sap Magic out-heals your Overwhelm stacking, and every Volley tick that lands on him shortens the cooldown on that heal.","His all-in spike: W dash through your poke plus Q knockback locks you in melee, and one root from your E isn't enough to stop a tank.","Your first item helps but his W still dashes onto you, and a tank shrugs off the chip your Q and autos build between his engages.","Stalemate — your passive scales but you can't kill a frontline tank, and he can't burst you, so the lane goes even into the late game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Skill","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Solar Snare plus Q poke is your one early window, but Indestructible heals the trade off and Death's Grasp answers your root the moment it ends."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Realm of Death (his R) is the lane: he banishes you 1v1, steals your AP and stats, and there is no wall or root to save you in that box."},{"when":"1st item","text":"He buys a Riftmaker/Rylai spike and his isolated Q does more in one box than your whole poke chain — your W cannot block a melee slam."},{"when":"Late","text":"If you survive to two items and full Overwhelm stacks, your ranged R detonation finally lets you chunk him before he can close — but only with Flash up for his E."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root then kite backward so his E pull and Q can't isolate you","Stay past 700 range — Death's Grasp is an area pull, so Rebuttal cannot reflect it","Stall to two items and full Overwhelm so your ranged R detonation chunks him from outside his range"],"foe":["Land E to pull you in, then Q on you isolated for the bonus damage","Pop R the instant your W and Flash are down to drag you 1v1 and steal your AP","Hug minimum range so your poke is wasted and every all-in is an E-Q-R box"]},"early":"Level 1 is a real fight — your ranged auto and Radiant Volley out-range his 675-range Obliterate, and Indestructible is the only thing keeping him healthy, so chip him and don't overstay. The trap is Level 2-3: you get Q and Solar Snare and want to root-and-poke, but Death's Grasp reaches 700 and cancels your spacing the second the root ends. Obliterate also deals bonus damage to an isolated target, so never step away from your own wave to trade — standing in your minions is a straight damage cut.","mid":"This is where it goes wrong, and it's why the lane is HARD. At 6 Realm of Death takes you into a 1v1 box from 650 range and steals your AP — there is no kiting inside that wall. It is a 140s cooldown at rank 1, so surviving one buys you two quiet minutes. Indestructible turns everything you chip him for into a heal every 12s, so bring Grievous Wounds before you commit to a poke war, and keep Flash exclusively for the moment his R drops you next to him.","late":"If you reach two items with full Overwhelm stacks you finally have an out: your R detonates on him from any range, so you can chunk or threaten an execute before he ever closes the gap. But it stays knife-edge — one landed E into his R erases you, and he scales as a juggernaut too. Play with your team, never get caught sidelaning where he can isolate you, and only commit when your Flash is up to answer the box.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s, but your ranged auto plus one ability out-pokes his melee Q while his W shield is his only sustain — a genuine coin-flip.","You get Solar Snare, but Death's Grasp answers the root from 700 and Indestructible heals off the Q poke you meant to punish with.","With Q, E and W up he can pull you in and W-heal through your poke, and you have no second CC to stop the isolation.","Obliterate deals bonus damage when it catches you alone, and one root can't kite a 700-range pull plus his slow.","Realm of Death drags you 1v1 and steals your AP — no wall or root saves you in that box, so this is his hardest spike.","His first-item Riftmaker/Rylai outscales your poke and his W blocks nothing you throw, so every all-in is his.","At two items with full Overwhelm your ranged R detonation finally lets you chunk him before he closes — even, but only with Flash for his E."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"nasus","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a free punish every time Nasus walks up to last-hit a stack with Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your accumulated Overwhelm stacks for burst from range — your cleanest kill window before he itemizes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Wither flips the lane: 700 range on a 15s cycle beats your 550 auto, and a Nasus who reaches you turns your kite into a death."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"A 200+ stack Nasus with Fury of the Sands outscales your poke — it adds attack range, armour and MR while Wither locks the whole duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2 first and root him with Solar Snare the moment he steps up to Q a minion","Stack Overwhelm with Q poke and empowered autos, then detonate with Golden Eclipse at 6 to deny his early stacks","Permaharass him off the wave and pressure his back-line CS so he never free-farms his Q stacks"],"foe":["Wither you (W) to gut your move speed and attack speed so you can't kite, then E shred and Q execute","Farm Q stacks safely under tower and weather your early poke without dying","Hit 2+ items where R lifesteal and size let him walk through your poke and one-shot with stacked Q"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — one ability and your 550-range auto can chip him but you can't commit. Your real window opens at 2: take Q then E so when Nasus shuffles up to last-hit, Solar Snare's root plus a Q barrage is a free chunk he can't answer with no dash and no range. Keep poking from max range, stack Overwhelm, and never let him farm Q stacks in peace — your only path in this lane is to make his early miserable. Watch his Wither cooldown; once it's up, do not get cornered.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your peak. Your Q ranks up, Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated trades, and at 6 Golden Eclipse detonates all of it for burst from range — this is where you punish a not-yet-itemized Nasus and try to set him behind on stacks. Root with Solar Snare, kite back through the slow field, and rain Q. But respect Wither: if he lands W on you it cripples your move and attack speed and your whole kite collapses, so trade only when his W is down and you have space to retreat.","late":"This is where the 28.57% lives. Once Nasus hits 2+ items and a big stack count, the lane is lost — Fury of the Sands adds attack range, armour and MR on a 120s cooldown, and Wither locks you for the entire fight. His R also burns a share of max health, so stacking HP does not buy you a single extra second. Your only hope is the lead you built early: end before ~25 minutes, group with your team, and never get caught alone where one Wither plus Q deletes you.","whys":["One ability and your ranged auto poke, but Nasus's Level 1 is just as weak — you can chip him but can't commit yet.","Q plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish when Nasus steps up to Q a minion — he has no dash to dodge it.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke and root an immobile Nasus — he has no projectile to punish you with and can only farm and eat it.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks accumulate from every trade — a pre-item Nasus can't reach you to answer the poke.","Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up stacks for ranged burst — your hardest kill threat before he comes online.","Wither flips it: it guts your move and attack speed so your kite fails, and a single item lets him close and Q-chunk you.","A stacked, itemized Nasus statchecks you — R lifesteal and size facetank your poke, Wither locks you, and his Q one-shots your frame."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Mel","Skill","Nautilus","Nautilus","Nautilus","Nautilus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare root is your one clean early punish — catch him stepping up to last-hit before Dredge Line's 1150 range matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse can detonate your Overwhelm stacks from range, but Depth Charge only needs one knockup to chain into Staggering Blow's root and Riptide — this is HIS spike, not yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nautilus buys boots plus a tank item and walks through your poke; Dredge Line now reliably catches you for the Staggering Blow root and Riptide follow-up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Any Nautilus engage is a near-guaranteed kill on you — Dredge Line into Staggering Blow into Depth Charge is more lockdown than you can survive without Flash."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2 first and land Solar Snare on him as he steps up for CS, then Q-poke the chunk","Hold W to eat his Q hook — destroying the projectile denies his entire engage and fires it back as your damage","Sit at max 550 range and never give him a flat path to walk a hook into you"],"foe":["Land Dredge Line to drag you in, then proc Staggering Blow's root on the next auto for a free combo","Wait out your W cooldown, then hook — your only projectile-counter has a long downtime","Use Depth Charge's knockup to lock you from any approach, since you have no dash to escape the chain"]},"early":"At Level 1 it's even — one ability each, just trade Q chips and respect that Staggering Blow roots on his first auto. Level 2 is your single best window: Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lets you land a guaranteed punish when he steps up to last-hit, so play for that. But once Titan's Wrath is up the lane tilts — Rebuttal does return Dredge Line, yet at 38s against his 14s hook it only ever covers one attempt in three. Never stand on a straight line into him, because his 1150-range hook out-ranges every spell you own.","mid":"This is where it slips away. Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks, but Nautilus just builds tank and walks through your poke — chip damage doesn't kill a tank, and he only needs ONE good Q hook to end the trade. At 6 his R single-target knockup chains with his passive root and E AOE into more lockdown than you can survive without Flash. Bait his hook with W positioning, dodge his telegraphed Q, and accept you're farming, not winning. Don't greed a Golden Eclipse detonate if it means standing still in hook range.","late":"You lose the straight engage all game. A late Nautilus is unkillable in lane and every cooldown of his is a kill threat on your squishy frame — Q hook into passive root into E into R knockup is a full chain-CC sentence and you have zero dashes to break it. Your value is entirely on the side: peel for your carries with E's root and W, detonate Overwhelm stacks from max range in fights, and never facecheck or walk a lane where he can land a blind hook. Flash up, group, and don't try to 1v1 the tank.","whys":["One ability each and your ranged auto pokes, but his autos apply a passive root the moment you're in range — genuinely even.","Q plus Solar Snare on an 11s cycle punishes any step-up for CS before his 14s Dredge Line is online.","Titan's Wrath comes online and so does the hook — Rebuttal returns Dredge Line, but 38s against 14s covers one in three.","He starts building tank and your Q poke can't kill through it, while a single Q hook into passive root flips any trade.","His R single-target knockup chains with passive root and E for lockdown you can't escape without a dash — his spike, not yours.","Nautilus buys a tank item and boots and walks through your poke; his hook now reliably lands the full combo.","Late, any engage is lethal on your squishy frame — Q hook, passive root, E, R is more chain CC than you can survive 1v1."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"neeko","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a free punish the second she steps up to last-hit or tries to E-root you first."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range and executes her squishy frame the instant she's chunked."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With mana and AP you chain Q pokes and Rebuttal answers Tangle-Barbs; Pop Blossom it can only blank, never return — your peak."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her threat window: a clone (W) feint into her R AOE stun lets the jungler collapse on your rooted, dashless frame."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit your Lvl 2 Q + Solar Snare root to punish her stepping up before her own E lands","Hold W for Tangle-Barbs — Pop Blossom is a leap, not a projectile, nothing to reflect","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, then detonate Golden Eclipse to execute her low-HP frame"],"foe":["Land her E root or R stun to lock your dashless frame for a jungle collapse","Use her W clone to bait your W/E cooldowns and disguise the angle of her engage","Poke with Q and scale her AOE to set up cross-map picks once she has items"]},"early":"Neeko is a fellow squishy mage with no escape, so the lane is about who lands their root first — and yours is faster: Solar Snare is 11s against her 12s Tangle-Barbs at rank 1. At level 1 you both just trade autos and a single ability, roughly even. From level 2 the moment she steps up to last-hit or winds up her own E, you root her and unload Q for free. Watch what Tangle-Barbs passes through: if it kills a unit on the way it comes out larger, faster and roots for longer, so never shelter behind a dying minion.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your takeover. Your Q ranks up, Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated pokes, and at 6 Golden Eclipse detonates all of it from any range — on a squishy Neeko that's an execute window. Bait her cooldowns: she'll feint with her W clone to disguise an engage, so don't burn your W or E on the fake. Her real threat is W-into-Pop Blossom. Rebuttal blanks that damage but cannot return it and will not stop the stun, so answer it with distance, not with a button.","late":"You stay even-to-favored straight up — she's as fragile as you, dies if your R catches her chunked, and your root arrives first. The danger is never the 1v1: it's Pop Blossom landing in a teamfight to set up a pick on your flashless, peel-less frame, and while she's disguised its wind-up is hidden entirely. Any immobilise breaks Inherent Glamour, so a Solar Snare on a suspicious ally unmasks her. Win or end before she finds a five-man R off a flank.","whys":["You both have one ability and a ranged auto — even footing, and neither of you has the projectile count or burst to commit yet.","Your Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish the moment she steps up, and she has no dash to escape it.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke and out-root her, and W eats her E root projectile and reflects it as your damage.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from every trade — you own the lane against a dashless mage who can't close on you.","Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up stacks from range and executes her squishy frame the instant she's chunked.","Mana and AP let you chain Q pokes freely while Rebuttal answers Tangle-Barbs and your 11s root beats her 12s — your peak.","Both stay fragile and your W still eats her R, but her teamfight R stun on your flashless frame keeps it a coinflip — even, not lost."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Skill","Olaf","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare (E) online — root him as he steps up for a CS and stack Overwhelm with empowered autos before he can axe-chase."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Olaf's Ragnarok (R) makes him immune to your root for as long as he keeps attacking, and Reckless Swing is true damage — armour and MR buy nothing inside it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With mana and AP you chain Q pokes and detonate Golden Eclipse (R) from range, but only when his Ragnarok is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Group fights favor you — his single-target R can't reach you if you sit behind your team, while your R executes whatever he dove."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) on him as he walks up to last-hit, then Q-poke and stack Overwhelm before he closes","Track his Ragnarok (R) cooldown and only commit your all-in when it's down","Use Rebuttal (W) to reflect his Undertow axe and to kite the slow, not as a stat-check against his ult"],"foe":["Walk you down under Ragnarok (R) so your root is consumed for nothing and his true damage ignores your resistances","Land Undertow (Q) axe to slow you and close the gap your poke relies on","Buy early Merc Treads / hexdrinker and sustain through your Q pokes with his lifesteal"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are your window. At 2 you'll have Q and Solar Snare (E) — root him the instant he steps into the wave for a CS and unload empowered autos to build Overwhelm. His only answer pre-6 is the Undertow axe slow, so sidestep it and keep your 550 range. Don't waste W as a shield against his autos; save the movement speed to dodge the axe. He can't all-in you safely until 6, so farm-pressure him and chip his health bar.","mid":"At 6 the lane flips. Ragnarok (R) makes Olaf immune to your Solar Snare root AND deals true damage that ignores your Rebuttal shield — inside that window your entire disengage kit is blank and he statchecks you. The whole mid-game is a cooldown war: when his R is up, respect it and farm at max range; when it's down, that's your kill window — Q-poke, E-root, and detonate Golden Eclipse to chunk or execute. Never trade your health for his when he can flip the script with one button.","late":"Late game is genuinely even and comes down to positioning. Olaf is single-target — if you sit behind your frontline, his R can't reach you and your Q rains on the whole fight while your passive scales infinitely. But one mistake, one facecheck, and he Ragnarok-dives you through every shield and CC you own and you die instantly with no flash. Keep peel up, hold Solar Snare for whoever he's NOT immune to, and let your team body-block his run at you.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s — one ability and an auto each; deny his Q last-hits and set up your level 2 spike.","Q + Solar Snare lands a guaranteed root on him as he steps up for CS — your strongest early punish before his R exists.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke and out-disengage a pre-6 Olaf whose only tool is the axe slow.","Even window — his axe slow lets him trade back, but you still root-and-kite if you respect the gap.","Ragnarok makes him immune to my root while he keeps swinging, and Reckless Swing is true damage armour cannot reduce.","Even — your mana and AP let you chain pokes and detonate R, but only on his Ragnarok cooldown, so it nets out.","Even and positional — your ranged R out-zones him in groups, but a single Ragnarok dive deletes your flash-less frame."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"ornn","win":["Mel","Skill","Ornn","Ornn","Mel","Ornn","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your only window: Q poke plus Solar Snare root before Bellows Breath and the Volcanic Rupture pillar come online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R double-knockup with the call-back stampede is a point-and-click setup your single root can't answer once he hits you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ornn self-itemizes his Forge so he hits resist breakpoints early — your Q and empowered-auto poke stop chunking his effective HP."},{"when":"Late","text":"Bellows Breath's last gout applies Brittle and Call of the Forge God re-applies it, and you cannot peel his front line off your carries."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke from past 800 — Volcanic Rupture is his longest laning spell and both your spells out-range it","Hold Solar Snare's root for the exact moment he commits a W charge or E pillar engage","Keep W up to body-block his pillar/Brittle engage line and disengage before he stacks Brittle on you"],"foe":["Close your 550 range with Searing Charge, then Brittle you with Bellows Breath","Drop a Volcanic Rupture pillar, then Searing Charge into it so the terrain hit knocks you up","Hit Level 6 and chain R's double knockup into Brittle-amped follow-up damage"]},"early":"Treat Ornn like the one tank you don't get to bully. Your Q area poke and empowered autos do chip him, but he out-sustains it with raw tank stats and never has to walk into you — he just farms and waits for a Searing Charge angle. Your one good window is Level 2-3: land Q, then hold Solar Snare for the instant he steps up, because that root is the only CC you have and you can't afford to whiff it. Never stand near a fresh Volcanic Rupture pillar — Searing Charge knocks up when Ornn hits terrain, and the pillar is the terrain he wants.","mid":"This is where the lane slips away. Ornn self-itemizes his Forge, so he hits armor/MR breakpoints faster than a normal tank and your Q poke stops mattering against his effective HP. At 6 his R is the problem: Call of the Forge God is a double knockup that ignores your max-range plan entirely — one recast and you're airborne and Brittle before you can W or root. You only have one piece of CC and zero dashes, so once he lands a charge or an R on you, you're dead. Stop trading the moment Solar Snare is on cooldown.","late":"You lose this outright late. Bellows Breath makes you Brittle and Call of the Forge God re-applies it on a 140s cooldown, and your infinitely-scaling passive doesn't matter if you're knocked up and deleted. Call of the Forge God's double knockup is a teamfight-starting button you have no answer to without Flash up, and you can't peel his front line off your carries. Your job shrinks to landing R detonations and Radiant Volley from the very back; do not get caught alone, because one Searing Charge into a wall is a death sentence.","whys":["You have one ability and your ranged auto; he has tank base stats and clears safely, so neither of you commits and the trade math favors his sustain.","Q plus Solar Snare gives you a punish window, but Ornn's W charge and E pillar are also coming online, so it's a coin-flip on who lands CC first.","Searing Charge closes 450 and knocks you up the moment Ornn collides with terrain or his own pillar — one root can't cover it.","Ornn self-forges resist items, hitting armor/MR breakpoints that make your Q area poke and empowered autos stop chunking his effective HP.","Golden Eclipse needs built-up stacks, but his R double-knockup lands first and Brittle-amped follow-up bursts you before you detonate.","His self-itemized Forge spike outpaces your first-item poke window — he's tankier than you can chip while staying immobile and safe.","Brittle (W) shreds your resists and amplifies burst on your squishy frame, and you can neither peel his front line nor survive his R catch."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"pantheon","win":["Mel","Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon","Mel","Pantheon","Pantheon"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q Radiant Volley plus a Solar Snare root punishes every step Pantheon takes to last-hit, since his W stun has to close 600 range you keep poking through."},{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Pantheon's threat window: Mortal Will empowers his next spell every few casts, and a point-click Shield Vault stun into that spear chunks you if you contest the wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range, but his R Grand Starfall global means he can answer a low Pantheon elsewhere, keeping the level-6 window even."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Lost Chapter mana and your first AP item, you chain Q pokes and detonate R freely as Pantheon's flat damage falls off hard into your range advantage."}],"wants":{"you":["Stay at 550 range and stack Overwhelm with Q Radiant Volley and empowered autos so you never enter his W-stun range","Land Solar Snare (E) the instant he steps up for CS, then poke the rooted Pantheon free for a full stack-build","Save Rebuttal (W) to eat his empowered Q spear, returning it as your own magic damage and denying his poke"],"foe":["Walk you down with a point-click Shield Vault stun into a Mortal Will empowered Comet Spear","Win the level 1-2 all-in before you have Solar Snare and W online to root and disengage","Spike hard levels 1-6 and roam off Grand Starfall (R) before his flat damage falls off into your items"]},"early":"Pantheon is a real level-1 threat and I'm not, so I don't contest the wave toe-to-toe early — Mortal Will empowers his next spell every few casts, and a point-click W stun into that spear can chunk my squishy frame. I farm at max distance with Q Radiant Volley instead. The lane turns at level 2: Q poke plus my Solar Snare root means any step he takes to last-hit eats a guaranteed punish he can't stun his way out of, because Shield Vault has to close 600 range I'm already poking through. By 3 I have W Rebuttal up to eat his Q spear and fire it back, so I own the trade pattern.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are mine on poke — my Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks pile on from every trade he's forced to take walking up, while his flat early damage stops scaling. I keep my distance, root with Solar Snare the moment he commits, and never let him land the W-stun-into-Q burst that's his only real answer. Level 6 is the even window: Golden Eclipse detonates all my built-up Overwhelm from any range and threatens an execute, but his Grand Starfall is global, so a low Pantheon can recall or my kill pressure gets answered with a roam — I respect that and don't over-extend hunting the solo kill.","late":"First item is my takeover: with Lost Chapter mana and my first AP component I chain Q pokes and detonate R basically on cooldown, and Pantheon's flat-scaling kit falls off a cliff into my range and Overwhelm execute. This is the opposite of my scaler matchups — there's no Pantheon late-game spike to fear, so I don't have to rush the lane. I keep the poke war going, deny his roams by shoving and pushing him under tower, and my infinitely-scaling passive only widens the gap. Just keep W Rebuttal up for his all-in and never get caught flat by a flanking Grand Starfall.","whys":["Even at 1 — Mortal Will empowers his spear and his W stun threatens your squishy body, but you out-range him, so neither of you commits cleanly with one ability.","Your second point gives you Q poke plus Solar Snare's root, so any step he takes to last-hit eats a guaranteed punish his W stun can't answer from outside your range.","With Q, E and Rebuttal you poke, root and return his spear — but Aegis Assault blocks frontal damage on 22s, so never volley the brace.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from every forced trade while his flat early damage stops scaling — you own the gap-close-reliant bully here.","Even at 6 — Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks for an execute threat from range, but his global Grand Starfall lets him answer your kill pressure with a roam elsewhere.","Lost Chapter mana and your first AP item let you chain Q pokes and detonate R freely as Pantheon's flat damage collapses into your range advantage.","There's no Pantheon scaling spike to fear — your range, Overwhelm execute and infinitely-scaling passive only widen the gap the longer the game goes."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"poppy","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Skill","Skill","Skill","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare lets you root Poppy as she steps to last-hit and stack Overwhelm before her passive shield can soak it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up Overwhelm from range, your one clean burst window before she stacks armor and HP."},{"when":"Mid lane","text":"Stand in open river/lane, never hug your wall — Poppy's E only stuns if she pins you to terrain, so deny the wall and her all-in is dead."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Poppy itemizes tank and her passive shields eat your poke; her E-Q-R combo one-shots your squishy frame if she ever reaches you."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root the instant Poppy steps up for CS, then chain Q poke into Overwhelm stacks","Fight in open ground so Poppy's E has no wall to pin you against for the stun","Cancel Keeper’s Verdict with Solar Snare — a channel, so your 11s root eats her 140s ult"],"foe":["Pin you to a wall with E for the stun, then Q-knockup and unload her whole combo","Soak your Q poke with her passive shield and tank stats, then walk you down at full HP","Itemize armor/HP so your magic poke falls off and her R can peel or zone you in fights"]},"early":"Poppy is immobile apart from E, so your Level 2 Q-plus-Solar-Snare punish lands clean — root her as she steps up to last-hit and stack Overwhelm before her passive shield refreshes. The one rule: never lane against your own wall. Her E only stuns if she charges you into terrain, so stand in the open and her engage just shoves you a few feet with no CC. Poke the tip of Q, keep her out of E range, and save W for her Iron Ambassador buckler — reflect it and she gets no shield.","mid":"Levels 4-6 you own the poke war as long as you stay disciplined about positioning — but Poppy is a tank who soaks it with her passive shield and starting armor, so you won't kill her outright. At 6, Golden Eclipse cashes in your stacks for a real burst, your best window before she itemizes. If she lands E into a wall, you eat her Q-knockup and full combo, so play around open ground and she has no all-in. Bait her E by hugging open lane, then punish the cooldown with Solar Snare.","late":"This is where Poppy reclaims the lane. Once she's stacked armor and HP her passive shields swallow your Q poke and your Overwhelm damage gets blunted by her tankiness. If she ever closes the gap — E into terrain, Q knockup, R to isolate you — your squishy frame folds with no dash to escape. Her R is a 140s channel your root cancels outright, so hold Solar Snare for it, never path along walls, and lean on your team to focus her while you poke from max range.","whys":["Both of you are weak at Level 1 with one ability — you poke at 550 range, but Poppy's passive shield soaks it, so neither commits.","Q plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish on Poppy as she steps up to last-hit, before her shield refreshes.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke an immobile Poppy who has only E to close the gap — keep her at range.","You stack Overwhelm from repeated trades, but Poppy's passive shield and tank base stats soak enough that it stays even.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks for burst, but Poppy's HP and shield mean it chunks rather than kills — a window, not a finisher.","Your poke spike meets her first tank item — her shields start eating your damage, so it flattens back to even.","Poppy out-scales the trade: stacked armor and HP soak your magic poke, and her E-Q-R combo one-shots you if she reaches you."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"quinn","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel","Skill","Quinn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare is your one guaranteed punish, but Quinn's Harrier move speed and E vault let her dodge the orb — bait her Harrier proc first, then root."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — your one clean window to delete a squishy Quinn before she kites out with E."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter / Liandry's lets you chain Q pokes and reflect her Harrier autos with Rebuttal — your strongest sustained-trade window."},{"when":"Late","text":"Quinn's roams and 2-item kite take over — Blinding Assault plus Harrier outspaces my poke and she splitpushes me off the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root after she burns Harrier move speed, then Q-poke and stack Overwhelm before she repositions","Hold Rebuttal to eat her Harrier-empowered autos and fire them back as your own magic damage","Hit 6 with stacks loaded so Golden Eclipse executes her squishy frame from range"],"foe":["Kite at the edge of your Q with Harrier move speed and chip you between cooldowns","Blind my empowered auto with Blinding Assault, then vault out of Solar Snare","Roam on every recall window since she clears wave and outruns your one immobile CC"]},"early":"Quinn is the rare ranged enemy who can actually fight back at your range, so this isn't a free lane. Your Q poke and Solar Snare root are your only commit, but her passive Harrier move speed and E vault let her sidestep the orb if you throw it raw — bait her Harrier proc or her E first, then root the predictable step-up. Don't sit in lane eating her empowered autos for free; her poke trades evenly with yours, and she has a blind to shut off your stack-building basics.","mid":"This is your window if you've stacked Overwhelm — at 6, Golden Eclipse detonates from any range and her squishy frame can't survive a loaded execute, so the moment she steps up for a trade is your kill threat. Hold Rebuttal for her empowered autos: the wall eats the projectile and fires it back as your damage. But respect her E — the vault knockback plus blind is her escape AND her disengage, so don't blow Solar Snare until that's down or she just vaults out of the root window.","late":"You lose the long game here. Quinn's roams, blind, and Harrier kite outscale your poke once she's two items deep — she sits past your Q range, chips you, and never gives you the clean Golden Eclipse window. Worse, she splitpushes and roams off vision faster than your single immobile CC can answer. Win or stabilize the lane before her items come online, ward your flanks against her roams, and let your team handle her in teamfights where your R can still pick her off.","whys":["You out-range her slightly but with one ability and no projectile count you can't commit — trade autos and deny her Harrier last-hits.","Q + Solar Snare is your guaranteed punish, but her Harrier move speed and E vault dodge a raw orb — make her burn it first.","Q, E and W are all online, yet Blinding Assault wastes my loaded auto and Vault kites my root — a true coin-flip of cooldowns.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks, but she answers every poke with Harrier kite and E disengage — neither of you owns it.","Golden Eclipse detonates stacked Overwhelm from any range and executes her squishy frame — your one clear lead before she kites out.","Liandry's plus mana lets me chain pokes and reflect her autos with Rebuttal, but Blinding Assault and Harrier keep the trade even.","Two-item Quinn kites past my Q range, blinds my autos with her Q, and roams off the map — she reclaims the lane and the game."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"renekton","win":["Mel","Skill","Renekton","Renekton","Mel","Renekton","Renekton"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Radiant Volley plus an 11s Solar Snare punishes free the moment Slice and Dice commits him to a cannon or a last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Renekton's biggest window: at 50+ Fury, Ruthless Predator stuns 1.5s instead of 0.75s and Cull the Meek chunks you — stay out of melee range early."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range — root him with E and burst him out as he commits his dash."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter / Liandry's online: your Q poke and empowered autos out-cycle his fury, and W eats nothing of his but your sustained chip wins every exchange."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Q at max range and stack Overwhelm with empowered autos so he never closes for free","Snare the instant Slice and Dice lands — his dash is 16s at rank 1, your root 11s","Survive his level 1-3 fury windows, then take over from 4 onward as he falls off"],"foe":["Land Ruthless Predator above 50 Fury for a 1.5s stun while your E is down","Use his E dash to gap-close past your poke and trade in melee range","Snowball the lane levels 1-6 before his kit falls off into your items"]},"early":"Level 1 is a mutual stand-off — you each have one ability online, so last-hit at max Q range and refuse to walk anywhere near his stun for a trade you don't need. From 2 the lane is yours: the moment he dashes for a cannon or steps up to last-hit, Solar Snare roots him and a full Q barrage plus empowered autos punish for free. The real danger is his level 1-3 fury window — an empowered W stun into a fury combo chunks you hard if you're caught at melee range with E down — so poke on your terms, hold Rebuttal for his dash-in, and stack Overwhelm while his kill windows tick away.","mid":"This is your window. From 4-5 your Q rank-ups and accumulating Overwhelm stacks let you chip him every time he tries to commit, and Rebuttal's barrier plus the move speed lets you disengage his dash. At 6 your Golden Eclipse detonates all that stored Overwhelm from any range — bait his E dash in, root him with Solar Snare, and burst him out as he's stuck in your slow field. He has no sustained threat once you survive the initial all-in, so make him whiff his fury and punish the long cooldowns.","late":"By two items the lane is yours to close — Renekton is one of the hardest fall-off champions in the game, so if you've out-farmed him he simply can't kill you anymore. The caveat is he doesn't out-scale you; he just becomes a flanking diver looking for one bad position. Keep your E up for when he flashes in, ward your flanks, and don't get caught alone in the open where a fury W-stun bypasses your kite. Detonate him in teamfights from the backline and the game's already won.","whys":["At level 1 he has only one ability and so do you — neither commits, so last-hit at Q range and refuse to walk into his stun.","Q plus Solar Snare's root gives you a guaranteed punish the instant he dashes or steps up — your strongest early window before his fury comes fully online.","With Q, E and W up you poke, snare the spot Slice and Dice lands on, and Rebuttal blanks the Cull the Meek chunk.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm piles on, but Cull the Meek heals him back every 7s — Morellonomicon is what ends that argument.","Golden Eclipse turns built-up stacks into a ranged execute — root him in your slow field and detonate as he commits his dash.","Lost Chapter and your first AP item let you chain pokes freely while his fury-empowered combos start losing the damage race.","He out-scales nobody, but a fed-flank fury W-stun still bypasses your kite — play safe, hold E for his dive and let your range win the fight."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"riven","win":["Mel","Skill","Riven","Riven","Mel","Riven","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's 1.5s root lands a free punish the instant Riven steps up to last-hit before she has all three Q dashes."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Riven's spike, not yours: third Broken Wings into Ki Burst into R jumps your poke range — but R's Wind Slash is a projectile Rebuttal reflects."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter / Liandry's online — chain-poke at 550 range, stack Overwhelm, and threaten the R execute every time she walks up."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Riven's full lethality build out-statchecks you in melee; one clean Broken Wings into Ki Burst kills you through Rebuttal if you mistime it."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Rebuttal for Broken Wings' third knockup, or Wind Slash — her R is the one projectile you can reflect","Land Solar Snare's root the moment she dashes in so she's stuck in the slow field while you kite and stack Overwhelm","Stack Overwhelm with Q + empowered autos so Golden Eclipse executes her before her lethality build comes online"],"foe":["Bait out your Rebuttal, then commit Broken Wings' third knockup into Ki Burst before it returns","Use her Q dashes and E shield-dash to sidestep your Solar Snare and Q bolts and close the 550 gap","Snowball an early lethality lead so she one-combos you through your shield from 2+ items on"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you have one ability and your ranged auto, she has one Q dash, neither of you can commit. The lane flips your way at 2: the second she walks up to last-hit, drop Q on the wave and throw Solar Snare for the ~1.5s root, then auto her in the slow field — she has no third Q dash yet to escape it. At 3 you add W; do NOT waste it eating her autos, save the barrier for her actual engage. Farm at max range, chunk her every time she creeps forward, and keep her off your stacks.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are yours: Q ranks up, Overwhelm piles on from repeated trades, and a Riven with no item lead can't punch through your kite. The danger is 6 — that's HER spike, not yours. Her all-in is third-Q knockup into W stun into R, and it can leap your whole 550 range and burst you before you detonate. The whole matchup is your W: hold it to negate the third-Q knockup or her dash chain, then Solar Snare the rooted-in-place Riven, kite the slow field, and Golden Eclipse the leftover HP. Bait the combo, eat it with W, punish the cooldown.","late":"This is where she reclaims the lane. A fully-itemized lethality Riven out-statchecks your squishy frame — one clean third-Q+W stun combo kills you through your shield if you misjudge W, and you have zero dashes to reposition once she's on top of you. Your infinitely-scaling passive keeps you relevant in teamfights, but the straight side-lane 1v1 is hers now. Don't get caught alone, hold Flash for her engage, and let your frontline soak the combo while you Q and execute from the backline.","whys":["You both have one ability online — your ranged auto pokes but you lack the projectile count to commit, and she only has one Q dash, so it's a wash.","Q plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish the moment she steps up, and without her third Q dash she can't escape the slow field.","With Q, E and W up you poke and root — once Valor is spent she has 10s with no shield-dash out of your snare.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from every trade; a pre-item Riven simply can't out-trade you at 550 range.","Golden Eclipse adds your execute, but 6 is her spike too — Blade of the Exile lengthens her reach and Wind Slash finishes the leap, so it's a knife-edge.","Lost Chapter / Liandry's lets you chain-poke and threaten the R execute freely while she's still building lethality and can't yet one-combo you.","Full-build lethality Riven out-statchecks your squishy frame — one clean third-Q+W stun all-in kills you through the shield, and you have no dash to escape it."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Skill","Skill","Rumble","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Solar Snare root plus Q poke is your cleanest punish window — catch Rumble before he has Flamespitter ranks to out-trade you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range, but his Equalizer drops a zone you cannot stand in — the all-in is mutual, not one-sided."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter / Liandry's online: chain Q pokes and detonate freely while his mana still gates how often Flamespitter can overheat."},{"when":"Danger Zone","text":"Rumble's biggest threat: a Danger Zone Flamespitter walks you down through your kite if Electro Harpoon's slow lands first — watch the heat bar."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root then Q-stack Overwhelm before stepping back out of Flamespitter range","Reflect Electro Harpoon with Rebuttal to deny both the slow and the magic resist shred","Detonate Golden Eclipse to chunk him the instant he commits to an overheat trade"],"foe":["Land Electro Harpoon to slow you and shred your MR, then walk you down with Flamespitter","Sit above 50% heat so every Danger Zone Flamespitter burns harder through your short trades","Drop The Equalizer across your kite path so you can't poke from max range safely"]},"early":"Most Mel matchups into melee are free — this one isn't, because Rumble isn't gap-close-reliant, he's a sustained-DPS bruiser who answers poke with his own W shield and move speed. Level 2 is still your window: land Solar Snare's root and tag him with Q while his Flamespitter is only rank one and can't out-trade you. Don't sit in his face trading autos — his W shield negates your chip and his E harpoon slow pins you for the burn. Poke at max range and back off before he closes.","mid":"This is a genuine coinflip, not a free lane. Your Q ranks and Overwhelm stacks build pressure, but a Danger Zone Flamespitter out-DPSes your short trades, and Electro Harpoon's slow plus MR shred strips the kite you live on. Reflect that harpoon with Rebuttal — no slow, no trade. At 6 your Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks from range, but don't walk into The Equalizer to do it; bait him past 100% heat, where Overheating locks his casts, then commit while he can only auto.","late":"Even-to-losing here. Rumble's Equalizer becomes a teamfight zoning tool that carves your squishy frame out of poke range, and his Liandry's-and-tank-item DPS shreds you if his E harpoon catches you flat-footed. Your infinitely-scaling passive keeps you relevant, but he statchecks your short trades once both of you are itemized. Hold flash for his harpoon, never face an overheated Flamespitter without W up, and let your team body him while you execute from the back.","whys":["Both of you are mediocre level 1 — he has only rank-one Flamespitter and you have one ability, so it's a wash of trading autos at range.","Solar Snare's root plus Q is a guaranteed punish before his Flamespitter ranks let him out-sustain your poke.","Scrap Shield is a flat 6s, so it answers nearly every poke — the level-3 spike that crushes immobile melee flattens to even here.","Your Q ranks build Overwhelm, but a Danger Zone Flamespitter and Electro Harpoon's slow trade back — it stays a coinflip on setup.","Golden Eclipse detonates from range, but his Equalizer zones your kite path, so the 6 all-in is mutual rather than yours.","Lost Chapter mana lets you chain pokes and detonate stacks faster than his mana lets Flamespitter overheat — your cleanest itemized window.","He out-scales the short trade: Equalizer zoning plus Liandry's DPS through your squishy frame reclaims the lane once both of you itemize."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"ryze","win":["Mel","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ryze","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — root him as he steps to last-hit and chunk him with a free Q barrage before he can Q-E-flux back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — if you've poked him with Q and empowered autos, R turns that stored damage into a burst or execute."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your power peak vs a 615-range early Ryze — mana and AP let you chain Q pokes, reflect Spell Flux so Rune Prison only slows, and detonate freely."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His threat window — Tear stacks and 2-3 items turn Spell Flux into Rune Prison into Overload, a machine-gun chain; respect the all-in once Archangel's is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Reflect Spell Flux with Rebuttal — with no Flux on you, Rune Prison lands as a slow and Overload stops bouncing","Land Solar Snare's root on him as he steps up, then stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos for an R detonation","Win on the gold lead from 1-3 items and end before his Tear stacks and ult turn him into a raid boss"],"foe":["Stack Tear/Archangel's and reach 2+ items where his Q-E-flux root chain out-spams your poke","Land Spell Flux first so his Rune Prison roots instead of slows, then chain Overload","Survive your early poke, farm safely with spammy Q resets, and scale into the raid-boss late game"]},"early":"Ryze is one of your cleanest early lanes — Rune Prison and Spell Flux both reach only 615 and he has no dash, and you're a 550-range artillery bully. At level 2 your Q barrage plus Solar Snare's root is a guaranteed punish when he steps up to last-hit; root him and rain Q on him before his Flux chain is even reliable. Hold W (Rebuttal) for Spell Flux above all — the wall eats that projectile and fires it back, and an unfluxed Rune Prison is only a slow. Don't walk into his wave for a greedy auto inside 615.","mid":"This is your takeover. With Q ranked, E root, and W shutting off his combo, you own the gap-close-less Ryze — he has no dash, only his Q-E root to stick you, so as long as you respect that one combo you poke him for free and stack Overwhelm every trade. At 6, Golden Eclipse detonates all that stored Overwhelm from any range — if you've been chip-stacking with Q and empowered autos, R is a burst or an execute. First item is your absolute peak: mana to chain Q, AP to make every detonation hurt. Force him low and deny his farm so his scaling never arrives.","late":"Be honest — Ryze is a hard scaler and the 2+ item window is his. Once his Tear is stacked and Archangel's plus a second item are online, his Q-E-flux becomes a spammy machine-gun root chain that out-DPSes your poke and locks you down; you have one CC and no dashes, so a clean Q-E from him can kill you. Your infinitely-scaling passive keeps you relevant, but you don't out-statcheck a fed Ryze. Win the lane in the first three items, push your lead onto the map, and let your team help close before his realm-warp roams and raid-boss mid-game take over.","whys":["At level 1 with one ability and your ranged auto you can poke, but so can a pre-stack Ryze with his Q — neither of you can commit yet.","Q barrage plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish as he steps up to last-hit, before his Q-E-flux combo is reliable.","With Q, E and W online you poke, root, and reflect Spell Flux — with no Flux on you, Rune Prison only slows instead of rooting.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated trades while his dash-less, single-combo kit can't escape or out-poke you.","Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up Overwhelm from any range — stacked poke becomes a burst or execute he can't answer at 6.","First item gives you mana to chain Q and AP to detonate freely against a melee-tier early Ryze — this is your most dominant window.","He out-scales hard: stacked Tear plus Archangel's chains Spell Flux into Rune Prison into Overload fast enough to kill your squishy frame."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"sejuani","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Sejuani","Sejuani"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish when Sejuani steps up to last-hit minions."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Ranked-up Q and accumulating Overwhelm stacks let you chip her armor-stacked HP bar before her sustain frost matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your built stacks from range, but she has Glacial Prison ult to answer with a long-range hard CC."},{"when":"Late","text":"Permafrost stuns you at max Frost stacks and her next hit shatters you for massive magic damage — she owns 2+ items."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root the moment she walks up for CS, then free-fire Q and empowered autos","Stay outside 650 — Arctic Assault range — so Winter's Wrath never stacks Frost","Use W to body-block her R cast and disengage rather than to fight her head-on"],"foe":["Stack Frost with Winter's Wrath, stun with Permafrost, then shatter you with the next hit","Stack armor/HP and let Frostbite W chunk a fixed percent of your low health bar","Throw Glacial Prison from 1300 range while Rebuttal is down — lit, the bola comes back"]},"early":"Sejuani does have a dash — Arctic Assault (Q), 650 range on 18s at rank 1 — so your level 2 Solar Snare window is real only while it is down. She also does not care about chip: Fury of the North's Frost Armor grants armour, magic resist and immunity to slows, so Solar Snare's outer slow ring is dead text and only the centre root holds her. Winter's Wrath (W) stacks Frost on you every swing; at max stacks Permafrost (E) stuns, and her next hit shatters you for massive magic damage.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your cleanest stretch — ranked Q plus stacking Overwhelm erodes even her armour-heavy bar from max range, and Arctic Assault (18s at rank 1, 650 range) is her only way in. Hold Rebuttal (W): 38s at rank 1 falling to 26, it prevents all damage and reflects projectiles. At 6 that decides the lane — Glacial Prison is a 1300-range bola and it is a projectile, so a lit Rebuttal sends it straight back and stuns her in her own ice storm. Arctic Assault is a charge, not a projectile: Rebuttal only blanks its damage.","late":"She wins the long game. Frost Armor's armour and magic resist blunt your volleys, and the rest of her kit is hard CC: Winter's Wrath stacks Frost, Permafrost stuns at max stacks, and her follow-up hit shatters you for massive magic damage. Glacial Prison opens fights from 1300 range on a 120/105/90s cooldown. You have no dash and one root to peel with. Keep your distance, save Rebuttal for the bola, and let your frontline eat the engage while you detonate from the back.","whys":["Both of you are weak with one ability — you can poke at 550 range but lack the projectile count to commit, and she just farms it up.","Q plus Solar Snare's ~1.5s root guarantees a punish when this dashless tank steps up to last-hit.","She comes online too — armor stacking and her always-charging Permafrost mean your chip does not snowball, so it levels out.","Ranked Q and accumulating Overwhelm let you out-poke a gap-close-less tank who cannot answer max-range pressure.","Golden Eclipse turns stacks into burst, but Glacial Prison is an equal-range hard CC that catches you — it nets out even.","Your first-item poke spike is strong, but a tank's resists blunt it and she contributes CC regardless, keeping it skill.","Frost Armor's resists plus a Permafrost stun into the shatter out-statcheck your fragile frame once she itemizes — she reclaims it."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"sett","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel","Skill","Mel","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your 550-range auto plus first Q bolt out-poke Sett before he has W stored or E grab — chip him while he can only walk up to last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Grit is stored and Facebreaker is up he can pull you in and land a true-damage centre punch — his Haymaker trade overtakes your poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Sett's R suppress-slam ignores your lack of dashes: if his jungler holds you, he ults you to his team and you have no W projectile to eat a point-blank slam."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With Zhonya's and AP online you stack Overwhelm from max range and detonate Golden Eclipse before he closes — the lane re-opens if you got vision and never get grabbed."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-1 poke war with ranged autos and a Q bolt before Sett stores any W damage","Solar Snare him the instant he steps up to E-grab, rooting him out of his own combo","Stay on the same side of him as your wave — with nothing behind him Facebreaker slows instead of stunning"],"foe":["Bait your snare, then Facebreaker you across the wave and unload a stored Haymaker","Soak your poke on purpose — the damage he takes is the Grit that loads Haymaker","Land R suppress to drag you out of position, ideally with jungle, where you have no dash to answer"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: at 550 range with your ranged auto and the first Radiant Volley bolt you chip Sett while he can only walk up to CS, and Haymaker has nothing stored yet. But respect how fast this flips — the moment Grit is charged and Facebreaker is up, every step inside 490 risks a pull into a true-damage centre punch. Save Solar Snare to root him out of Facebreaker range, not to poke. And know the price of chip: every point of damage he absorbs is stored as the Grit that fuels that punch, so poke and step back rather than stand and trade.","mid":"This is Sett's window and you have to play honest. Levels 4-6 his stored-W smash and E-grab out-trade your short pokes, and your only CC is on the E you need held for self-peel — so you can't both poke and stay safe. At 6 his R suppress completely ignores your zero-dash kit: if his jungler shows, he ults you to the tower and there's nothing to W. Farm at max Q range, only step up when his W bar is empty and E is on cooldown, and never face him without flash up. Bait the grab, side-step, THEN punish with Q and a snare.","late":"The lane re-opens once you're itemized. With Zhonya's to survive his all-in and AP feeding Overwhelm, you stack from 550 range and detonate Golden Eclipse before Sett ever reaches you, while his single-target R becomes far less scary if you have vision and peel. Keep him at arm's length, never walk into a fog grab, and let your stored magic damage execute him as he commits. If he ever lands R on you flush, though, you still die — so the whole late game is positioning and ward discipline, not statchecking him.","whys":["At level 1 your 550-range auto and first Q bolt out-poke Sett, who has no stored W and can only walk up to last-hit.","Once his W is storing damage and E is up, his grab-into-smash trade matches your poke — it is a genuine coin-flip on who steps first.","With W stored and E grab online, Sett can grab-stun you and dump a fully-charged true-damage smash that your single root cannot fully answer.","Facebreaker is 16s to your snare's 11s, so your root returns first — but every point of chip you land is Grit loading Haymaker.","Golden Eclipse on your side is range damage, but his R suppress-slam drags your dashless frame to his team with no W to eat it.","Blackfire Torch outpaces his first bruiser item: he still has to walk 950 to reach a 490-range Facebreaker.","With Zhonya's and AP you stack Overwhelm and detonate from max range — even, provided you keep vision and never get grabbed flush."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"shen","win":["Mel","Skill","Shen","Shen","Mel","Shen","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare lets you root a stepping-up Shen and punish him before his E taunt range and W auto-block come fully online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm from range — and your Solar Snare cancels Stand United outright, because that global is a channel."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Shen's threat window: Shadow Dash taunts you in and Spirit's Refuge eats your empowered auto — Radiant Volley is an ability, so keep casting it through the zone."},{"when":"Late","text":"Shen's global R lets him win the map while out-sustaining your poke 1v1 — you scale evenly at best and he's the tankier body."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root to lock Shen before he can E taunt-dash onto you, then chunk with Q and empowered autos","Snare Shen the instant Stand United starts channelling — the channel breaks and his 200s global is spent","Use Rebuttal's shield and move speed to disengage his E taunt all-in, not just to eat his Q poke"],"foe":["E taunt-dash onto you to lock you in place for his Q-empowered melee trade and force you out of poke range","Pop Spirit's Refuge as your empowered auto lands, blanking the biggest hit of the trade","Use global R to roam-impact other lanes and trade evenly while out-sustaining your poke into the scaling game"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you have 550 range and your Q bolts, but Shen just farms with his Q-empowered swings and doesn't need to step into your poke range. Your real window is Level 2-3: Q plus Solar Snare's root means a Shen who walks up to last-hit eats a guaranteed punish before his E taunt gives him a gap-close answer. The thing to respect is that root spacing — if you whiff Solar Snare you have no second CC and nothing to stop his E taunt-dash from pulling you into a melee trade where his W Spirit's Refuge eats your empowered autos.","mid":"Levels 3-5 tilt to Shen and you have to play honest. Shadow Dash covers 600 units and taunts, and the instant he lands it Spirit's Refuge blocks basic attacks inside its zone — so hold the empowered auto and keep dropping Radiant Volley, which is an ability and lands through it anyway. Hold Rebuttal to break his all-in, not to eat poke. Level 6 cuts both ways: Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range, and Solar Snare cancels Stand United while he is still channelling it.","late":"This is where the 37.5% lives. Shen scales into an even-to-tankier body that out-sustains your poke in a straight 1v1, and Stand United means he's impacting the whole map while you're stuck pushing a sidelane you can't actually win solo. Your Overwhelm passive keeps you relevant, but he statchecks your squishy frame the moment Shadow Dash lands and Spirit's Refuge eats your attacks. Don't solo-duel him late — group, snare the Stand United channel to strand the ally he was rescuing, and peel his taunt in 5v5s.","whys":["Even at level 1 — your 550 range and Q chip are real, but Shen has no reason to step up and just farms safely with Q-empowered swings.","Q plus Solar Snare's ~1.5s root lets you punish a Shen who walks up to CS before his E taunt range gives him a gap-close answer.","Shadow Dash is 18s at rank 1 but reaches 600, and Spirit's Refuge blanks your empowered auto the moment he commits to the trade.","Shadow Dash drains 150 of his 200 energy, so the taunt and a 140-energy Twilight Assault rarely arrive back to back.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range — bait his E and W down first and this is your one clean burst window.","His tank itemization plus W auto-block out-sustains your poke, and his E taunt statchecks your squishy body once he's on you.","Shen out-scales this into an even-to-tankier 1v1 and his global R wins the map while you're stuck soloing a side you can't take."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"singed","win":["Mel","Skill","Singed","Singed","Mel","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q + Solar Snare you can root him the instant he steps inside Fling's 125 range, then walk out and Q-poke the rooted target free."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — even as he flings and runs, you chunk or execute him before he resets with poison trail."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your AP + mana spike (Liandry's/Lost Chapter) lets you chain Q poke and detonate freely while a not-yet-tanky Singed has no way to close the gap."},{"when":"Late","text":"His danger window: full Rylai's/Riftmaker drain-tank Singed eats your poke, perma-slows you with Poison Trail, and runs you down past one Solar Snare."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold Solar Snare for the step inside Fling's 125 range, root him, then Q-poke and back off before Poison Trail builds","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos pre-6 so Golden Eclipse is a real execute threat the second R is up","Shove him off his proxy wave and deny the CS/XP his whole drain-tank scaling depends on"],"foe":["Throw Mega Adhesive first, then Fling you into it — landing in that goo roots you on top of the Poison Trail","Proxy farm behind your wave and stack Rylai's/sustain so he out-heals your poke and tanks your burst","Build move speed and Rylai's so his 17s Mega Adhesive outlasts your 11s snare all game"]},"early":"Singed only has Fling and Poison Trail early, and neither out-ranges your 550 Q — so this is your window to bully. Hold Solar Snare for the exact moment he walks inside Fling's 125 range: root him, Q the stationary target, then step out before the trail tics you down. Do NOT dry-Q the wave while he is that close, because his kill pattern is flipping you into the trail and toward his tower. Keep stacking Overwhelm off Q and empowered autos while he still can't sustain it.","mid":"This is your takeover. With Q ranked and Solar Snare's root plus slow field, you control every step-up — he can't reach you without eating a poke he can't yet drain back. At 6, Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up Overwhelm from any range, so even as he flings and kites away on his move speed, you chunk or execute him first. Read the ground before you read his cooldowns: once Mega Adhesive is thrown you have 17 seconds at rank 1 where a Fling has no goo to root you in. Force fights on his proxy waves.","late":"This is where Singed reclaims it. Once he's full drain-tank — Rylai's, Riftmaker, sustain — he eats your poke, his Rylai's W-trail and W move speed perma-slow you, and your single Solar Snare can't peel him when he flings and runs you down. You stay relevant on Overwhelm scaling, but you're a 550-range squishy with no dash and one CC against a target you can no longer kite. Close the game on your first-item lead and the tempo from a denied proxy — never let it reach a 1v1 sidelane where he flings you under his tower.","whys":["Fling reaches 125 and Poison Trail is a toggle he pays mana for — poke him as he steps to the wave.","Solar Snare is 11s to Fling's 10s — root him as he commits and free-poke the rooted target.","With Q, E and W online you out-range his fling, root his step-ups, and disengage his poison trail with W's shield and ms.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from repeated pokes faster than a pre-Rylai's Singed can drain them back.","Golden Eclipse detonates stacked Overwhelm from any range, so you chunk or execute him even as he flings and kites away.","Your AP + mana item lets you chain Q and detonate freely while he still has no gap-close to punish you.","Full drain-tank Singed out-sustains your poke and his Rylai's slow plus move speed run you down past your one root — play safe and end before this."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"sion","win":["Skill","Mel","Skill","Sion","Sion","Sion","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke into Solar Snare root is your one clean punish window before he buys armor and stacks health — land E on him stepping up for a cannon."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"A charged Decimating Smash is the threat: it connects, Soul Furnace detonates on top of you, and you have no dash out of the follow-up."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Golden Eclipse should execute — but his health pool plus Glory in Death mean the detonation rarely closes the kill and he reanimates to keep swinging at you."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Sion's MR and HP scaling outpace your Overwhelm; he buys Spirit Visage/Force of Nature, soaks your poke, and turns into a teamfight engage you can't peel."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2 first and land Solar Snare's root the instant he walks up to last-hit a cannon, then Q-stack while he is stuck","Reflect Roar of the Slayer with Rebuttal — that 800-range poke is the only projectile in his kit","Stack Overwhelm in the 15 seconds after Soul Furnace detonates — that is the one window with no shield in the way"],"foe":["Charge Decimating Smash to the knockup, then walk in behind Soul Furnace and re-cast it for the chunk","Buy early armor and stack health so Overwhelm's execute threshold never triggers on his fat HP bar","Scale into a tank, perma-shove, and flank with Unstoppable Onslaught, which charges through your CC"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you have one ability and your ranged auto, he just walks up and last-hits behind Soul Furnace. Your one real window is Level 2: get Q and E first, and the moment he steps up for a cannon, land Solar Snare's root and unload Q bolts while he's stuck. After that it gets ugly. Soul Furnace soaks your Q poke, Roar of the Slayer reaches 800 against your 950, and a charged Decimating Smash is a death sentence — zero dashes means one landed knockup is a full combo. Stay at max range, never facecheck for the cannon, and respect a charged Q from fog.","mid":"This is where the lane slips away. On paper your kit eats immobile juggernauts, but Sion isn't trying to all-in you — he buys armor, stacks health, and shoves the wave into your tower so you can't punish. Your Overwhelm execute needs the stored damage to exceed his health-plus-shields, and Soul Furnace plus a growing HP bar means that threshold almost never trips. At 6 your Golden Eclipse should be a kill, but Glory in Death means even a good detonation just reanimates him to keep swinging or take your tower. Spend Rebuttal reflecting Roar of the Slayer, which also knocks a minion back through everyone behind it.","late":"You lose the scaling race outright. Sion becomes a frontline tank with Spirit Visage and Force of Nature — your Overwhelm stacks and empowered autos tickle his MR-stacked HP, and your execute threshold is a fantasy against a 4000-HP bruiser. Worse, he stops caring about lane: he perma-shoves, then R-flanks your backline from across the map with an unstoppable charge you cannot stop with one 1.5s root. Your value is sieging from max range in teamfights and saving W to deny his engage — but the 1v1 and the map both belong to him. Win nothing in lane and you have nothing late.","whys":["You both have weak Level 1s — one ability and an auto each — and his W shield blanks your single Q, so neither of you commits.","Q plus Solar Snare's root is your one guaranteed punish: catch him stepping up for a cannon before his armor and HP make trades pointless.","Soul Furnace shields him and re-casts after 3s for its damage, but you can reflect Roar of the Slayer — so the trade evens out.","A charged Decimating Smash into Roar of the Slayer out-damages your poke, and you have no dash out of the follow-up.","Golden Eclipse should execute, but his huge HP bar keeps you under the threshold and his zombie passive revives him through your detonation.","First item he is a tank soaking your Q and empowered autos; your Overwhelm can't out-pace his health-plus-MR stacking.","He out-scales hard: a full-tank Sion with R engage shrugs off your poke and flanks your backline while you can only siege from range."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Swain","Swain","Skill","Skill","Swain","Swain"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your W (Rebuttal) eats his E hook and Q poke and fires them back as your damage — your only clean trade windows are when his E is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His Demonic Ascension (R) flips every extended fight: once he drains he out-heals your Q poke, so never stand in it past your own R detonation."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Swain's first AP item (Liandry's/Blackfire) overlapping Death's Hand bolts and Vision of Empire out-DPS your Overwhelm chip."},{"when":"Late","text":"Soul-stacked Swain with R uptime kites your snare and drains your team — your fragile frame gets pulled and bursted before R lands."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold W (Rebuttal) for his E hook and Q bolt — eating his pull is your single biggest swing in this lane","Land Solar Snare (E) root only when his W bomb and E are down, then Q-stack and R before he can drain back","Cross-map and roam — you cannot win the straight 1v1, so deny him farm and snare for your jungler instead"],"foe":["Land his E (Nevermove) root to pin you so his Q and W bomb land free while you have no dash to escape","Drag every fight long with R drain so his sustain out-paces your Overwhelm poke","Stack souls off your wave and scale into an unkillable AOE teamfight monster"]},"early":"My one tool here is W — Rebuttal eats his E hook and his Q bolt and throws them back, so the whole early game is baiting his E onto my wall. At levels 1-3 I can match his Q poke and even land Solar Snare for a punish, but the moment his E lands I have no dash to escape and his Q-W combo chunks me hard. Never walk up to CS with my W already spent; if his E is down, that's my window to step up, snare, and Q-stack.","mid":"This is where it slides away. By 4-6 his Q passive ranks and his bomb (W) out-trades my short pokes, and the second his R comes online any extended fight is lost — Demonic Ascension out-heals my Q drip and turns my Overwhelm stacks into a losing race. I can still threaten a snare-into-R burst if I catch him with R down and his pull on cooldown, but if I miss E I'm a fragile mage standing in his drain with no escape. Bait the hook, never the duel.","late":"Late I'm the squishy one and he's the AOE monster. Soul-stacked Swain pulls me with E from fog and drains my whole frame before my R detonation lands, and my W only blocks one projectile in a teamfight full of threats. My job is to never get caught — sit max range, snare him off my carries, and detonate Overwhelm from safety. I do NOT win the side-lane 1v1; force him into grouped fights where my R can hit his stacked team and let my frontline eat his drain.","whys":["Both of you are ranged pokers at level 1 — you can match his Q, and your auto plus first ability trade even before his kit comes online.","His E pull is still single-rank and your W can eat it — with snare plus W reflect you can hold the trade even, but barely.","Death's Hand stacks damage per bolt up close, so he out-pokes your short trades and his E hook punishes your zero-dash frame.","His Q ramps and every Vision of Empire hit feeds a Ravenous Flock fragment that out-heals your Overwhelm poke.","Demonic Ascension (R) drains through your Q poke and out-heals any fight you commit to — never duel him past 6.","His first AP item's burn plus W bomb out-DPS your stack-and-detonate before your R is even worth casting.","Soul-stacked Swain pulls you from fog and drains your squishy frame before R lands — you lose the 1v1 outright and only matter as a peel/snare bot."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Sylas","Sylas","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare root punishes every time Sylas walks up to last-hit or tries Abscond into Chain Lash."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks for burst from range, but Hijack can take that same ult — at rank 1 it is 80s, so a wasted Hijack is a real window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter / Liandry's online: chain Q pokes and Overwhelm detonations to chunk him before his W drain heals it back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kingslayer's heal out-statchecks your poke once he has AP — buy Grievous Wounds before this window or his sustain beats your kite."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare root the instant he E-dashes in, then Q-poke and back away before his W drain lands","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, then detonate with Golden Eclipse from max range while he is low","Hold W to eat his E projectile / poke and feed it back as your own magic damage"],"foe":["Abscond in and recast Abduct to close the gap, then Chain Lash slow into Kingslayer","Bait or wait out your Solar Snare root, then all-in when his E and your one CC are down","Steal your Golden Eclipse with R, or scale to 2+ AP items where his drain-heal out-sustains your poke"]},"early":"Sylas has to walk into your 550 range to farm, and that is where you tax him. At level 2 with Q and Solar Snare, root him the moment he steps up for a last-hit or commits an early Abscond, then layer Q bolts and empowered autos to stack Overwhelm. His E is only a 400 dash and it does not stun — Abduct's chain is the reach, so if that whiffs he eats free poke. Hold W for the Abduct chain and fire it back.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are yours: your Q ranks up, Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated trades, and you can chunk him before his W drain heals it back. The key read at 6 is his R — Golden Eclipse is a brutal execute on a stacked, low Sylas, but he can STEAL it with his own ultimate. Only detonate when his R is on cooldown, and never burn your one root into a Sylas who still has E up to dash on top of you. Bait the E, root the recovery, then Eclipse.","late":"This flips. Once Sylas has two AP items his Q/W drain-and-heal turns every all-in into a sustained fight you cannot kite forever — he dashes in, stuns with E, and out-statchecks your short trades while healing through your poke. You stay fragile with zero dashes and one CC. Don't take 1v1s into a fed itemized Sylas; group, hold W for his engage, and let your team punish him while you detonate Overwhelm from the back.","whys":["Level 1 you both have one ability — your 550 range pokes but you lack the projectile count to commit, and his single E can punish a step-up.","Q plus Solar Snare gives you a guaranteed root-and-poke punish every time Sylas walks up to last-hit.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke him, root his Abscond, and feed the Abduct chain back through your wall.","Your Q ranks and Overwhelm stacks accumulate faster than his W drain can heal, so you win the repeated trades.","Golden Eclipse executes a stacked Sylas from range, but he can steal it with R — even window, only commit when his ult is down.","Lost Chapter and your first AP item let you chain pokes and detonate freely before his drain-heal recovers.","Two AP items turn Kingslayer into sustain that out-statchecks unmitigated poke — without Grievous Wounds his all-in beats your kite from here."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"tahmkench","win":["Mel","Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench","Mel","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — root him as he walks up to last-hit and chunk a tank who cannot dash out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range — bait the Thick Skin shield out first, it is up every 3s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your power peak — mana and AP let you chain Q poke and execute through his sustain; force every fight here."},{"when":"Lvl 3+","text":"His threat window: three An Acquired Taste stacks arm both the Tongue Lash stun and Devour (R) — count them, not his Q."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare on his step-up so he eats Q poke he cannot grey-heal back fast enough","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, then detonate Golden Eclipse once Thick Skin's shield is spent","Hold W to eat his Q tongue projectile and fire it back, denying his only gap-close stun"],"foe":["Build three An Acquired Taste stacks — that is what arms his stun and Devour","Soak poke and out-last it with grey-health passive plus percent-HP sustain over a long lane","Shove and use R to roam other lanes since he cannot win the 1v1 outright"]},"early":"Tahm is slow, has no dash, and walks up to melee CS — exactly the laner Solar Snare was built to punish. At level 2-3, root him as he steps for a minion and rain Q on top, then weave your empowered auto; he cannot escape a 1.5s root. The one thing to respect is the stack counter: at three An Acquired Taste stacks his Tongue Lash stuns, so never stand still in tongue range once it is full.","mid":"This is your lane to take over. As Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks pile from repeated trades, you out-poke him faster than Thick Skin can refund it, and at 6 Golden Eclipse detonates those stacks from any range — a tank with no mobility cannot dodge or close the gap. Bait his Tongue Lash first, then root, poke, and detonate. The only way he kills you is at three An Acquired Taste stacks, where a whiffed root becomes a stun into Devour (R).","late":"You win the straight-up lane all game — he cannot out-damage your stacked poke and execute, and Thick Skin only stretches the lane, it never wins it. The real problem is the map: Devour (R) both eats you at three stacks and saves his allies in fights. Keep your distance, never let the counter reach three in a sidelane, and keep chunking — but ward for his roams so a held lane never becomes a lost game elsewhere.","whys":["You both have a weak level 1 — Tongue Lash only damages and slows until three An Acquired Taste stacks land, so take your free CS.","Q + Solar Snare lets you root the dashless tank as he steps for a minion and stack a punish he cannot grey-heal back in time.","With Q, E and W online you poke, root and eat his tongue projectile — he has no answer to a ranged mage he can't reach.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm accumulates from every trade, out-pacing the Thick Skin refund on an immobile target.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stored stacks from range — cash it once Thick Skin (E) has already been spent on a shield.","First-item mana and AP let you chain Q pokes and execute freely — his sustain can't out-last your detonations now.","He never out-scales you in the 1v1, but his grey-health bulk and R roam make this a Skill window — respect his map pressure, not his lane."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"teemo","win":["Skill","Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Skill","Teemo","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Solar Snare (E) lands a guaranteed root the instant Teemo steps up for a cannon — your one clean punish window before his blind defines the lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — if you've poked him low with Q he can't blind a button-press execute, your one real spike."},{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Teemo's Blinding Dart (Q) kills your empowered autos — but it is a projectile, so Rebuttal reflects it and blinds him instead. It is 7s flat."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Liandry's/Nashor's Teemo out-ranges and out-poisons you while shrooms wall your retreat lanes — his peak window, not yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit your Q (Radiant Volley) barrage from max range to stack Overwhelm without ever stepping into Blinding Dart auto range","Land Solar Snare (E) on a Teemo who steps up to last-hit, then dump a full Q before the root breaks","Reach Level 6 with stacks built so Golden Eclipse can execute him from range before his blind matters"],"foe":["Blind your empowered autos with Q every trade so your Overwhelm never stacks","Kite at his 500+ range on Move Quick (W) and chip you with Toxic Shot (E) poison you can't cleanse","Stack shrooms on your retreat paths and the side brush so you can never reposition safely"]},"early":"Two ranged champs, but his range and his blind beat mine. Teemo's Blinding Dart shuts off my empowered autos, so every stack I try to build through an auto just dies — I have to do my Overwhelm work with Q (Radiant Volley) from max range, never by stepping up to auto him. My one real early play is Level 2 Solar Snare: if he walks up to last-hit, throw the orb, root him, and dump a Q barrage before it breaks. Outside that, eat the poison, farm with the tip of Q, and do not chase — he kites my whole kit with move speed.","mid":"This is where he pulls ahead. His E poison ticks me down for free and his Q is up for every trade, so I can't win a sustained poke war at his range. The exception is Level 6: if I've quietly stacked Overwhelm with Q pokes, Golden Eclipse detonates from any range and he can't blind a button — that's my one kill window, so set it up before I press R. Otherwise hold W (Rebuttal) for when he commits a real auto-poke combo so I eat his projectile and fling it back. Do not facecheck for him — his shrooms are already on my flanks.","late":"I lose the lane long-term and I lose the map. Teemo out-ranges me, his poison out-DPSes my poke, and his shrooms turn every choke and retreat lane into a death trap my squishy frame can't survive. Guerrilla Warfare (P) also lets him sit invisible in brush and move while hidden there, and I have no dash and no reveal. Give up the splitpush side, group with my team where Golden Eclipse can detonate multiple stacked targets, and never walk a brush line alone.","whys":["One ability and a ranged auto each — even footing, but his Blinding Dart already threatens to cancel any auto I commit, so I only trade with Q.","My Q + Solar Snare gives me a guaranteed root punish if he steps up, but he can blind the Q-empowered auto follow-up, keeping it even.","His Q is up every 7s and Toxic Shot chips me every trade — but any Q tick strips Move Quick's passive speed, so keep him tagged.","As his blind and poison scale he owns the sustained poke war; my short trades can't out-damage his free chip from outside my Q.","Golden Eclipse detonates stacked Overwhelm from any range and he can't blind an instant — if I poked him low, this is my one stage to kill him.","His Liandry's/Nashor's poke and shroom zoning out-range and out-sustain my Q, and his blind still blanks my autos — his peak.","He out-ranges and out-poisons me while shrooms wall my retreats; I have no escape if he reaches me, so the long game is his."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"trundle","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel","Trundle","Skill","Trundle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare root lands a free punish if Trundle steps up to last-hit before his sustain is online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range, your one clean burst window before his Subjugate heal/tank turns the all-in."},{"when":"His Lvl 6 R","text":"Subjugate steals your Health, Armor and Magic Resistance and doubles the theft over four seconds, the moment he flips a losing trade."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"King's Tribute and Frozen Domain out-heal your poke, he gets too tanky for Overwhelm to execute, and Pillar of Ice walls you from 1000 range."}],"wants":{"you":["Root him at Solar Snare's centre from 1000, then stack Overwhelm with Q before King's Tribute heals it","Save Rebuttal, 38s at rank 1, for the damage immunity and move speed that kite you out of a Pillar of Ice wall","Detonate Golden Eclipse and back off before he can land Subjugate and out-heal the trade"],"foe":["Use Frozen Domain (W) move speed plus Pillar of Ice (E) to wall and run you down past your poke","Out-heal your chip with King's Tribute in Frozen Domain so Overwhelm never converts","Bait your Solar Snare, then engage on its long cooldown and Subjugate (R) to heal through your burst"]},"early":"Trundle has no dash and answers at Chomp's 300 range, so Radiant Volley at 950 and Solar Snare at 1000 are free as long as you respect Pillar of Ice (21s at rank 1). At level 2 you can root him the instant he walks up to a minion and chunk him before King's Tribute heals it back off the dying wave. Chomp is not his sustain — it saps your Attack Damage on a flat 3.5s — but his passive heals off every unit that dies near him, so punish the step-up and otherwise hold your stacks.","mid":"This is your window: keep max range, stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, and at 6 detonate Golden Eclipse — it shares Subjugate's 120/100/80 timer, so whoever ults first owns the fight. Never get walled: Pillar of Ice (21s, 1000 range) is impassable terrain and you have no dash, while Frozen Domain's move speed closes the gap. Subjugate steals your Health, Armor and Magic Resistance, so armour is the wrong buy — root the walk-up with Solar Snare and disengage before his R lands.","late":"He reclaims this lane outright once itemized. King's Tribute heals a percent of every unit that dies near him and Frozen Domain amplifies all of it, so buy Morellonomicon early or your poke never sticks. Subjugate steals Health, Armor and Magic Resistance — resist stacking hands him the stats — so buy damage and range instead. Stop trying to 1v1 the pillar all-in: group, kite him in the open where his only engage is walking, and never let him corner you on a wall.","whys":["You both have a weak level 1, but King's Tribute heals him off every dying minion, so a pure poke war is a coin flip on who lands first.","Q plus Solar Snare lets you root and punish him as he steps up to last-hit, before his Frozen Domain sustain is fully online.","Rebuttal blanks his damage, King's Tribute heals your chip back off the wave, so neither converts the trade cleanly, it is even.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm builds, but King's Tribute sustains through it, trading your poke for his heal at a wash.","Golden Eclipse and Subjugate share a 120/100/80 timer, but his steals your Health, Armor and MR outright — level 6 belongs to him.","Your first item lets you chain pokes, yet his sustain and pillar walk-up keep him in the fight, so the lane stays a stalemate.","He out-scales hard: King's Tribute out-sustains your poke and he gets too tanky for Overwhelm to execute, then Pillar of Ice corners you for the kill."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"tryndamere","win":["Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Skill","Tryndamere","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q plus Solar Snare's root is your cleanest punish — root him as he steps to last-hit and rain Radiant Volley before Spinning Slash comes online at 3."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your Overwhelm stacks for an execute, but his R Undying Rage holds him at 1 HP for 5s — time your R for AFTER his Undying Rage ends, not into it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your poke peak: chain Q and empowered autos to chunk him before he hits the crit/fury breakpoint that lets E-spin onto you erase the lane."},{"when":"Late","text":"His threat window — full-crit Trynd closes 650 with Spinning Slash, refunds your chip with Bloodlust, and survives your execute with Undying Rage."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root the instant he commits E, then stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos before he closes","Use Rebuttal's damage immunity and move speed to blank a spin, then retreat facing him","Win every short trade levels 2-5 and roam, so his late-game crit scaling never gets to matter"],"foe":["Bank Battle Fury off minions, then Spinning Slash past your poke and crit you down","Land Mocking Shout at 850 so the back-turned slow catches you running from the spin","Survive your level 6 execute with Undying Rage, then crit-spin you to death while he is unkillable for 5s"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours because Spinning Slash is not up yet — he can only walk at you. Use Radiant Volley to poke him off the wave and the moment he steps up to last-hit, throw Solar Snare to root him and stack Overwhelm through the field's slow. Hold Rebuttal for the crit burst, not for chip: it prevents damage outright, which is the only thing that blanks a spin. Do not push the wave — a shoved lane lets him Spinning Slash in on a gank or bank Fury freely.","mid":"Levels 4-6 tip toward even as Battle Fury and Spinning Slash (650 range, 12s at rank 1) come online. Your Q is ranking up and Overwhelm accumulating, so keep poking, but one spin puts him inside your range with no dash for you to answer. Mocking Shout only slows you if your back is turned, so retreat facing him. The trap at 6 is Undying Rage: do NOT fire Golden Eclipse into a Trynd you cannot kill outright. Root his engage, kite with Rebuttal, detonate once his R is down.","late":"This is where he takes over. A full-crit Tryndamere closes your 550 poke with Spinning Slash and shrugs off your execute with Undying Rage, while Bloodlust converts banked Fury straight back into health — buy Morellonomicon or the chip means nothing. Stop dueling: shove and roam, hit other lanes with R from range, and never get caught alone in a side lane. In teamfights peel yourself with Solar Snare and let your frontline soak the spin, but the solo kill belongs to him now.","whys":["He has no E to gap-close at level 1 — poke with Radiant Volley and last-hit at max range while he can only walk into it.","Q plus Solar Snare's root is a guaranteed punish on a dash-less Trynd stepping up for CS.","With Q, E and W online you poke, root and disengage anything a pre-Fury Trynd tries.","Even window: your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks, but his Fury and E-gap start to answer your kite.","Even at 6: Golden Eclipse threatens an execute, but Undying Rage lets him survive it for 5s and spin back — time it carefully.","His first crit items let E-spin reach you inside 550 range and out-DPS your poke trades.","Full-crit Trynd closes with Spinning Slash, refunds the chip with Bloodlust and survives your R with Undying Rage — roam and teamfight."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"urgot","win":["Mel","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Mel"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare root lands a guaranteed punish if Urgot walks up to last-hit before Echoing Flames is ranked — your one clean early window."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Purge drops to 6s at rank 3 and 0s at rank 5, so his Echoing Flames chip never stops once he is inside your range — and you have no dash out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fear Beyond Death (R) ends you — but the chem-drill is a projectile, so Rebuttal answers it if you saved it for exactly this."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Tanky Urgot with Tabi/Bramble shrugs your magic poke while his percent-HP shotguns delete your squishy frame in a sustained fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit your Level 2 Q + Solar Snare root to punish Urgot stepping up for a single cannon-minion CS","Poke him hardest while Purge is running — it slows him, and his legs only reach you point-blank","Root him as he steps to Disdain — your 11s snare beats his 16s charge, so holding it is free"],"foe":["Charge in with Disdain (E), then hold you in Echoing Flames leg range while Purge runs","Land Disdain (E) to cross 475 units and hold you in leg range for the all-in","Land Fear Beyond Death (R) so any low-HP trade becomes a free execute kill"]},"early":"Your one real window is Level 2: if Urgot steps up to last-hit before Echoing Flames and Purge are online, Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish. After that it sours fast — his close-range chip out-sustains your Q, though Purge slows him while it runs. Don't trade autos into him. His legs are point-blank and not projectiles, but Corrosive Charge (Q) and Fear Beyond Death (R) both are, so Rebuttal has real targets — save it for the chem-drill instead.","mid":"This is where you lose the lane. Once Purge ranks up his close-range chip out-damages your Q — but it slows him while it runs, so that is when you poke, not when you flee. At 6 Disdain (E) closes 475 units and Fear Beyond Death executes you under the threshold. Hold Solar Snare for the moment he steps to charge: at 11s it comes back faster than his 16s Disdain, so holding it costs you no tempo. Hug your turret, take safe CS, and play for jungle ganks.","late":"You don't out-scale him in this specific lane. Urgot builds tanky with Tabi and Bramble, so your magic poke bounces off while his percent-max-HP shotgun legs shred your squishy frame in any sustained fight — and sustained DPS is exactly what he wants. Golden Eclipse can't execute through his health pool the way it does immobile squishies, and his R will out-execute you first. Stay grouped, never get caught sidelaning against him, and let your team peel; your stacks matter on the rest of his team, not on him.","whys":["You both have a weak level 1 with one ability — your ranged auto poke is mirrored by his, no clear owner yet.","Q plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish if he steps up to CS before his shotgun legs are online.","Echoing Flames off his autos and Purge comes online and starts out-sustaining your Q chip — it evens out and tips his way.","Ranked Echoing Flames legs out-damage your poke, and Disdain closes 475 units past the range you live on.","Disdain into Fear Beyond Death is lethal — 16s and 100s at rank 1, so both are trackable.","Tanky bruiser itemization shrugs your magic poke while his percent-HP legs keep shredding you in extended trades.","Tabi/Bramble Urgot out-statchecks your poke and his R execute beats Golden Eclipse against his health pool — he reclaims the late."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"vayne","win":["Skill","Vayne","Vayne","Skill","Skill","Vayne","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root pins Vayne the instant she steps up — Tumble is only a dash until Final Hour is up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from range — chunk or execute Vayne the moment she over-extends for a CS."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With your first AP item plus mana you chain-poke and detonate freely; this is the cleanest kill window before her crit items come online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Vayne's biggest threat: Silver Bolts procs on the third attack or ability, and Condemn counts as one — two autos and the bolt is the whole combo past two items."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root every time Vayne steps into Q range, then stack Overwhelm for the R detonation","Hold Rebuttal for Condemn — the bolt is a projectile, so the wall throws it back at her","Snowball the level 3-to-first-item window and end the game before her crit items take over"],"foe":["Tumble the reset auto in, then Condemn as the third Silver Bolts hit for true damage","Farm under tower and scale to two crit items where her percent-HP true damage shreds you","Bait your E cooldown, then Condemn you into a wall for a free all-in or jungler follow-up"]},"early":"Vayne is helpless into your range early — she has no waveclear and no answer to Q poke while she's stuck last-hitting under threat. At level 2 with Q plus Solar Snare, root her the second she walks up for a CS and chunk her with the field's slow follow-up. Hold Rebuttal for Condemn itself — it is a projectile, so W reflects it — and spend the root freely, because Tumble hides nothing before 6.","mid":"This is your takeover window. With Q ranked and Overwhelm stacking off every poke, you out-range and out-chunk her completely — she can't trade back without Silver Bolts procs you simply don't let her land. At 6, Golden Eclipse turns built-up stacks into an execute from any range, so detonate the moment she steps up greedy. Bait her Tumble with a Q feint, then Solar Snare the landing spot and follow with R.","late":"You are on a clock. From two items onward Vayne flips the lane — Silver Bolts deal percent-max-HP true damage that melts your squishy frame, and Condemn into a wall is a death sentence with no dash to escape it. Win the game off your early-mid lead before her crit spike; if it goes long, you cannot duel her, so play for poke from max range, never get caught alone, and let your team peel for the detonation.","whys":["You have one ability and a ranged auto, and so does she — neither of you can commit, so just deny her last-hits and set up your level 2.","Q plus Solar Snare's ~1.5s root lands a guaranteed punish the moment she steps into CS range, before Tumble is a reliable escape.","With Q, E and W online you poke freely, root her step-ups and reflect Condemn itself with Rebuttal — she has no answer yet.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from repeated trades; she has no waveclear to answer your range and no sustain to heal the poke.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range, turning a greedy step-up into a chunk or execute she can't itemize against yet.","First AP item plus mana lets you chain pokes and detonate freely — your most dominant window before her crit items reach their spike.","She out-scales hard: itemized Silver Bolts true-damage shreds you and Condemn pins you to a wall — play safe and let your team handle her."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir","Skill","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Solar Snare (E) plus Radiant Volley (Q) you can root a Vlad who steps up to last-hit and chunk him before Sanguine Pool is leveled to bail him out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse (R) detonates your built-up Overwhelm stacks from range for a burst he can only dodge by pre-pooling — bait W first, then ult."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your mana-and-AP spike lets you chain Q pokes and R detonations freely while Vlad is still one Rylai's/Liandry's item from his own power tier."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Vlad's threat window: with two AP items his Q drain and untargetable W out-sustain your poke and his late teamfight burst eclipses your fragile body."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare (E) roots on a stepped-up Vlad and stack Overwhelm with Radiant Volley (Q) before he can pool out","Detonate Golden Eclipse (R) on full Overwhelm stacks the instant his Sanguine Pool (W) is on cooldown","Snowball your level 2-6 windows and end the lane before his second AP item out-sustains your poke"],"foe":["Sanguine Pool (W) the moment your Solar Snare lands or your R detonates, dodging the root and the execute entirely","Sustain through your Q poke with Transfusion and Hemoplague, refusing to break even on trades","Stall to two AP items where Rylai's/Liandry's let him out-poke and out-scale your squishy frame"]},"early":"Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s in the game, but my early presence is real and I can punish him. Levels 2-3 are my window: once Solar Snare (E) is up I root him the second he steps into the wave to last-hit, then Radiant Volley (Q) chunks him and stacks Overwhelm while Sanguine Pool (W) is still 28s at rank 1 and cannot save him every time. He has no mana, so watch Crimson Rush instead — a full bar means his next Transfusion hits and heals for far more. Don't dump into a Vlad who has already pooled; those 2s eat my root and stacks for free.","mid":"Levels 4-6 stay mine on paper — my Q ranks up, Overwhelm accumulates off repeated pokes, and at 6 Golden Eclipse (R) turns those stacks into a real burst threat from range. But Sanguine Pool is the whole problem: he goes untargetable for 2s through my E root AND through my R detonation, so I never commit either into an up pool. It is 28s at rank 1, so bait it with poke pressure, then chain E-root into Q into R while it is down. Rebuttal is gold too — it stops damage outright, so raise it for the Hemoplague detonation.","late":"This is where the lane gets away from me, and I have to be honest about it. Vlad is a hard scaler — Crimson Pact turns every point of his AP into bonus health, so each damage item also makes him bulkier, and without Grievous Wounds his Transfusion out-sustains my poke. Sanguine Pool dodges every targeted thing I own including the R execute. My Overwhelm passive keeps me relevant, but a full-build Vlad kites my dash-less, one-CC body. So cash in my level 2-6 and first-item windows hard, end the lane before his second item, and late-game stop trying to solo him — group, peel with Solar Snare, and let my team answer him.","whys":["Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s, but so are you with one ability — deny his Q last-hits and set up your level-2 power spike.","Solar Snare's root plus Radiant Volley lets you land a guaranteed punish on a Vlad who steps up, before his W pool is ranked to save him.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke and out-trade a pre-item Vlad — root, chunk, and bait his pool so its long cooldown is up when you commit.","It's a coin-flip stretch: you still out-poke him, but a zero-cost Transfusion every 9s claws your chip back without Grievous Wounds.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm for real burst — bait Sanguine Pool first, then ult, because the pool dodges the execute outright.","Your mana-and-AP first-item spike lets you chain pokes and detonations freely while he's still one item from his own power tier — force it now.","He out-scales hard: two-item Vlad out-sustains your poke, pools every targeted spell, and bursts your fragile body — play safe and let your team deal with him."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Mel","Volibear","Skill","Volibear"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a free punish when Voli steps up for CS before his Q dash is online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Stormbringer leaps 550 and disables your turret where it lands — at 6 he can dive you under tower, not just walk you down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lost Chapter into Liandry's lets you chain Q and detonate Overwhelm before Frenzied Maul's second cast heals it back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"An itemized Voli statchecks you — Frenzied Maul heals on the second cast and applies on-hit, so his attack speed, not armour, shreds you."}],"wants":{"you":["Root him with Solar Snare while Thundering Smash is charging so the stun never reaches you","Save Rebuttal, 38s at rank 1, for the damage immunity and move speed that break you out of a Frenzied Maul brawl","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos, then burst-execute with Golden Eclipse before his W heals it off"],"foe":["Slow you with Sky Splitter from 1200, then walk in with Thundering Smash and stun on his attack","Drag the trade long — Frenzied Maul's second cast on you heals him back every 5s","Hit 6 and dive you: Stormbringer disables your turret where it lands, so tower is not an exit"]},"early":"Thundering Smash is not a dash — it grants him speed toward you and stuns on his next attack, 12s at rank 1 and only 300 range — so levels 1-3 are yours to bully. At level 2 with Q and Solar Snare, root him the instant he walks up to last-hit and chunk him with Radiant Volley before he can answer. Hold Rebuttal for its damage immunity and move speed, not for chip. Keep your distance: once he reaches auto range The Relentless Storm ramps his attack speed and the brawl is his.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your strongest window — ranked-up Radiant Volley and accumulating Overwhelm let you whittle him down while Thundering Smash (300 range, 12s at rank 1) is his only way in and Sky Splitter (1200 range, 16s) merely slows you and shields him. Bait either one, then root him with Solar Snare the moment it is spent. But respect level 6: Stormbringer leaps 550, slows, hands him bonus health and disables your turret where he lands, so tower is not an exit any more. Never poke from a spot one leap can reach.","late":"This is a true coin-flip lane that tips on who itemizes their win condition first. Lost Chapter into Liandry's lets you chain Radiant Volley and detonate Golden Eclipse before Frenzied Maul's second cast heals the poke off — pair it with Morellonomicon or the heal simply wins the exchange for him. From two items on Volibear out-statchecks you: Frenzied Maul applies on-hit and The Relentless Storm keeps ramping his attack speed, so the instant Solar Snare is down your squishy body folds. Kite him with your team and never take the solo duel.","whys":["Voli is a weak level 1 with only one ability, but so are you with a single skill and no projectile count to commit — neither side can do real damage yet.","Q plus Solar Snare's root is a guaranteed punish on a Voli stepping up for CS — Thundering Smash only reaches 300 and Sky Splitter is not up.","With Q, E and W online you out-range and root every engage — Thundering Smash walks, it does not leap, so 950 range holds him off.","Ranked-up Q and stacking Overwhelm let you out-poke his single-target, dodgeable engage while his W heal can't keep pace with chain pokes.","Stormbringer leaps 550, slows, hands him bonus health and disables your turret where it lands — with no dash you cannot survive that all-in.","Lost Chapter / Liandry's lets you chain Q and detonate Golden Eclipse stacks faster than his W bite can heal them — your best window to close the coin-flip.","An itemized Voli out-scales you: Frenzied Maul's on-hit plus ramping attack speed statcheck your squishy frame the moment Solar Snare is down."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"warwick","win":["Mel","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Mel","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus Solar Snare's root lands a free punish on Warwick as he steps up for a creep — rooted, Jaws of the Beast cannot lunge."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up Overwhelm stacks from range — chunk or execute him before his W move-speed or R can reach you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With your first AP item and mana you chain Q pokes freely — buy Morellonomicon here, because Eternal Hunger triples its healing under 25%."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (R+Flash)","text":"Warwick's kill path is Infinite Duress off Flash — the leap distance scales with his Blood Hunt move speed, so the range you think is safe isn't. Hold Flash."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare the moment Warwick walks up — the root kills his lunge — then Q-poke him for free Overwhelm stacks","Stack Overwhelm with Q and empowered autos pre-6, then detonate with Golden Eclipse for the execute","Keep max range and save W/E to peel his R or W-engage — never let a dashless Warwick close the gap"],"foe":["Switch on Blood Hunt's chase speed the moment you drop under 50% health","Land Infinite Duress off Flash — its leap distance scales with his Blood Hunt move speed","Drag it long so Jaws of the Beast and a sub-25% Eternal Hunger out-heal your poke"]},"early":"Jaws of the Beast lunges only 365 units, so the early game is yours to dictate from 550 range. At level 2 grab Q + E: when he steps up to last-hit, land Solar Snare's root — rooted he cannot lunge at all — and free-poke him with Q while he's stuck, stacking Overwhelm. Don't waste E as a panic button; it's your anti-engage tool, so hold it if he's hovering Blood Hunt to walk you down. Eternal Hunger heals him under 50% health and triples that healing under 25%, so never leave him parked in that window.","mid":"This is your takeover. As Q ranks up you out-poke Jaws of the Beast's healing — he can't drain what he can't reach. At 6, Golden Eclipse turns your accumulated Overwhelm stacks into burst from range; bait his walk-up, root with Solar Snare, then detonate to chunk or execute. His one real threat is Infinite Duress, 110 seconds at rank 1 — a whiffed one leaves him answerless for nearly two minutes. Buy Morellonomicon by your second item; his sustain is the matchup.","late":"You owned the lane, but late is where a farmed Warwick claws back. Infinite Duress is 70s at rank 3 and its leap scales with his Blood Hunt speed, so a single suppress can delete your squishy frame before you cast — you have zero dashes and only E to peel. Blood Hunt also senses anyone under 50% health, so never sidelane chipped: that is exactly how he picks his target. Stay with your team, hold W for the real all-in, and close the game on the lead you built rather than duelling a drain tank with R up.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s, but your 550-range auto pokes Warwick for free — Jaws of the Beast lunges only 365 units, so he has to walk the gap.","Q + E online: Solar Snare roots him as he steps up for CS — a rooted Warwick cannot lunge Jaws of the Beast, so every Overwhelm stack is free.","With Q, E and W up you poke, root and wall his engage — Blood Hunt's chase speed only switches on once you drop under 50% health.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm piles from repeated trades; Jaws of the Beast heals on an 8s cooldown he rarely gets close enough to spend.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks from range for burst or execute — but Primal Howl's 2.5s damage reduction eats it, so wait out his E.","First AP item plus mana lets you chain Q pokes and W his way in — your power peak against a melee with no gap-closer.","Once itemized, Infinite Duress off Flash can lock and delete you, and Eternal Hunger triples its healing when HE falls under 25% — close on your lead."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"wukong","win":["Mel","Skill","Wukong","Wukong","Mel","Wukong","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + E online: when he steps up to last-hit, drop Radiant Volley and root him — rooted, neither Nimbus Strike nor Warrior Trickster will fire."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates every Overwhelm stack from any range — if Nimbus Strike brings him in low, R executes him before Cyclone ever spins up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your power peak: mana and AP let you chain Q pokes and re-root every 11s, while Crushing Blow's armour shred does nothing at all to a mage."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ all-in","text":"His threat window: Nimbus Strike into a Crushing Blow reset plus Cyclone's knockup chains past your one root and bursts you without Flash."}],"wants":{"you":["Root him before he commits — a rooted Wukong can cast neither Nimbus Strike nor Warrior Trickster","Stack Overwhelm with Q poke and empowered autos, then detonate with Golden Eclipse the moment he dives low","Hold W to eat his all-in burst and reset spacing — Stone Skin's stacking armour does nothing to your magic damage"],"foe":["Bait Solar Snare with the Warrior Trickster clone, then Nimbus Strike the real you","Nimbus Strike a minion to halve the gap, then Crushing Blow and Cyclone once your root is down","Wait for a gank or your missed root, then commit the full dive before your items come online"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely even — he can sit out of your single-ability range and you can't commit yet, so just hit Radiant Volley on the wave and farm. The lane flips at 2: Q plus Solar Snare means when he walks up for a CS, you land the root and start banking Overwhelm stacks he can't trade back through. Watch for Nimbus Strike targeting a minion to halve the gap first — root him before he commits, because a rooted Wukong cannot dash at all, and Stone Skin's armour is meaningless against your magic kit.","mid":"This is your lane. Your Q cooldown drops and Overwhelm stacks pile up every time he steps into range, so poke him low and respect only one thing: Nimbus Strike into Cyclone is his entire all-in, and Cyclone is 130 seconds at rank 1. Bait it with spacing, and the moment he has committed onto you, clamp Solar Snare's root and detonate with Golden Eclipse — at 6 your built-up stacks plus R can flat execute a diving Wukong from range. Don't blow the root on a Warrior Trickster clone, or you hand him the window.","late":"You stay strong into him as long as he can't one-shot the dive — your infinitely-scaling passive keeps your poke and execute relevant, and W still eats his engage burst. The danger is the all-in math flipping: a fed Wukong with cooldowns up can Nimbus Strike in, chain a Crushing Blow reset and Cyclone's knockup, and burst your squishy frame before R comes back. Keep Flash for his commit, never face-check brush where the Warrior Trickster clone can hide the engage, and play around your team — you win the poke war but lose the coinflip if he lands the full chain with no peel.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you have one ability and your ranged auto, but so does he, and he can stay out of range and farm until you commit.","Q plus Solar Snare gives you a guaranteed punish: rooted, he can cast neither Nimbus Strike nor Warrior Trickster, so the Overwhelm is free.","With Q, E and W online you out-poke him and the barrier eats his engage burst — Stone Skin's stacking armour does nothing against your magic damage.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm accumulates every trade; Cyclone is 130s at rank 1, so his real all-in only arrives about once every two minutes.","Golden Eclipse turns your stacks into a ranged execute — if Nimbus Strike brings him in low, you detonate before Cyclone ever spins up.","At first item your mana and AP let you chain Q pokes and re-root every 11 seconds, punishing every Nimbus Strike entry — this is your peak.","Even is fair late: your scaling passive keeps you relevant, but a fed Nimbus Strike into Cyclone can burst you, so it hinges on Flash and peel."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"yasuo","win":["Mel","Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo","Mel","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — bolt his step-up for CS, then root him for free Overwhelm before Wind Wall exists. It's 25s once it does."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — even if he E-dashes onto you, R + the execute threat punishes his commit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Mana and AP let you chain Q pokes and Rebuttal his whirlwind; a 2-stack Steel Tempest is the only projectile Yasuo owns, so that's the one to catch."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His threat window: 2 crit items plus Last Breath — but R needs an airborne target, so solo it only fires off his own 2-stack Steel Tempest."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare to pin him for stacked Q pokes while Wind Wall sits on its 25s cooldown","Hold Rebuttal for the 2-stack Steel Tempest whirlwind — his only projectile in the kit","Detonate Overwhelm with Golden Eclipse the instant he dashes in, before his crit items come online"],"foe":["Time Wind Wall's 4 seconds to swallow your Q bolts, autos and the Solar Snare orb","Build crit (IE/Shieldbow) and dash E through minions to close your 550 range","Land a 2-stack Steel Tempest so Last Breath finally has an airborne target to blink to"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours: Wind Wall has nothing to block yet and Solar Snare is hard to dodge. Poke with Q from max range; when he steps up at level 2, root him and stack Overwhelm with a second Q. Way of the Wanderer shields him whenever he moves, so isolated chip is absorbed — land two bolts in a row or none. Read the wave: Sweeping Blade dashes through minions, so a thick wave is his ladder to you.","mid":"Levels 4-6 you own the all-in. Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks pile from every trade, so by 6 a single Golden Eclipse can chunk or execute him from range even after Sweeping Blade lands him on you. Bait Wind Wall — fake a Q or step in — and remember it is 25 seconds at rank 1 but only lasts 4, so one spent wall buys you two clean volleys. Hold Rebuttal for the 2-stack Steel Tempest whirlwind, the only projectile he owns.","late":"From 2+ items the lane flips — this is a scaler you cannot out-stat. Once Yasuo has Infinity Edge and Shieldbow he dashes through your minions, Wind Wall deletes your entire ranged kit, and Last Breath blinks to anything airborne — in a teamfight every ally knockup is his ticket onto you. Win this game before ~25 minutes: snowball your early leads into towers and let your team body him, because an infinitely-scaling passive does not save a squishy who gets jumped.","whys":["You poke with Q and a ranged auto while he has only a melee Steel Tempest — and no Wind Wall yet to block a single bolt.","Q plus Solar Snare roots his step-up, but Sweeping Blade dashes through minions — root him when the wave is thin, not stacked.","With Q, E and Rebuttal online you poke, root and eat the whirlwind — a 2-stack Steel Tempest is the only projectile he has to give.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from repeated trades; Wind Wall is 25s at rank 1 and lasts 4, so most volleys land clean.","Golden Eclipse detonates built-up stacks from any range and is no projectile — Wind Wall cannot touch the execute.","Mana and first-item AP let you chain pokes; his Way of the Wanderer shield eats isolated bolts — land two in a row.","He out-scales hard — IE and Shieldbow plus Wind Wall, and Last Breath blinks onto anything your own team knocks airborne."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"yone","win":["Mel","Skill","Yone","Yone","Mel","Yone","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare online — root him stepping up for CS and chunk him with a Q before Spirit Cleave shields him into a trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fate Sealed is the kill threat — it blinks BEHIND the back of the line and pulls; hiding behind an ally is his landing zone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"He buys Berserker's + first crit item and Spirit Cleave's cooldown scales with attack speed — the shield eating your burst arrives faster."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-itemed Yone walks through your poke behind a Spirit Cleave shield, and one Fate Sealed pull into combo deletes your squishy frame."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2 first and land Solar Snare's root on him as he walks up for a minion, then Q-poke the free trade","Hold W to eat the third Mortal Steel and the Spirit Cleave swing — he has no projectile to reflect","Keep him out with Q and detonate Overwhelm the instant he commits, before Soul Unbound snaps him back to the body he left behind"],"foe":["Wait out your Solar Snare and Q, then land the third Mortal Steel on you and shield with Spirit Cleave","Bank Soul Unbound so any all-in is a free swing he can undo — 22s at rank 1, 10s at rank 5","Reach 6, then blink behind you with Fate Sealed and pull, where one root cannot save you"]},"early":"I have a real window early — at Level 2 with Q and Solar Snare I can root him as he steps up for a minion and stack a free Q-poke on top, and Soul Unbound does not exist yet to undo it. The catch is Spirit Cleave: a 700-range cone that shields him every time it lands, so I poke and back off and never stand in cleave range. He owns no projectile at all, so my W is damage immunity, not a reflect — spend it on the third Mortal Steel. My root is my only CC, so if I whiff it I have nothing.","mid":"From 4-6 the lane tilts toward him. My Q ranks up and Overwhelm builds from trades, but at 6 Fate Sealed blinks him behind the last champion in the line and pulls — 1000 range, 120s at rank 1 — and Soul Unbound lets him undo the trade afterwards. My Solar Snare is a single root I often won't have up for both his entrance and his exit. Worse, every ability he casts is free while my Q costs 70 mana, so his whiffs cost him nothing and mine cost me the next trade entirely.","late":"This is where the 42% lives. A two-item Yone walks through my Q poke behind a Spirit Cleave shield whose cooldown shrinks as he stacks attack speed, and one Fate Sealed pull off a Mortal Steel combo deletes my squishy frame before Overwhelm can matter. My infinite passive scaling does not save me when he simply gaps the range I rely on. Play for side-lane safety, spend W on his burst instead of saving it for a projectile he does not own, and let my team peel.","whys":["Both weak with one ability — Mortal Steel needs two stacks before it dashes at all, and I lack the projectile count, so I just set up CS.","My Q + Solar Snare punishes him stepping up, and Soul Unbound is not online yet to undo the trade at level 2.","With Q, E and W online I out-poke a Yone whose Spirit Cleave shield is still small, and my root denies his step-up outright.","His Mortal Steel ranks up and costs him nothing while my Q costs 70 mana — his misses are free and mine buy him the next window.","Fate Sealed arrives — it blinks behind the last champion in the line and pulls, and my single Solar Snare can't cover entrance and exit.","He buys Berserker's and a crit item; Spirit Cleave's cooldown scales with attack speed, so the shield eating my burst comes back faster.","Soul Unbound is 10s at rank 5, so he pokes from a spirit he can rewind, and one Fate Sealed combo deletes me whatever my passive scales to."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"yorick","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + Solar Snare lets you root Yorick the instant he steps up to a ghoul-walled minion and unload a free Radiant Volley before his ghouls reach you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates stacked Overwhelm from any range, so you can execute him over Dark Procession's wall without ever entering Walker-swarm distance."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With your first AP/mana item you chain Q pokes and break Dark Procession's wall down, out-zoning him off the wave as he sets up a slow-push."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Yorick has 2+ items, Maiden plus Dark Procession's wall pin you in the side lane and Mourning Mist's armour shred lets the Walkers out-trade you."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Solar Snare's root when he walks up to last-hit behind his ghouls, then free-cast Radiant Volley on the rooted target","Keep Rebuttal up for Mourning Mist so the mark that sprints his Walkers at you never lands","Build Overwhelm stacks with Q + empowered autos and detonate with Golden Eclipse from max range before he can swarm you"],"foe":["Wall you off the wave with Dark Procession so his Walkers and Maiden free-hit you while you cannot kite","Land Mourning Mist at 700 to shred your armour and sprint his Walkers on","Survive lane to 2+ items and a Maiden, then split-push the side lane where his trap kit beats your poke"]},"early":"Mourning Mist (E) is the only thing that turns this lane for him early — a 700-range globule on 12s at rank 1 that shreds your armour, slows you and marks you so his Mist Walkers sprint at the mark. Sidestep it or blank it with Rebuttal. He is pure melee with Walkers until 6, so when he steps up to last-hit behind his ghoul line, throw Solar Snare to root him and dump Radiant Volley while he cannot reach you. Dark Procession's wall is destructible — if he boxes you in, break it.","mid":"This is your best stretch: your Q ranks up, Overwhelm piles from repeated pokes, and at 6 Golden Eclipse detonates those stacks from any range — you can chunk him over Dark Procession's wall without entering Walker distance. Keep Rebuttal for the Mourning Mist engage; blanking it denies the mark that makes his Walkers sprint. Bait the wall out (20s at rank 1), then root and poke; never trade inside a full Walker swarm with Maiden up, because that is the only way he out-damages you.","late":"Yorick is a hard scaler and this is where the EVEN lane tips to him. With 2+ items and a Maiden, Dark Procession's wall plus Mourning Mist's armour shred trap you in the side lane and a full Walker wave out-trades your poke. Last Rites heals him every 6s at rank 1, so buy Morellonomicon or the chip never sticks. Don't try to 1v1 his split — shove and detonate from range, then group and let your team answer the Maiden. Without Flash up, one wall is a death.","whys":["You both have a soft level 1 — Yorick has only Q and a couple ghouls, you have one ability and a 550 auto, so it is a poke-trade with no commit either way.","Your Q + Solar Snare combo comes online and roots him as he steps to last-hit behind ghouls — a free Radiant Volley he cannot answer.","With Q, E and Rebuttal you root, poke and blank Mourning Mist, so the mark that speeds his Walkers never lands and you control the wave.","Your Q ranks up and Overwhelm stacks from repeated trades, but his ghoul count climbs too, so the lead is real yet not a stomp — call it your edge.","Golden Eclipse executes from any range, but Eulogy of the Isles answers with a Maiden that raises Walkers off every corpse — six nets out even.","Your first AP/mana item chains pokes, but Maiden plus a Last Rites heal every 6s out-lasts them — his item timing takes this stage, not yours.","He out-scales you hard — 2+ items, Maiden and Dark Procession's wall pin you in the side lane where Mourning Mist's armour shred and the Walker swarm delete your squishy frame, so let your team answer the split."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"zac","win":["Mel","Skill","Zac","Zac","Mel","Zac","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + E online: when Zac walks up to last-hit, root him with Solar Snare — rooted, Elastic Slingshot cannot launch — and pile Q explosions on."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates the Overwhelm you stacked from poke — but Cell Division splits him into four bloblets on death, so the kill may not stick."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With your first AP item you out-range every pickup attempt — and every ability he casts costs current health, so he walks himself down."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (his)","text":"Zac's only kill is a long-range E sling from fog or a flank — hold W to delete the E projectile and turn the gank attempt off entirely."}],"wants":{"you":["Root the E sling with Solar Snare or eat it with W's projectile wall so his only gap-close is dead","Stack Overwhelm with Q poke and empowered autos, then detonate with Golden Eclipse before he picks up blobs","Sit at 550 range and deny his passive blobs by zoning the spot where they drop"],"foe":["Land a surprise E sling from fog or a side angle to close the gap before you can react","Pick up his split-off passive blobs to undo your poke and reset the trade","Open with Stretching Strikes from 800, then Unstable Matter's percent-HP chip"]},"early":"Zac wants to walk up and last-hit, and that's exactly when you punish — at Level 2 with Q and E, root him with Solar Snare the moment he steps to a minion and dump Q explosions on the root. Rooted, Elastic Slingshot cannot launch at all, so the root is your real defence. Respect Stretching Strikes though: it reaches 800 units, near your own Q range, and every cast of his kit costs him a slice of his current health.","mid":"This is your window. Every trade stacks Overwhelm, and at 6 Golden Eclipse turns those stacks into a chunk he can't out-sustain — his blob pickups heal a fraction of a full-stack R plus the Solar Snare slow field. Keep zoning the blobs that split off when you hit him. But buy Morellonomicon before you count on the execute: Cell Division reforms him from four bloblets, so a kill only sticks if you clear them.","late":"You stomp the lane phase, but Zac scales into a teamfight engage tank, not a 1v1 — by 2+ items his job is to flank with Elastic Slingshot and chain Let's Bounce! through your backline, not duel you. Don't facecheck brush near objectives where his sling lurks, and keep W charged for his engage angle. Close the map before his pickups make him an unkillable frontline; your edge is the isolated lane, not the 5v5.","whys":["You have a 550-range auto and one ability; Zac pays current health for every cast, so his own farming pattern walks him toward your execute.","Q plus Solar Snare's root lands a guaranteed punish the instant Zac steps to a minion — rooted, Elastic Slingshot cannot launch.","With Q, E and W online you poke and root — Elastic Slingshot is 21s at rank 1, so a whiff is a free window.","Repeated trades stack Overwhelm faster than blob pickups heal it back, and Unstable Matter only reaches 350 — stay outside it.","Golden Eclipse detonates your stacks for a chunk his sustain can't answer — but Cell Division can reform him from surviving bloblets.","First AP item plus mana lets you chain Q and detonate freely while you out-range every blob-pickup attempt.","Zac scales into a flank-engage teamfight tank — by 2+ items he slings onto your backline and chains Let's Bounce!, so the lane edge stops mattering."]},
  {"a":"mel","b":"ziggs","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Q + E online means you can root him with Solar Snare the instant he steps to a bomb cast, then punish with empowered autos before he can reposition."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Golden Eclipse detonates your stacked Overwhelm from any range — if you've poked him with Q and autos, R can execute him through his minefield without ever closing distance."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Liandry's/Lost Chapter you chain Q pokes and reflect Bouncing Bomb with Rebuttal — your stacks plus R out-burst his single bomb."},{"when":"His R","text":"Bouncing Bomb casts at 850 against your 950 — what really out-ranges you is Satchel Charge at 1000 and a Mega Inferno Bomb thrown 5000."}],"wants":{"you":["Catch Bouncing Bomb mid-flight with Rebuttal and send it back as your own magic damage","Land Solar Snare's root when he over-extends to siege, then stack Overwhelm and detonate with R","Poke from 950 with Radiant Volley — you out-cast Bouncing Bomb's 850 by a hundred units"],"foe":["Land Satchel Charge from 1000 to knock you out of your own casting range","Drop Hexplosive Minefield at 900 to slow you off the wave and deny your only root","Out-siege you into towers where his longer range and AoE win the poke war"]},"early":"Two artillery mages, and the range war is yours, not his: Radiant Volley casts at 950 against Bouncing Bomb's 850, so poke first and step back. Your other edge is Solar Snare at 1000 — the instant he plants his feet to wind up a bomb, root him and follow with an empowered auto to stack Overwhelm. Watch Satchel Charge, 1000 range on 20s at rank 1, because it knocks you back out of your own range and resets the trade in his favour.","mid":"This is your best window, but it's narrow. Rebuttal is the swing tool — 38s at rank 1, and Bouncing Bomb is a thrown projectile, so catching one mid-flight flips a whole exchange. At 6, Golden Eclipse pays off all the Overwhelm you've stacked from Q and autos, so a clean poke sequence into R can chunk or execute him from across the lane. Walk straight through Hexplosive Minefield (16s) rather than around it, and root him while Satchel Charge is down.","late":"He does not out-range your Q — 850 against your 950 — but he does out-siege you: Hexplosive Minefield clears the waves you have to volley down, and Mega Inferno Bomb lands from 5000 on a 120/95/70 timer you cannot contest. You have no dash and one root. Stop trying to 1v1 the siege: rotate, look for Solar Snare picks in the river or on a flank, and let R finish anyone your team catches rather than soloing the artillery war.","whys":["Both of you are squishy artillery with one ability up — Radiant Volley casts 100 further than Bouncing Bomb, but neither can commit, so it is a coin flip.","Q + E gives you the root: he can't reposition out of Solar Snare before your empowered auto lands, so you own the level-2 punish window.","Your Q out-casts his by 100, but Satchel Charge reaches 1000 and knocks you back, so Rebuttal's reflect holds level 3 even.","Your Overwhelm stacks and Q rank-ups trade evenly into his bomb spam, but he can still kite the root — neither side runs the lane.","Golden Eclipse detonates your built-up Overwhelm from any range, turning a poke lead into an execute he can't outrun — your clearest kill window.","First item arms you both: your Liandry's stacks plus R answer his Lost Chapter bomb spam, keeping the siege even.","He out-sieges you late — Hexplosive Minefield clears what you must volley and Mega Inferno Bomb lands from 5000 — so the artillery war is his."]}
