window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"mel","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Full poke rotation online — space outside 425"},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R lets you cash stacked Overwhelm for real burst"},{"when":"2+ items","text":"One landed root now kills him — the duel of openers is even"}],"wants":{"you":["Max-range Q poke on his CS timings","E root and W held for his engage","Wave kept close to your tower"],"foe":["First-item Purgatory executes on a lone mage","Gap-close picks when your E is down","Soul Ignition refunds his chip damage"]},"early":"Play a clean spacing duel: your Q volleys out-range his marks, but he only needs one good gap-close to flip a trade, so poke on his last-hit animations and back off before he banks damage. Keep the wave near your side of the lane — a long lane is his best friend and your biggest liability.","mid":"Levels 4-6 stay honest — stack Overwhelm with steady poke and hold W Rebuttal for his nails rather than wasting it on chip. The real danger arrives at his first item: Purgatory executes you if he ever reaches you, and Silver Stake scales off your missing health, so never trade without E Solar Snare ready to root the dive.","late":"Post-two-items it becomes a duel of openers: your root-into-burst kills him, his pick-into-execute kills you. Stay behind your frontline, keep W loaded for his gap-close, and detonate Overwhelm with R the moment he commits — the first clean spell landed decides who walks away from every skirmish.","whys":["Even at level 1 — your ranged Q poke trades into his marks and slow, and nobody can force a kill.","Skill spacing decides level 2 — neither of you has kill threat yet, so it is poke placement against mark chip.","Level 3 stays even — your volley poke against his mark punish; whoever spaces better banks the HP lead.","Levels 4-5 remain a spacing duel with no clear favourite — keep W ready to blunt his commit.","Level 6 tilts to him — Purgatory executes a chipped mage outright, and Silver Stake hits hardest exactly as your health falls toward it.","His first-item spike is the danger window — once he gap-closes, Purgatory cleanly executes a defenceless mage, so never face him without E and W up.","Two items in it evens back out — his pick threat off E against your burst; whoever lands the opener wins."]});
