window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"mel","b":"zaahen","win":["Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Free poke before Aureate Rush and Dreaded Return"},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Root plus Rebuttal punish a careless Aureate Rush"},{"when":"Full Overwhelm stacks","text":"Golden Eclipse chunks him — but he can revive"}],"wants":{"you":["A poke lead banked before level 3","Solar Snare saved for Aureate Rush","Teamfights, never sidelane duels"],"foe":["Dreaded Return, an 850-range pull","Extended trades: Q and R both heal","Catching you with Solar Snare down"]},"early":"Bank your lead in the first two levels — poke him off CS while both kits are toothless, because from 3 on Aureate Rush and Dreaded Return reach you without him walking. Dreaded Return is an 850-range pull, barely inside your Q, so concede wave position rather than health and hold Solar Snare for his engage.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are survival: Dreaded Return drags you in from 850 range if you step past the halfway line, so farm with Q at max range and call for jungle help. At 6 a landed root plus Rebuttal can flip a careless Aureate Rush into a kill — but buy Morellonomicon, because The Darkin Glaive and Grim Deliverance both heal him.","late":"You lose the 1v1 at every item count, so stop laning into him: group first, push waves from range and leave the sidelane duel to someone tankier. In fights, root the frontline, stack Overwhelm from the backline and cash Golden Eclipse out of his reach — but know Cultivation of War can revive him once it fills.","whys":["Level 1 is an even farm phase — you can poke, but you cannot yet punish him for walking up.","Level 2 stays even — your Overwhelm has not ramped, but Aureate Rush is not online either, so both of you are toothless.","Level 3 tilts against you — Aureate Rush closes the gap and Dreaded Return pulls you 850 units, so respect every walk-up.","Levels 4-5 favour him — Dreaded Return drags you in from 850, and you have no escape once Solar Snare misses.","Level 6 is your skill-check reprieve — Zaahen casts no projectile, so Rebuttal is damage immunity; spend it on Grim Deliverance.","At first item The Darkin Glaive's healing out-paces your mana-hungry poke — buy Morellonomicon or stop chipping.","Two items in you cannot escape him one-on-one, and Cultivation of War can hand him a revive on top."]});
